export const REG_CHUNKS: RegChunk[] = [
  {"id": 1, "doc": "ug", "clause": "Preamble", "heading": "Institute Profile: Vision, Mission, Quality Policy, Objectives, Motto", "section": "Preamble", "text": "PERIYAR MANIAMMAI INSTITUTE OF SCIENCE & TECHNOLOGY Periyar Nagar, Vallam, Thanjavur - 613403 Tamil Nadu, India. Periyar Maniammai Institute of Science & Technology is committed to imparting quality education, emphasizing the integration of proficiency and human values, along with the ongoing enhancement of educational quality. Vision Statement: To be a university of global dynamism with excellence in knowledge and innovation, ensuring social responsibility for creating an egalitarian society. Mission:  Offering well-balanced programs with scholarly faculty and state-of-the-art facilities to impart a high level of knowledge.  Providing student-centered education and fostering their growth in critical thinking, creativity, entrepreneurship, problem-solving, and collaborative work.  Engaging in progressive and meaningful research with a focus on sustainable development.  Empowering students to acquire the skills necessary for global competencies.  Instilling universal values, self-respect, gender equality, dignity, and ethics Quality Policy: To be a leading institution of excellence in education and research, providing professional competence to meet academic, scholastic, and societal needs. Objectives:  To provide value-based education with social responsibility and ethics to both urban and underserved rural students.  To achieve excellence in education and empower students to attain global competence.  To promote a culture of research and innovation in young minds, fostering academic excellence, and encouraging lifelong learning.  To engage in specialized areas with a proven ability to make distinctive contributions to the objectives of the higher education system across diverse disciplines.  To engage in extramural studies, extension programmes, and field outreach activities to contribute to the development of society. The Motto: THINK – INNOVATE – TRANSFORM PERIYAR MANIAMMAI INSTITUTE OF SCIENCE & TECHNOLOGY REGULATIONS: R-2024 CHOICE BASED CREDIT SYSTEM (CBCS) (Common to all B.Tech. Programmes) Full -Time Programmes (8 Semesters / 6 Semesters Lateral Entry Scheme) (with effect from the academic year 2024 - 2025)"},
  {"id": 2, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R1", "heading": "DEFINITIONS AND NOMENCLATURE", "section": "R1. DEFINITIONS AND NOMENCLATURE", "text": "DEFINITIONS AND NOMENCLATURE i. \"Institute\" means Periyar Maniammai Institute of Science & Technology (Institute Deemed to be University). ii. \"Degree\" means that academic award conferred upon a student on successful completion of a programme designed to achieve the defined attributes. It is referred to as an Undergraduate (UG) Degree, that is B.Tech. Degree. iii. \"Discipline\" means branch of a B.Tech. Degree Programme, like Civil Engineering, Electrical and Electronics Engineering, etc. iv. \"Programme\" means cohesive arrangement of courses, co-curricular and extracurricular activities to accomplish predetermined objectives leading to awarding of a degree. v. \"Course\" means a theory / practical / theory integrated with practical subject studied in a semester, like Mathematics, Coding Techniques, Data Structures, etc. vi. \"Dean (Academic Courses)\" means the authority of the Institution who is responsible for all the academic activities of the departments for implementation of relevant rules and regulations. vii. \"Dean (FET)\" means Dean of Faculty of Engineering and Technology. viii. \"Controller of Examinations\" means the authority of the Institution who is responsible for all the activities of the examinations. ix. \"HoD\" means the Head of the Department concerned. x. \"MoU\" means the agreement signed between two parties either in India or Abroad to improve the academic standards. xi. \"Chairperson, BoS\" means Chairperson of Board of Studies of each department. xii. \"Department Advisory Committee\" means the committee constituted by the Institution for approving academic matters of the department. xiii. \"Honours\" degree means award of additional qualification to well performing UG students on earning the specified additional credits and satisfying the relevant degree award conditions. xiv. \"Specialization\" means award of additional qualification to the students on earning the specified additional credits from the courses offered in the same department. xv. \"Minor\" degree means award of additional qualification to the students on earning the specified additional credits from the courses offered in other departments. xvi. \"E-Resources\" means learning materials saved electronically in online storage or cloud platform, which shall be accessed from anywhere and anytime online or shall be accessed offline by downloading the relevant materials. xvii. \"MOOCs\" means Massive Open Online Courses available at both introductory and advanced levels accessible from \"E-Resources\". xviii. \"AICTE\" means All India Council for Technical Education established at New Delhi. xix. \"UGC\" means University Grants Commission established at New Delhi. xx. \"Academic Council\" means the approval granting authority for all academic related activities like framing of academic policies, approval of regulations, courses, syllabus etc. xxi. \"Bonafide Student\" means one who has enrolled for at least one course in the curriculum as per regulations and has paid the tuition fee for the same."},
  {"id": 3, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R2", "heading": "ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "ADMISSION PROCEDURE"},
  {"id": 4, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R2.1", "heading": "Regular Admission", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Regular Admission The students seeking admission to the Bachelor of Technology programme shall require satisfying eligibility criteria as prescribed by the Institution from time to time."},
  {"id": 5, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R2.1.1", "heading": "Candidates for admission to the first year of the B.Tech. Degree", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates for admission to the first year of the B.Tech. Degree Programmes shall be required to have passed the Higher Secondary Examination (10 + 2 Academic Stream) with Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry as three of the four subjects of study under Part III or any Examination recognized as equivalent. (OR) Should have passed the Higher Secondary Examination of Vocational stream (Vocational groups in Engineering / Technology)."},
  {"id": 6, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R2.2", "heading": "Lateral Entry Admission", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Lateral Entry Admission"},
  {"id": 7, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R2.2.1", "heading": "The candidates who possess the Diploma in Engineering / Technology", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "The candidates who possess the Diploma in Engineering / Technology awarded by the State Board of Technical Education, Tamil Nadu, or its equivalent are eligible to apply for lateral entry admission to the third semester of B.Tech. Degree Programme as per the norms of the Institution from time to time."},
  {"id": 8, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R2.2.2", "heading": "The candidates who possess the Degree in Science (10+2+3 stream) with", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "The candidates who possess the Degree in Science (10+2+3 stream) with Mathematics as a subject at the B.Sc. level are eligible to apply for lateral entry admission to the third semester of B.Tech. Degree Programme. However, such candidates shall undergo additional engineering courses in the third and fourth semesters as prescribed by the concerned department."},
  {"id": 9, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R2.3", "heading": "Transfer of Candidates from Other Institutions", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Transfer of Candidates from Other Institutions A candidate can join from any other University / Institution in the beginning of academic year, subject to the recommendations of Equivalence Committee and approval of Dean (Academic Courses) of the Institution."},
  {"id": 10, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R2.3.1", "heading": "Such candidates should not have any standing arrears at the time of", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Such candidates should not have any standing arrears at the time of admission and they should undergo additional courses, if necessary, as recommended by the Equivalence Committee. The candidate should submit the Transfer Certificate (TC) obtained from the Institution last studied."},
  {"id": 11, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R2.4", "heading": "The eligibility criteria such as discipline, minimum marks required,", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "The eligibility criteria such as discipline, minimum marks required, number of attempts, the age limit, and physical fitness shall be as described by the Academic Council of the Institution from time to time."},
  {"id": 12, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R2.5", "heading": "If, at any time after admission, it is found that a candidate has not fulfilled", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "If, at any time after admission, it is found that a candidate has not fulfilled any of the requirements stipulated by the Institution, the Dean (Academic Courses) may revoke the admission of the candidate and report the matter to the Registrar for further action."},
  {"id": 13, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R3", "heading": "PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "section": "R3. PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "text": "PROGRAMMES OF STUDY"},
  {"id": 14, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R3.1", "heading": "A student may be given admission to any one of the programmes of study", "section": "R3. PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "text": "A student may be given admission to any one of the programmes of study (as given in the following table) approved by AICTE and offered at the Institution. Sl. No. UG Programmes 1. B.Tech. Aerospace Engineering 2. B.Tech. Biotechnology 3. B.Tech. Computer Science and Engineering Sl. No. UG Programmes B.Tech. Computer Science and Engineering 4. (Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning) B.Tech. Computer Science and Engineering 5. (Cyber Security) 6. B.Tech. Electronics and Communication Engineering 7. B.Tech. Electrical and Electronics Engineering 8. B.Tech. Mechanical Engineering 9. B.Tech. Civil Engineering 10. B.Tech. Artificial Intelligence and Data Science"},
  {"id": 15, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R3.2", "heading": "Change of Programme of Study", "section": "R3. PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "text": "Change of Programme of Study"},
  {"id": 16, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R3.2.1", "heading": "Students can transfer from one B.Tech. programme to another", "section": "R3. PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "text": "Students can transfer from one B.Tech. programme to another programme of study only after successfully completing the first year, which includes the first two semesters."},
  {"id": 17, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R3.2.2", "heading": "Eligibility for transfer to a specific programme is limited to students who", "section": "R3. PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "text": "Eligibility for transfer to a specific programme is limited to students who meet the admission criteria for the programme of study and depends on the availability of vacant seats."},
  {"id": 18, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R3.2.3", "heading": "Students intending to change their programme must apply to the Dean", "section": "R3. PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "text": "Students intending to change their programme must apply to the Dean (Academic Courses) at the beginning of second semester of the first year of study before the specified closing date."},
  {"id": 19, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R3.2.4", "heading": "Students intending to change their programme of study may indicate up", "section": "R3. PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "text": "Students intending to change their programme of study may indicate up to three preferences of programmes in the order of priority for their desired change, as the decision will be based strictly on merit and the availability of vacancies."},
  {"id": 20, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R3.2.5", "heading": "Programme changes will be granted based solely on the merit of eligible", "section": "R3. PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "text": "Programme changes will be granted based solely on the merit of eligible applicants. The CGPA of students at the end of the second semester will determine the rank order for applicants requesting a programme change. The percentage of marks obtained in HSC / Diploma, and PMIST Entrance Examination will also be considered in case of a tie."},
  {"id": 21, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R3.2.6", "heading": "Approved programme changes for intended students, as per the Clause", "section": "R3. PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "text": "Approved programme changes for intended students, as per the Clause"},
  {"id": 22, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R3.2", "heading": "will take effect from the third semester. No further programme", "section": "R3. PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "text": "will take effect from the third semester. No further programme changes will be allowed thereafter."},
  {"id": 23, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R3.2.7", "heading": "All programme changes allowed at this stage are final and binding on the", "section": "R3. PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "text": "All programme changes allowed at this stage are final and binding on the applicants. Students cannot refuse the offered programme change under any circumstances."},
  {"id": 24, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4", "heading": "STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME"},
  {"id": 25, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.1 (part 1)", "heading": "Categorization of Courses", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Categorization of Courses Every B.Tech. Programme shall have a curriculum with syllabus comprising of Theory, Theory integrated with Practical, Practical integrated with Theory, and Practical courses with well-defined Programme Educational Objectives (PEOs), Programme Specific Outcomes (PSOs), and Programme Outcomes (POs) as per Outcome Based Education (OBE). The content of each course is designed based on the Course Outcomes (COs). The programmes shall cover the following category of courses as per the guidelines of AICTE / UGC. a. Foundation Courses Humanities and Social Sciences including Management Courses include Technical English, Engineering Ethics and Human Values, Communicationskills and Management courses. Basic Science Courses include Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry,Biology for Engineers, Environmental Sciences, etc. Engineering Science Courses include Engineering Practices, Engineering Graphics, Basics of Electrical / Electronics / Mechanical / Civil / Computer Engineering, Instrumentation etc. b. Professional Core Courses include the core courses relevant to the chosen specialization / branch. c. Professional Elective Courses include the elective courses relevant to the chosen specialization / branch. d. Open Elective Courses shall provide an opportunity to study a course from any discipline that includes the courses relevant to the chosen specialization, the courses that enhance soft and managerial skills, the courses a student can choose from the curriculum of other B.Tech."},
  {"id": 26, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.1 (part 2)", "heading": "Categorization of Courses", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "programmes and the courses offered by the other departments such as Indian Knowledge System,Economics for Engineers, Financial Engineering etc. e. Employability Enhancement Courses include Internship, Career Development Skills, Creative and Innovative Projects, Coding Techniques, Seminar, Professional Practices, Value Added Courses, Case Study, and Industrial Training. f. Online Courses allow the students to habituate independent learning through Massive Open Online Courses (MOOCs) restricted to NPTEL / SWAYAM / other online courses offered by premier institutions. g. Audit Courses expose the students to Unnat Bharath Abhiyan, Constitution of India, Essence of Indian Traditional Knowledge, Yoga, English for Research Paper Writing, Pedagogy Studies, Stress Management and Personality Development through Life Enlightenment Skills. This category of courses is mandatory non-credit courses for the students. There should be enough number of elective courses available for students to choose from. The combination of various courses should be designed in a way that, by the end of the programme, students are not only well-prepared for their specific professional fields but also have developed a sense of social consciousness. The credit requirements for each category of courses are outlined in Table 1. Table 1: Credit Requirements for each category of Courses Sl. No. Category of Courses Credits Foundation Courses (Humanities and Social Sciences including 1. Management Courses, Basic Science and Engineering 60 Science Courses) 2. Professional Core Courses 60 3."},
  {"id": 27, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.1 (part 3)", "heading": "Categorization of Courses", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Professional Elective Courses 18 Open Elective Courses (Soft and Managerial Skills, Core and Elective 4. Courses offered by other Departments, Indian 9 Knowledge System, Economics and Finance) Employability Enhancement Courses (Professional Practices, Value-added, Skill 5. Development Courses including Community Engagement and Social Responsibility, Internship, and 27 Projects) 6. Online Courses 6 Courses lead to Specialization / Minor / Honours 7. 20 Degree 8. Audit Courses ---"},
  {"id": 28, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.2", "heading": "Every B.Tech. Degree Programme will have a balanced curriculum as per", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Every B.Tech. Degree Programme will have a balanced curriculum as per AICTE / UGC guidelines and syllabus for the courses with required outcomes approved by the Academic Council."},
  {"id": 29, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.3", "heading": "The curriculum of the first and second semesters shall be common for all", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "The curriculum of the first and second semesters shall be common for all the B.Tech. Degree Programmes."},
  {"id": 30, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.4", "heading": "The curriculum of any B.Tech. Degree Programme is designed to include", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "The curriculum of any B.Tech. Degree Programme is designed to include a maximum of 180 credits for the award of the degree. If a student opted for specialization, minor, or honours degree, he / she must complete additional courses to earn an additional 20 credits for the award of degree."},
  {"id": 31, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.5", "heading": "The curriculum of a semester normally shall have a blend of 6 lecture-", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "The curriculum of a semester normally shall have a blend of 6 lecture- based courses and upto 3 laboratory courses except for the pre - final and final semesters. In addition, Audit Course(s) may be included. Each course may have credits assigned as per Clause R4.6. However, the total number of courses per semester shall not exceed 10, including Audit Courses (11 courses in case of Specialization / Minor / Honours degree). Pre-final semester shall have 6 lecture courses, a Project (Phase 1) and laboratory courses not exceeding 2. The final semester shall have an online course and a Project (Phase 2)."},
  {"id": 32, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.6", "heading": "Credit Assignment", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Credit Assignment Each course is assigned a certain number of credits based on the details provided in Table 2. Table 2: Credit Assignment Contact Period per Week Credit One Lecture Period 1 One Tutorial Period 1 Two Practical / Laboratory Periods 1 Every two weeks of Industrial Training / Internship 1 The contact periods per week for laboratory courses can only be in multiples of 2."},
  {"id": 33, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.7", "heading": "In special cases such as Specialization / Minor / Honours degree", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "In special cases such as Specialization / Minor / Honours degree requirement, or doing an additional elective course, students may be permitted to take seven lecture-based and four laboratory-based courses subject to the recommendation of the Mentor and approval of the Head of the Department. However, the maximum number of credits registered in any semester shall not exceed 30."},
  {"id": 34, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.8", "heading": "A student shall register for additional courses by paying the prescribed", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "A student shall register for additional courses by paying the prescribed fee."},
  {"id": 35, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.9", "heading": "Personality and Character Development", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Personality and Character Development All students shall enroll, on admission, in any one of the personality and character development programmes (NCC / NSS / NSO / YRC / RRC) and undergo training for about 80 hours and attend a camp of about seven days. The training shall include classes on first aid, health and hygiene awareness."},
  {"id": 36, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.9.1", "heading": "National Cadet Corps (NCC) will have about 20 parades.", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "National Cadet Corps (NCC) will have about 20 parades."},
  {"id": 37, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.9.2", "heading": "National Service Scheme (NSS) will have social service activities in and", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "National Service Scheme (NSS) will have social service activities in and around the Institution. The activities will include practical projects on recycling and reusing of biodegradable and dry / solid waste towards sustainable development."},
  {"id": 38, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.9.3", "heading": "National Sports Organization (NSO) will have activities related to", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "National Sports Organization (NSO) will have activities related to sports, games, drills, yoga and any physical exercises."},
  {"id": 39, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.9.4", "heading": "Youth Red Cross (YRC) will have activities related to health and", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Youth Red Cross (YRC) will have activities related to health and hygiene awareness, and social services in and around the Institution"},
  {"id": 40, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.9.5", "heading": "Red Ribbon Club (RRC) will have activities related to social services", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Red Ribbon Club (RRC) will have activities related to social services such as health awareness, blood donation camps etc., in and around the Institution."},
  {"id": 41, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.9.6", "heading": "While the training activities will normally be during weekends, the camp", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "While the training activities will normally be during weekends, the camp will normally be during the vacation period."},
  {"id": 42, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.9.7", "heading": "Every student shall put in a minimum of 75 percent attendance in the", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Every student shall put in a minimum of 75 percent attendance in the training and attend the camp compulsorily. The training and camp shall be completed during the first year of the programme. However, for valid reasons, the Dean (Academic Courses) may permit a student to complete this requirement in the second year."},
  {"id": 43, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.10", "heading": "Mandatory Induction Programme", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Mandatory Induction Programme All first year students should undergo three weeks' mandatory induction programme at the beginning of the first semester. The programme comprises physical activity, creative arts, universal human values, proficiency modules, lectures by eminent people, visits to local areas and familiarization to department / branch & innovations."},
  {"id": 44, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.11 (part 1)", "heading": "Assigning Course Codes", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Assigning Course Codes Category of Course UG / PG Regulation Courses / Classification Sequence 1 character 2 characters Programmes 1 character Number 2 characters 2 characters The course code consists of 8 characters, and it is divided into 5 parts. Part 1: One character (Alphabet) – U or P represents UG or PG programme. Part 2: Two characters (Numerals) represent Regulations. Part 3: Two characters (Alphabets) represent the Category of Courses / Professional Core Courses, Professional Elective Courses, Open Elective Courses, Online Courses, and Specialization Courses within the Department. Employability Enhancement Courses (EM): Year and Semester-wise programme specific courses. General Engineering Courses (GE): Year and Semester-wise foundation courses like Basic Science Courses, and Engineering Science Courses. Value Added Courses (VA): Courses related to programme specific, domain specific, skill based, and courses related to thrust areas and industrial requirements. Audit Courses (AU): Non-credit courses - Courses related to general skills, life skills, language skills, visionary skills, understanding historical events, understanding the successful stories of Philanthropists, Indian Constitution, Environmental Science etc. Part 4: One character (single numeral) – 1 to 9 represents the classification of the courses related to the specific programme. Classification Code Purpose (6th character) 1-4 Year of Study 6 Courses related to Specialization within the Department 7 Open Elective Courses 8 Online Courses 9 Elective Courses related to the specific programme Part 5:"},
  {"id": 45, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.11 (part 2)", "heading": "Assigning Course Codes", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Two characters (Numerals) represent the sequence number of the courses in each category, further, to represent the courses to beoffered in the odd and even semesters. Sequence 01 to 49 represents courses in the odd semester. Sequence 51 to 99 represents courses in the even semester. The codes for the Value Added and Audit courses will be general, applied to all programmes offered at the Institution. Although there are only four segments in the codes assigned to these courses, they consist of eight characters in total. Part 4 andPart 5 are combined to create a sequential number ranging from 001 to 999. The two alphabetical characters (Part 3) used to represent various programmes and categories of courses offered in all UG degree programmes are listed below in Table 3. Table 3: Two Character Representation of Category of Programme / Courses Sl. No. Name of the Programme / Course Code 1 English EN 2 Mathematics MA 3 Physics PH 4 Chemistry CH 5 General Engineering / Management Studies GE 6 B.Tech. Aerospace Engineering AS 7 B.Tech. Biotechnology BT 8 B.Tech. Civil Engineering CE 9 B.Tech. Computer Science and Engineering CS B.Tech. Computer Science and Engineering 10 CI (ArtificialIntelligence and Machine Learning) B.Tech. Computer Science and Engineering 11 CC (CyberSecurity) 12 B.Tech. Artificial Intelligence and Data science AD 13 B.Tech. Electrical and Electronics Engineering EE 14 B.Tech. Electronics and Communication Engineering EC 15 B.Tech. Mechanical Engineering ME 16 Employability Enhancement Courses EM 17 Value Added Courses VA 18 Audit Courses AU"},
  {"id": 46, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.12", "heading": "Medium of Instruction", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Medium of Instruction The medium of instruction is English for all courses, seminar presentations and project / thesis / dissertation reports. However, bilingual language policy (English and Tamil) shall be adopted wherever applicable."},
  {"id": 47, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.13", "heading": "Industrial Training / Internship", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Industrial Training / Internship"},
  {"id": 48, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.13.1", "heading": "The students may undergo Industrial training / Internship for a period (a", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "The students may undergo Industrial training / Internship for a period (a minimum of 6 weeks in one or more slots) as specified in the Curriculum during summer / winter vacation. In this case, the training must be undergone continuously in the same organization for the entire period of each slot (a slot equals 2 weeks). The students may undergo Internship at a Research Organization / University / Industry (after due approval from the Head of the Department / Dean (FET)). The credits are distributed in Table 4 as follows: Table 4: Training Period and Assigned Credits Duration of Credits Industrial Training / Internship 2 weeks 1 4 weeks 2 >= 6 weeks 3"},
  {"id": 49, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.13.2", "heading": "The student is expected to submit a report and it shall be evaluated by a", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "The student is expected to submit a report and it shall be evaluated by a team of faculty members nominated by the Head of the Department. Based on the recommendations, the student will be awarded credits, and the results will be sent to the Controller of Examinations for further processing."},
  {"id": 50, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.14", "heading": "Industrial Visit", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Industrial Visit Every student is expected to undergo one industrial visit every year starting from the second year of the programme with the approval of the Head of the Department / Dean (FET). The Head of the Department shall ensure that necessary arrangements are made in this regard."},
  {"id": 51, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.15", "heading": "Semester Long Project Work / Industrial Project / Internship", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Semester Long Project Work / Industrial Project / Internship"},
  {"id": 52, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.15.1", "heading": "In the final semester, students shall undertake a semester long project", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "In the final semester, students shall undertake a semester long project work in their own discipline to obtain hands-on experience."},
  {"id": 53, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.15.2", "heading": "Project work may be assigned to a single student or to a group of students,", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Project work may be assigned to a single student or to a group of students, not exceeding 3 per group with a guide from the same department. However, if the project is of interdisciplinary nature, then students from different programmes are permitted to form a group and the guide can be from other departments also."},
  {"id": 54, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.15.3", "heading": "Students are permitted to undertake a semester long industrial project or", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Students are permitted to undertake a semester long industrial project or semester long internship in an industry / research organization in lieu of the final semester project work, provided the domain of such projects or internships come under the same discipline and approved by Department Advisory Committee and the industry has no objection in submitting the work carried out as a report. This industrial project or internship is apart from the summer industrial training or summer internship, if any."},
  {"id": 55, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.15.4", "heading": "If the outcome of the project work is the development of a finished", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "If the outcome of the project work is the development of a finished product then it may lead to a start-up activity."},
  {"id": 56, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.15.5", "heading": "The students have to submit a project report or internship report or start-", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "The students have to submit a project report or internship report or start- up report on or before the last working day of the semester and the assessment of the same is detailed in Clause R13.8."},
  {"id": 57, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.16", "heading": "Value Added Courses", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Value Added Courses"},
  {"id": 58, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.16.1", "heading": "Students may optionally undergo Value Added Courses and the credits", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Students may optionally undergo Value Added Courses and the credits earned through the Value-Added Courses shall be over and above the total credit requirement prescribed in the curriculum for the award of the degree. Courses with two / three credits shall be offered by a Department with the prior approval from the Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 59, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.16.2", "heading": "The details of the syllabus, time table and faculty may be sent to the", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "The details of the syllabus, time table and faculty may be sent to the Office of the Dean (Academic Courses) after approval from the Department Advisory Committee concerned."},
  {"id": 60, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.16.3", "heading": "Students shall be allowed to take these courses offered in other", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Students shall be allowed to take these courses offered in other Departments also, but with the permission of the Head of the Department of student and Head of the department offering the course."},
  {"id": 61, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.16.4", "heading": "Courses once approved shall be made available in the Institution's", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Courses once approved shall be made available in the Institution's website with information to Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 62, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.16.5", "heading": "The students shall register for additional value-added courses by paying", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "The students shall register for additional value-added courses by paying the prescribed fee."},
  {"id": 63, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.17", "heading": "Off Campus Courses and Transfer of Credits", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Off Campus Courses and Transfer of Credits"},
  {"id": 64, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.17.1", "heading": "Students are permitted to optionally enroll and study a maximum of three", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Students are permitted to optionally enroll and study a maximum of three off-campus courses in physical / online / hybrid mode under each UG programme with the approval of the Head of the Department, Dean (FET) and Dean (Academic Courses) as per the Regulations. The successful completion of these courses through any of the above modes shall be considered in lieu of professional elective / open elective courses listed in the curriculum as approved by Department Advisory Committee."},
  {"id": 65, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.17.2", "heading": "Students are permitted to optionally enroll and study online courses", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Students are permitted to optionally enroll and study online courses through SWAYAM / NPTEL / online courses offered by premier Institutions. The credit transfer is to be done based on the marks and certificate provided by them. The number of credits and transfer of credits are based on the procedure explained in Table 5 and the Mapping of the marks with the grades is explained in Table 6. The mapping of marks with grades is applicable, only if the student passes the course as per the guidelines of the institutions offering the courses. The credits earned by the candidate shall be added if the same courses offered at different levels and at different times. Table 5: Duration of the Course and Number of Credits Sl. No. No. of Weeks Credits 1. 4 weeks 1 2. 8 weeks 2 3. >= 12 weeks 3 Table 6: Mapping of Marks Scored in Online Course and Letter Grades Sl. No. Letter Grade Marks 1. O 90 - 100 2. A+ 80 - 89 3. A 70 - 79 4. B+ 60 - 69 5. B 50 - 59 6. C 40 - 49"},
  {"id": 66, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.17.3", "heading": "Students are also permitted to enroll and undergo courses in online mode", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Students are also permitted to enroll and undergo courses in online mode at Universities in India / Abroad. Further, the students are permitted to study courses of a particular semester in a University / Institution based on MoU. The marks / credits earned by the student shall be transferred based on the decision of the Credit Equivalence Committee constituted by Dean (Academic Courses) and approved by the Institution."},
  {"id": 67, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.18", "heading": "B.Tech. (Honours) / B.Tech. Minor Degree Programme", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "B.Tech. (Honours) / B.Tech. Minor Degree Programme B.Tech. (Honours) and B.Tech. (Minor with Specialization) in another Discipline will be optional for students and the students shall be permitted to select any one of them only. B.Tech. (Honours) Degree Programme Honours is a specialized degree that focuses on the area of the students' interest, which encourages advanced levels of study and multidisciplinary learning. Honours qualification enhances professional development and facilitates gaining recognition at the time of graduation for advanced and distinguished work contributed by the undergraduate students."},
  {"id": 68, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.18.1", "heading": "Eligibility Criteria for Registration B.Tech. (Honours)", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Eligibility Criteria for Registration B.Tech. (Honours) Every student at the Institution intending to register for the \"Honours\" qualification shall fulfill the following academic requirements: a. Registration to \"Honours\" qualification shall start from third semester onwards. b. Students should have passed all the courses in the first and second semesters in first attempt and have obtained CGPA >= 8.0. c. The lateral entry students / B.Sc. graduates shall be permitted to register for the courses from Semester IV onwards provided the students have earned a minimum GPA of 7.50 in Semester III and have cleared all courses in the first attempt. They should undergo two additional courses as recommended by the respective department, one course in the 4th semester and the other course in the 5th semester."},
  {"id": 69, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.18.2", "heading": "Registration Procedure", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Registration Procedure a. Any student who meets the eligibility criteria specified above and intends to register for the \"Honours\" qualification shall apply to the Institution through Head of the Department / Dean (FET) in a prescribed form along with the prescribed application fee within 15 days after notification by the Institution. b. There will be no limit on the intake of students for registration for \"Honours\" qualification. c. Notification for approved registrants will be intimated by the Dean (Academic Courses) within a week period of time after the closing date. d. The selected students shall pay a one-time non-refundable registration fee along with the tuition fee as prescribed by the Institution to confirm the registration."},
  {"id": 70, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.18.3", "heading": "Additional Course Works B.Tech. (Honours)", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Additional Course Works B.Tech. (Honours) a. In addition to the courses prescribed by the Institution to be completed successfully in all the semesters for the relevant degree award, each student registered for \"Honours\" degree qualification shall have to take up additional course works from a specified group of professional electives (vertical) or from any of the verticals of the same programme that lead to an additional 20 credits (maximum) as recommended by AICTE. b. All the additional course works should be completed within the minimum prescribed duration for the award of the degree. c. Students opting for an Honours degree shall be allowed to learn one or two courses online. d. Students should have passed all the additional courses in th e first attempt and have obtained CGPA >= 8.0."},
  {"id": 71, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.18.4", "heading": "B.Tech. Minor with Specialization in another Discipline", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "B.Tech. Minor with Specialization in another Discipline \"Minor\" Degree shall be awarded to the UG students on earning the specific extra credits after satisfying the relevant degree award conditions."},
  {"id": 72, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.18.5", "heading": "The students opting for Minor degree qualification will be permitted to", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "The students opting for Minor degree qualification will be permitted to register for the additional courses from Semester III onwards."},
  {"id": 73, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.18.6", "heading": "The student should have earned an additional 20 credits in any one of the", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "The student should have earned an additional 20 credits in any one of the verticals offered from other Engineering Disciplines / Science and Humanities / Management studies."},
  {"id": 74, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.18.7", "heading": "The student must enroll for these additional courses separately and should", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "The student must enroll for these additional courses separately and should pay a one-time non-refundable registration fee, a tuition fee for studying these additional courses and an additional examination fee."},
  {"id": 75, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.18.8", "heading": "The students can optionally enroll and earn a maximum of 6 credits in", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "The students can optionally enroll and earn a maximum of 6 credits in online mode from SWAYAM / NPTEL / other Online courses offered by premier institutions as approved by the Head of the Department, Dean FET, and Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 76, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.18.9", "heading": "All the additional course works should be completed within the minimum", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "All the additional course works should be completed within the minimum prescribed duration (vide Clause R5) for the award of the degree."},
  {"id": 77, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R5", "heading": "DURATION OF THE PROGRAMME", "section": "R5. DURATION OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "DURATION OF THE PROGRAMME"},
  {"id": 78, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R5.1", "heading": "A student is ordinarily expected to complete the B.Tech. Degree", "section": "R5. DURATION OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "A student is ordinarily expected to complete the B.Tech. Degree Programme in 8 semesters (four academic years) but in any case, not more than 14 Semesters (seven academic years) for HSC (or equivalent) candidates and not more than 12 semesters (six academic years) for lateralentry candidates."},
  {"id": 79, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R5.2", "heading": "Each semester shall normally consist of 90 working days including the", "section": "R5. DURATION OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "Each semester shall normally consist of 90 working days including the days during which the continuous assessments examinations are conducted. The Dean (Academic Courses) shall ensure that every teacher imparts instruction as per the number of periods / hours specified in the syllabus and that the teacher delivers the full content of the specified syllabus for the course being taught."},
  {"id": 80, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R5.3", "heading": "The total period for completion of the programme reckoned from the", "section": "R5. DURATION OF THE PROGRAMME", "text": "The total period for completion of the programme reckoned from the commencement of the first semester to which the candidate was admitted shall not exceed the maximum period specified in Clause R5.1 irrespective of the period of Break of Study (vide Clause R17) or prevention (vide Clause R7.7) in order that he / she may be eligible for theaward of the degree (vide Clause R16.1)."},
  {"id": 81, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6", "heading": "COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION The courses that a student registers in a semester includes: i. Courses of the current semester (including mandatory non-credit courses). ii. Course(s) in which he / she has not been permitted to appear for the end semester examinations for want of the minimum required attendance if such courses are offered in that semester. iii. Professional or Open elective course(s) opted by the students in lieu of the same category of courses in which he / she has failed, if the courses are offered in the semester. iv. The student shall register for the project work in the VII / VIII semester. v. Any other course(s) the student wishes to register as per norms (vide Clauses R4.7, R4.8, R4.15, R4.16, R4.17, and R4.18) with the approval of Head of the Department, Dean (FET), and Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 82, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.1", "heading": "Each student, on admission, shall be assigned to a Mentor (vide Clause", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Each student, on admission, shall be assigned to a Mentor (vide Clause R9), who shall advice and counsel the student about the details of the academic programme and the choice of courses, considering the student's academic background and career objectives."},
  {"id": 83, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.2", "heading": "Each student shall register for all the courses prescribed in the curriculum", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Each student shall register for all the courses prescribed in the curriculum of the first semester of study."},
  {"id": 84, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.3", "heading": "After registering for a course, the student should attend classes, satisfy", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "After registering for a course, the student should attend classes, satisfy attendance requirements (vide Clause R7), earn continuous assessment marks, and appear for the end semester examinations."},
  {"id": 85, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.4", "heading": "Enrollment for all the courses listed in the curriculum from the semesters", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Enrollment for all the courses listed in the curriculum from the semesters II to VIII and additional courses for Honours, Specialization and Minor from the semesters III to VII will commence five working days prior to the commencement of the succeeding semester. The courses for Honours, Specialization, and Minor shall be registered separately under additional courses. The candidate makes the choice of electives in consultation with his / her Mentor."},
  {"id": 86, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.5", "heading": "Late registration will be permitted with a fine amount as prescribed by", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Late registration will be permitted with a fine amount as prescribed by theInstitution up to two weeks from the last date specified for registration."},
  {"id": 87, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.6", "heading": "The student shall enroll for the courses with the guidance of the Mentor.", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The student shall enroll for the courses with the guidance of the Mentor. If the student wishes, the student may drop or add courses (vide Clause R6.9) within five working days after the commencement of the concerned semester and complete the registration process duly authorized by the Course Instructor / Mentor."},
  {"id": 88, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.7", "heading": "The list of students approved by the respective Course Instructor as", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The list of students approved by the respective Course Instructor as discussed in the Class Committee (vide Clause R10) shall be final and would be considered for attendance, grades, and calculation of CGPA and no changes shall be made thereafter."},
  {"id": 89, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.8", "heading": "The candidate will be eligible for enrollment only if he / she has cleared", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The candidate will be eligible for enrollment only if he / she has cleared all the dues to the Institution such as Hostel fees, Library due, Laboratory breakages etc., of the previous semester and paid all required prescribed fees for the current semester, provided he / she is not debarred from the Institution on account of disciplinary matters."},
  {"id": 90, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.9", "heading": "FLEXIBILITY TO ADD OR DROP COURSES", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "FLEXIBILITY TO ADD OR DROP COURSES"},
  {"id": 91, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.9.1", "heading": "A student must earn the total number of credits specified in the", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "A student must earn the total number of credits specified in the curriculum of the chosen programme of study to be eligible to obtain the degree. However, the student is permitted to earn more than the total number of credits prescribed in the curriculum of the programme. In such cases, the minimum number of credits required for the completion of the programme would be considered for CGPA calculation."},
  {"id": 92, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.9.2", "heading": "From third semester onwards, each student has to register all courses", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "From third semester onwards, each student has to register all courses in the curriculum of a respective semester (with the facility to drop courses to a maximum of 8 credits). The dropping of courses shall be decided as per prerequisite requirements in consultation with the Mentor."},
  {"id": 93, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.9.3", "heading": "The student can also register for courses in which he / she failed in the", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The student can also register for courses in which he / she failed in the earlier semesters. In such cases the student shall do reappearance registration for those courses or redo the courses when they are offered."},
  {"id": 94, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.9.4", "heading": "In case, the student fails to secure pass in an elective course, he / she shall", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "In case, the student fails to secure pass in an elective course, he / she shall be allowed to opt for a change in elective and register for the same and do attend the classes to meet the criteria stated in Clause R7 and the failed elective shall not be listed in the Grade Sheet."},
  {"id": 95, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.9.5", "heading": "In any case, adding or dropping or redoing of courses, the total number", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "In any case, adding or dropping or redoing of courses, the total number of credits that a student is allowed to register per semester cannot exceed 30."},
  {"id": 96, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.9.6", "heading": "For an elective to be offered, the department shall specify the minimum", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "For an elective to be offered, the department shall specify the minimum number of students required."},
  {"id": 97, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.10", "heading": "Reappearance Registration", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Reappearance Registration"},
  {"id": 98, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.10.1", "heading": "If a student fails in a theory / practical / theory integrated with practical", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "If a student fails in a theory / practical / theory integrated with practical course, and practical integrated with theory course, the student shall do reappearance registration for that course in the subsequent semester, and appear for the end semester examination. However, the continuous assessment marks obtained by the student will be retained for the subsequent arrear attempts."},
  {"id": 99, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.10.2", "heading": "If the course in which the student has failed is a professional elective or", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "If the course in which the student has failed is a professional elective or anopen elective, the student will be permitted to register for the same in the subsequent semesters and shall appear for the end semester examination. If a student registers for the same professional / open elective, then the Clause R 6.10.1 is applicable. If a student registers for any other professional / open elective, he / she must attend the classes and fulfil the attendance requirements (vide Clause R7), earn continuous assessment marks, and appear for the end semester examination."},
  {"id": 100, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.10.3", "heading": "The student who fails in project work shall register for the same in the", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The student who fails in project work shall register for the same in the subsequent semester, when offered next, and repeat the course. In this case, the student must satisfy attendance requirements (vide Clause R7), earn continuous assessment marks and appear for the end semester examination."},
  {"id": 101, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.10.4", "heading": "Students are not eligible to reappear for the courses that they have already", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Students are not eligible to reappear for the courses that they have already passed in a semester for improvement of Grade / Marks."},
  {"id": 102, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.11", "heading": "Redoing a Course", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Redoing a Course Redoing a course means re-registering for a course, attending all classes, fulfilling the attendance requirements as per Clause R7, earning fresh continuous assessment marks and appearing for the end semester examination. A student must redo a course in the following conditions:"},
  {"id": 103, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.11.1", "heading": "If a student is prevented from writing the end semester examination of", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "If a student is prevented from writing the end semester examination of anycore course due to lack of attendance, the student has to register for that course again when offered next and redo the course."},
  {"id": 104, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.11.2", "heading": "If a student is prevented from writing the end semester examination of", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "If a student is prevented from writing the end semester examination of any professional / open elective course due to lack of attendance, the student can opt to register for the same course again when offered next and redo the course, or he / she can opt to register for a different professional / open elective course when it is offered, attend classes, fulfill the attendance requirements as per Clause R7, secure continuous assessment marks and appear for end semester examination."},
  {"id": 105, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.11.3", "heading": "If a student fails to secure a pass in any theory / laboratory / theory", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "If a student fails to secure a pass in any theory / laboratory / theory integrated with laboratory / laboratory integrated with theory course (including elective theory), he / she is given a maximum of three arrear attempts to complete the course as per Clause R14.3. If the student still fails to secure a pass, he / she shall register for the same when offered next and redo the course."},
  {"id": 106, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.11.4", "heading": "If the course in which the student fails to secure a pass even after three", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "If the course in which the student fails to secure a pass even after three arrear attempts is a professional / open elective course, then the student can opt for a different professional / open elective course, register for the same when it is offered, attend classes, fulfill the attendance requirements as per Clause R7, secure continuous assessment marks and appear for end semester examination."},
  {"id": 107, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.11.5", "heading": "The student who fails in any Project work (Phase 1 / Phase 2) shall", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The student who fails in any Project work (Phase 1 / Phase 2) shall register for the course again, when offered next, and redo the course. In this case, the student shall attend the reviews and fulfill the attendance requirements as per Clause R7."},
  {"id": 108, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.11.6", "heading": "The student who fails in Seminar / Internship / Case Study and Industrial", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The student who fails in Seminar / Internship / Case Study and Industrial / Practical Training and Creative and Innovative project shall register for the same in the subsequent semester and redo the course. In this case, the student shall attend the classes and fulfill the attendance requirements as per Clause R7."},
  {"id": 109, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7", "heading": "REQUIREMENTS FOR APPEARING FOR THE END", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "REQUIREMENTS FOR APPEARING FOR THE END SEMESTER EXAMINATIONS A student who has fulfilled the conditions, vide Clause R7.3 and Clause"},
  {"id": 110, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.4", "heading": "shall be deemed to have satisfied the attendance requirements for", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "shall be deemed to have satisfied the attendance requirements for appearing for the end semester examination of a particular course."},
  {"id": 111, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.1", "heading": "All students must attend every lecture, tutorial, and practical classes.", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "All students must attend every lecture, tutorial, and practical classes."},
  {"id": 112, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.2", "heading": "Attendance record will be maintained based upon roll calls (or any", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "Attendance record will be maintained based upon roll calls (or any equivalent operation) in every scheduled lecture, tutorial, and practical class. The Class Advisor will maintain and consolidate the attendance record for all the courses (lectures, tutorials, and practicals together, as applicable)."},
  {"id": 113, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.3", "heading": "Ideally every student is expected to attend all periods and earn 100", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "Ideally every student is expected to attend all periods and earn 100 percent attendance. However, the student shall secure not less than 75 percent attendance, course wise, considering the number of periods required for that course, as specified in the curriculum."},
  {"id": 114, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.4", "heading": "If a student secures attendance between 65 percent and less than 75", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "If a student secures attendance between 65 percent and less than 75 percent in any course in the current semester, due to medical reasons (hospitalization / accident / specific illness) or due to participation in the College / University / State / National / International level Sports events, with prior permission from the Head of the Department concerned and Dean (FET), the student shall be given exemption from the prescribed attendance requirement and the student shall be permitted to appear for the end semester examination of that course. In all such cases, the students should submit the required documents on joining after the absence to the Head of the Department through the Mentor."},
  {"id": 115, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.5", "heading": "A student shall normally be permitted to appear for the end semester", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "A student shall normally be permitted to appear for the end semester examination of the course if the student has satisfied the attendance requirements (Clauses R7.3 and R7.4) and has registered for the examination in those courses of that semester by paying the prescribed fee."},
  {"id": 116, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.6", "heading": "A student who has an attendance of less than 75 percent will not be", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "A student who has an attendance of less than 75 percent will not be permitted to appear for the end semester examination in the course in which the shortage exists. His / her registration for that course will be treated as cancelled and he / she shall be awarded 'SA' grade (\"Shortage ofAttendance\" i.e., registration is cancelled due to lack of attendance) in that course. This grade shall appear in the Result Sheet. The student should register and repeat the course as and when it is offered next."},
  {"id": 117, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.7", "heading": "Students who do not satisfy Clauses R7.3 and R7.4 or who secure less", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "Students who do not satisfy Clauses R7.3 and R7.4 or who secure less than 65 percent attendance in a course will not be permitted to write the end semester examination of that course (vide Clause R7). The student must register and redo the course when it is offered next as per Clause"},
  {"id": 118, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R6.11", "heading": "If the course in which the student has been prevented is a", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "If the course in which the student has been prevented is a professional / open elective, the student can opt to redo the same course or opt for different professional / open elective course as per Clause R6.11.2."},
  {"id": 119, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.8", "heading": "If a student has shortage of attendance in all the registered courses, he", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "If a student has shortage of attendance in all the registered courses, he / she would not be permitted to move to the higher semester and must repeat the current semester in the subsequent year."},
  {"id": 120, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.9", "heading": "In the case of reappearance registration for a course, the attendance", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "In the case of reappearance registration for a course, the attendance requirement as mentioned in Clauses R7.3 and R7.4 is not applicable. However, the student must register for the examination in that course by paying the prescribed fee."},
  {"id": 121, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.10", "heading": "If the student needs leave for a short duration (less than two weeks), prior", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "If the student needs leave for a short duration (less than two weeks), prior application for the leave shall have to be submitted to the Head of the Department concerned stating the reasons for the leave requested along with supporting documents and such leave may be granted by the Head of the Department."},
  {"id": 122, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.11", "heading": "Absence for the period not exceeding two weeks in a semester due to", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "Absence for the period not exceeding two weeks in a semester due to sickness or any other unavoidable reasons for which prior application could not be made may be condoned by the Head of the Department provided the given explanation is acceptable."},
  {"id": 123, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.12", "heading": "If the period of absence is likely to exceed two weeks, a prior application", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "If the period of absence is likely to exceed two weeks, a prior application for grant of leave will have to be submitted through Head of the Department / Dean (FET) to the Dean (Academic Courses) with supporting documents. In such case the decision to grant leave shall be taken by the Dean (Academic Courses) on the recommendation of the Head of the Department and Dean (FET)."},
  {"id": 124, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.13", "heading": "A student who is absent due to illness or any other emergency, up to a", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "A student who is absent due to illness or any other emergency, up to a maximum of two weeks, should approach the Class Advisor / Course Coordinator / Course Instructor for assignments and laboratory work."},
  {"id": 125, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.14", "heading": "In case, the period of absence on medical grounds is more than 20", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "In case, the period of absence on medical grounds is more than 20 working days during the semester, the student may apply for withdrawal from the semester, i.e. withdrawal from all courses registered in that semester."},
  {"id": 126, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R7.15", "heading": "If a student is continuously absent from the Institution for more than four", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "If a student is continuously absent from the Institution for more than four weeks without any notification to the Dean (Academic Courses), his / her name will be removed from the Institution rolls and the same should be informed to his / her parents immediately."},
  {"id": 127, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R8", "heading": "CLASS ADVISOR", "section": "R8. CLASS ADVISOR", "text": "CLASS ADVISOR There shall be a Class Advisor for each class. The Class Advisor will be one among the course instructors of the class. He / She will be appointed by the Head of the department concerned. The Class Advisor is the ex-officio member and the Convener of the class committee. The responsibilities of the Class Advisor shall be: a. To act as the channel of communication between the Head of the Department and the students of the respective class. b. To collect and maintain various details such as attendance, assessment marks and long leave particulars. c. To help the Chairperson of the class committee in planning and conducting the class committee meetings. d. To monitor the academic performance of the students including attendance and to inform the class committee. e. To coordinate with each instructor in performing analysis of results ofcontinuous assessments and end semester examinations and in estimating CO – PO attainment. f. To attend to the students' welfare activities like awards, medals, scholarships, and industrial visits."},
  {"id": 128, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R9", "heading": "MENTOR", "section": "R9. MENTOR", "text": "MENTOR To help the students in planning their courses of study and for general advice on the academic programme, the Head of the Department will attach a certain number of students to a teacher of the Department, who shall function as Mentor for those students throughout their period of study. The Mentor shall advise the students in registering and reappearance registering of courses, authorize the process, monitor their attendance and progress and counsel them periodically. If necessary, the Mentor may also discuss with or inform the parents about the progress / performance of the students concerned. The number of students assigned to a Mentor will be decided by the Head of the Department. However, the strength shall not exceed 20 students per Mentor. The responsibilities of the Mentor shall be: a. To inform the interpretation of Regulations to the students and their rights and duties. b. To inform the code of conduct to be maintained in the campus anddisciplinary actions. c. To inform the students about the various facilities and activities available to enhance the students' curricular and co-curricular activities. d. To guide in the process of enrollment and registration of the courses. e. To authorize the final registration of the courses at the beginning of each semester. f. To monitor the academic and general performance of the students including attendance and to counsel them accordingly. g. To collect and maintain the students' academic and co-curricular records. h. To facilitate and collect students' feedback about the course and course instructor. i. To facilitate and collect the course exit survey and programme exit survey. j. To provide all the details of the academic, including feedback, training, scholarship, placement, co-curricular, and extracurricular activities of the students to the Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 129, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R10 (part 1)", "heading": "CLASS COMMITTEE", "section": "R10. CLASS COMMITTEE", "text": "CLASS COMMITTEE A class committee consists of all teachers of the class concerned, student representatives and a chairperson who does not handle any course for the class. It is like the \"Quality Circle\" (more commonly used in industries), with the overall goal of improving the teaching-learning process. The class committee shall be constituted by the Head of the Department within 7 days from the commencement of classes. The Class Advisor and the Head of the Department will attend the meeting. The Dean (Academic Courses), Dean (FET), and the Mentor(s) shall be called to attend the meeting as special invitees, if required. The functions of the class committee include: a. Solving problems experienced by students in the classroom and in the laboratories in consultation with the Head of the Department, Dean (FET), and Dean (Academic Courses). b. Clarifying the Regulations of the degree programme and the details of rules therein. c. Informing the student representatives about the academic schedule including the dates of assessments and the syllabus coverage for each assessment. d. Informing the student representatives, the details of Regulations regarding weightage used for each assessment. e. Discussing in the class committee meeting the breakup of marks for each experiment / exercise / module of work, in case of practical courses (laboratory / project work / seminar, etc.) and informing the students. f. Analyzing the performance of the students of the class after each assessment and finding ways and means of improving their performance. g."},
  {"id": 130, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R10 (part 2)", "heading": "CLASS COMMITTEE", "section": "R10. CLASS COMMITTEE", "text": "Identifying the students who are low achievers or weak in their courses if any, and requesting the teachers concerned to provide some additional help or guidance or coaching to such students. The class committee is normally constituted by the Head of the Department.However, if the students of different programmes are mixed in each class, the class committee is to be constituted by the Dean (Academic Courses). At least 4 student representatives from the respective class (usually 2 boys and 2 girls) shall be included in the class committee. The Chairperson of the class committee is required to prepare the minutes of every meeting, submit the same to the Head of the Department within two days of the meeting and arrange to circulate the same among students concerned and teachers. A copy of the minutes shall be displayed in the notice board. If there are some points in the minutes requiring action by the Institution, the same shall be brought to the notice of the Registrar through Dean (FET) and Dean (Academic Courses). The first meeting of the class committee shall be held within 10 days from the date of commencement of the semester. The enrollment of courses including add and drop of the courses will be finalized. The nature and weightage of continuous assessments shall be decided in the first meeting, within the framework of the Regulations and the same shall be communicated to the students. Two or three subsequent meetings in a semester may be held at suitable intervals."},
  {"id": 131, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R10 (part 3)", "heading": "CLASS COMMITTEE", "section": "R10. CLASS COMMITTEE", "text": "During these meetings the student members representing the entire class, shall meaningfully interact and express their opinions and suggestions of the class students to improvethe effectiveness of the teaching-learning process. In each meeting, the actiontaken report based on the minutes of the previous meeting is to be presented and discussed by the Chairperson of the class committee. After the completion of the end semester examination and evaluation process, the course instructor shall keep the record of marks and grades earned by the students for the computation of CO and PO attainments."},
  {"id": 132, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R11", "heading": "COMMON COURSE COMMITTEE", "section": "R11. COMMON COURSE COMMITTEE", "text": "COMMON COURSE COMMITTEE A theory course handled by more than one teacher, or each common theory course offered to more than one discipline or group of disciplines, shall have a \"Common Course Committee\" comprising of all the instructors teaching that common course with one of them nominated as Course Coordinator. The nomination of the Course Coordinator shall be made by the Dean (Academic Courses) in consultation with the Dean (FET) and the Heads of the Departments, from among the instructors teaching the common course either from a single department or several departments. The committee shall be constituted by the Dean (Academic Courses) within 5 days from the commencement of the semester. The first meeting of the Common Course Committee shall be held within 5 days from the date of formation of the committee. The lesson plan, books and references to be followed shall be decided at the first meeting. The \"Common Course Committee\" shall meet as often as possible and ensure uniform evaluation of continuous assessments after arriving at a common scheme of evaluation for the assessments (vide Clause R13). Wherever feasible, the common course committee shall prepare a common question paper for the continuous assessment tests, objective type test and end semester examination. The question paper for the end semester examination shall be set by the Course Coordinator, in consultation with all the teachers. The common course committee shall meet to decide the multiplication factor for the respective batch of students, if required. The minutes in this regard shall be sent to all the concerned Head of the Department and the Controller of Examinations."},
  {"id": 133, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R12", "heading": "PERFORMANCE ANALYSIS COMMITTEE", "section": "R12. PERFORMANCE ANALYSIS COMMITTEE", "text": "PERFORMANCE ANALYSIS COMMITTEE The Performance Analysis Committee will consist of the same members as the class committee but including the Dean (Academic Courses), Director (IQAC), Dean (FET), and the Head of the Department and excluding the student members. An external member from an allied department shall be nominated by the Dean (Academic Courses) in consultation with the Vice Chancellor to the Performance Analysis Committee. The meeting of the Performance Analysis Committee is to be held within 10 days from the last day of the end semester examinations to analyze the performance of the students in all courses of study by estimating the CO - PO attainment levels and finalize the grade ranges for each course and forward the statement of grades to Dean (Academic Courses) immediately, through the Headof the Department and Dean (FET). The Performance Analysis Committee, by collective wisdom, should ensure that the clustering / grading / pass–fail decisions have been reasonably balanced. The attendance registers of all the courses with all the continuous assessment marks, end semester marks, Tabulation Register, grades, and grade-ranges entered in the register are also to be sent to Dean (Academic Courses) immediately through the Head of the Department and Dean (FET) for forwarding to the Controller of Examinations."},
  {"id": 134, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13", "heading": "SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION The End Semester examinations for theory, theory integrated with practical, practical integrated with theory, and practical courses will be of 3 hours duration. These examinations shall normally be conducted between October and December during the odd semesters and between April and June during the even semesters. For practical, practical integrated with theory, and project courses, the end semester examination will be conducted with an external examiner appointed by the Controller of Examinations."},
  {"id": 135, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.1", "heading": "Assessment Procedures for Awarding Marks", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Assessment Procedures for Awarding Marks All B.Tech. programmes consist of Theory, Theory integrated with Practical, Practical, Practical integrated with Theory Courses and Employability Enhancement Courses. Employability Enhancement Courses include Project Work, Seminar, Professional Practices, Case Study and Industrial / Practical Training, Skill Development Courses / Value Added Courses. Appearance in End Semester Examination is mandatory for all courses including Theory, Theory integrated with Practical, Practical, Practical integrated with Theory courses, project work, and all lecture-based employability enhancement courses. Performance in each course of study shall be evaluated based on: i) Continuous Assessments throughout the semester and ii) End Semester Examination The evaluation shall be based on Outcome Based Education and the relevant rubrics shall be followed."},
  {"id": 136, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.2", "heading": "Each course, Theory, Theory Integrated with Practical, Practical,", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Each course, Theory, Theory Integrated with Practical, Practical, Practical Integrated with Theory, Project Work, and Value Added Course shall be evaluated for a maximum of 100 marks. The weightage for continuous assessment marks and end semester examination marks are given in Table 7."},
  {"id": 137, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.3", "heading": "Some domain specific courses included under Employability", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Some domain specific courses included under Employability Enhancement Courses are evaluated by internal assessments only. There is no evaluation for Audit Courses. However, minimum attendance requirements as per Clause R7 shall be satisfied. Table 7: Weightage of Marks Marks Weightage (%) Sl. Category of Courses Continuous End Semester No. Assessment Examination 1 Theory Courses 40 60 2 Laboratory Courses 75 25 Theory integrated with Theory - 20 3 Theory - 60 Laboratory Courses Laboratory - 20 Laboratory integrated with Theory - 25 4 Laboratory - 25 Theory Courses Laboratory - 50 5 Project Work 60 40 Value Added Courses, Skill Development Courses, 6 100 --- Internship and Online Courses (with one credit)"},
  {"id": 138, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.4", "heading": "Every teacher is required to maintain an \"ATTENDANCE AND", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Every teacher is required to maintain an \"ATTENDANCE AND ASSESSMENT RECORD\" for every semester, which consists of attendance marked in each class of Theory / Theory Integrated with Practical / Practical / Practical Integrated with Theory / EEC / Audit Courses, the assessment marks, and the record of class work (topics covered), separately for each course handled by the teacher. The attendance book completed in all respects should be submitted to the Head of the Department periodically (three times in a semester) for checking the syllabus coverage and the records of assessment marks and attendance. The Head of the Department and Dean (FET) will affix signature and date after due verification. At the end of the semester, the record should be verified by the Dean (Academic Courses)who shall keep this document in safe custody for 5 years. The records of attendance and assessment of both current and previous semesters should be available for auditing."},
  {"id": 139, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.5", "heading": "Assessment for Theory Courses", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Assessment for Theory Courses"},
  {"id": 140, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.5.1", "heading": "The End Semester Examinations for theory courses will be 3-hours", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "The End Semester Examinations for theory courses will be 3-hours duration for 100 marks and shall normally be conducted between October and December during the odd semesters and between April and June during the even semesters. The marks obtained by the student shall be converted to weightage of 60 percent."},
  {"id": 141, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.5.2 (part 1)", "heading": "Continuous Assessment Evaluation for Theory Courses", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Continuous Assessment Evaluation for Theory Courses i. The mode(s) of internal evaluation is / are to be decided for each course in the class committee. ii. The handwritten notes taken by students while attending classes are to be regularly monitored by the course teacher. Ten marks shall be awarded for the best handwritten notes, while the other handwritten notes will be evaluated comparatively with marks of 2, 4, 6, and 8. iii. There should be objective type assessment to evaluate the students for all courses exactly from 45 days to 60 days after commencement of classes in a semester and the weightage is 20 marks. There shall be 20, 40 or 50 questions based on the course. The duration of the assessment shall be 60 minutes for each course. iv. There shall be assignment / tutorial / quiz / case study / seminar / mini-project type of assessment for each course as decided in the class committee and the faculty must evaluate fairly for all the students relatively for 20 marks. v. All regular assessment tests are to be conducted for 100 marks and the marks obtained by the students are converted to 40 marks while evaluating continuous assessment marks. Three assessment tests are to be conducted for each course. vi. The question paper is to be set considering the appropriate Bloom's Taxonomy levels and to cope with the prescribed course outcomes. vii. The regular first assessment test is to be conducted between 30 and 35 days from the commencement of classes for the semester with the portion of syllabus covered up to 4 weeks. The test duration shall be a minimum of 1 hour."},
  {"id": 142, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.5.2 (part 2)", "heading": "Continuous Assessment Evaluation for Theory Courses", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "The mark obtained in the regular first assessment test (written for 100 marks) is converted to 90 percent to which the marks obtained for handwritten notes (maximum 10) is to be added to make it 100 (Continuous Assessment 1). viii. The second assessment test, termed as Mid-term test is to be conducted between 60 and 65 days from the commencement of classes for the semester with the portion of syllabus covered up to 8 weeks. The test duration shall be 2 hours. The question paper should have 5 questions in Part A and 3 questions in Part B. Marks obtained in the Mid-term assessment test (written for 100 marks) is converted to 70 percent to which the marks obtained for handwritten notes (maximum 10 marks) and marks obtained in the objective type of assessment (maximum 20 marks) are to be added to make it 100 (Continuous Assessment 2). ix. The third assessment test, termed as Model Examination is to be conducted between 80 and 85 days from the commencement of classes for the semester with the portion of syllabus covered up to 11 weeks. The test duration shall be 3 hours. The pattern of the question paper is as per the end semester regular examination. Marks obtained in the Model Examination (written for100 marks) is converted to 70 % to which the marks obtained for handwritten notes (maximum 10 marks) and marks obtained in the Quiz / Seminar / Mini-project assessment (maximum 20 marks) are to be added to make it 100 (Continuous Assessment 3). x. The continuous assessment mark is calculated either using Method 1 or Method 2 as follows: Method 1:"},
  {"id": 143, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.5.2 (part 3)", "heading": "Continuous Assessment Evaluation for Theory Courses", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "(Marks in (Continuous Assessment 1+ Continuous Assessment 2 + Continuous Assessment 3) / 300) X 40 Method 2: Handwritten notes (10) + Objective Type test (20) + Quiz / Seminar (10) + First assessment test (20) + Mid-term test (20) + Model Examination (20) = 100 marks. Reduce the marks obtained by each candidate to 40 percent and shall be submitted as continuous assessment marks. The commencement date of assessments and the number of weeks to be considered for syllabus coverage shall be fixed or modified as per the academic schedule prescribed by the Dean (Academic Courses) and Controller of Examinations."},
  {"id": 144, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.5.3", "heading": "In case, a student misses the assessment due to medical reasons", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "In case, a student misses the assessment due to medical reasons (hospitalization / accident / specific illness) or due to participation in the College / University / State / National / International level Competitions / NSS / NCC camps / Internships with prior permission from the Head of the Department and Dean (FET), only one re-assessment may be given at the end of the semester after getting approval from the Dean (Academic Courses) by the concerned Head of the Department and Course Instructor."},
  {"id": 145, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.6", "heading": "Assessment for Theory Integrated with Practical Courses and", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Assessment for Theory Integrated with Practical Courses and Practical Integrated with Theory Courses Each theory integrated with practical or practical integrated with theory course shall be evaluated for a maximum of 100 marks as shown in Table 8. Table 8: Assessment Weightage Marks (in percentage) Category Assessmen Assessment End Sl. No. t for for Semester ofCourse Theory Laboratory Examination Theory integrated 20 (Two 20 (Continuous 60 (Theory 1. with Practical Assessments) Evaluation) Examination) Practical integrated 25 (One 50 (Continuous 25 (Practical 2. withTheory Assessment) Evaluation) Examination) For theory integrated with practical courses, the end semester examinations will be conducted as theory examinations. For practical integrated with theory courses, the end semester examinations will be conducted and evaluated with an external examiner appointed by Controller of Examinations. The procedure for conduct of continuous assessments for laboratory component is as per the Clause R13.7. The two assessment tests for theory are written tests. The weighted average shall be converted into 40 marks for continuous assessment in case of theory integrated with practical courses and into 75 marks for practical integrated with theory courses."},
  {"id": 146, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.7", "heading": "Assessment for Laboratory Courses", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Assessment for Laboratory Courses"},
  {"id": 147, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.7.1", "heading": "Every laboratory exercise / experiment shall be evaluated based on the", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Every laboratory exercise / experiment shall be evaluated based on the student's performance during the laboratory class and the maintenance of laboratory records."},
  {"id": 148, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.7.2", "heading": "There shall be at least one assessment test for laboratory courses.", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "There shall be at least one assessment test for laboratory courses."},
  {"id": 149, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.7.3", "heading": "The criteria for arriving at the continuous assessment marks of 75 will be", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "The criteria for arriving at the continuous assessment marks of 75 will be as per the following scheme: for successful completion of all the prescribed experiments / exercises done in the laboratory including observation and record work, 75 percent of marks shall be awarded, and 25 percent marks shall be awarded for the assessment test. The total marks earned by the student in continuous assessments shall be converted into a maximum of 75 marks and rounded to the nearest integer."},
  {"id": 150, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.7.4", "heading": "The end semester examination for laboratory courses shall be for 25", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "The end semester examination for laboratory courses shall be for 25 marks and shall include viva-voce also as a part of it. The viva-voce examination shall be conducted by an external examiner appointed by the Controller of Examinations."},
  {"id": 151, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.7.5", "heading": "The end semester examination for laboratory courses will be of 3 hours", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "The end semester examination for laboratory courses will be of 3 hours duration and shall normally be conducted before the start of the theory examinations for that semester."},
  {"id": 152, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.8", "heading": "Assessment for Project Work (Phase 1 and Phase 2)", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Assessment for Project Work (Phase 1 and Phase 2)"},
  {"id": 153, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.8.1", "heading": "For Project work out of 100 marks, the maximum mark for continuous", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "For Project work out of 100 marks, the maximum mark for continuous assessment is fixed as 60 and the end semester examination (project report evaluation and viva-voce examination) carries 40 marks. Project work may be assigned to a single student or to a group of students, not exceeding 3 per group. Project Phase 2 in the eighth semester must be continuation of Project Phase 1 in the seventh semester with the same team members and supervisor if the students are pursuing their project work within the campus."},
  {"id": 154, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.8.2", "heading": "There shall be three assessments (each 100 marks) during the semester", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "There shall be three assessments (each 100 marks) during the semester by a review committee. The student shall make a presentation on the progress made before the committee. The Head of the Department shall constitute a review committee for each programme. There shall be a minimum of three members in the review committee. The committee shall consist of the supervisor (project guide), project coordinator and domain expert from the concerned / allied department. The total marks obtained in the three reviews shall be converted to a maximum of 60 marks rounded to the nearest integer. The review meetings, if necessary, may also be arranged in online mode with prior approval from the Dean (Academic Courses) and a suitable record of the meetings shall be maintained."},
  {"id": 155, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.8.3", "heading": "The student(s) is (are) expected to submit the project report on or before", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "The student(s) is (are) expected to submit the project report on or before the last working day of the semester. The end semester examination for the project work shall consist of the evaluation of the final project report submitted by the student or students of the project group by an external examiner, followed by a Viva-voce examination conducted separately for each student by a committee consisting of the external examiner and an internal examiner (other than project guide). The project coordinator shall be the internal examiner. The Head of the Department with the approval of Controller of Examinations shall appoint the external examiner for the end semester examination of the project work."},
  {"id": 156, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.8.4", "heading": "The continuous assessment and viva-voce examination marks for", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "The continuous assessment and viva-voce examination marks for projectwork shall be distributed as indicated below in Table 9: Table 9: Continuous Assessment and End Semester Examination Marks for the Project Work End Semester Examinations Continuous Assessment (60 Marks) (40 Marks) Review Viva-voce Review I Review II Project Report III Examination Guide External Internal External 10 20 30 10 10 10 10"},
  {"id": 157, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.8.5", "heading": "If the project report is not submitted on or before the specified deadline,", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "If the project report is not submitted on or before the specified deadline, an extension of time up to a maximum limit of 30 days may be given for the submission of project work with due approval obtained from the Dean (Academic Courses) and the same needs to be communicated to Controller of Examinations. If the project report is not submitted even beyond the extended time, then the student is deemed to have failed in the Project Work. In the above two cases, double the amount of prescribed Viva-voce examination fee shall be collected from the students."},
  {"id": 158, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.8.6", "heading": "A student may, however, in certain cases, be permitted to work on the", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "A student may, however, in certain cases, be permitted to work on the project in an Industry / Research organization on the recommendation of the Head of the Department and Dean (FET), with the approval of the Dean (Academic Courses). In such cases, the project work shall be jointly supervised by a faculty member (project guide) of the department and an expert from the organization (project coordinator) and the student shall be instructed to report the progress periodically and to attend the project reviews for evaluating the progress. The student will produce a certificate of attendance from the Industry / Research organization where the project is carried out. In case of industrial projects, the marks allotted for the project guide will be shared equally by the guide from the department and the coordinator from the industry."},
  {"id": 159, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.9", "heading": "Assessment for Seminar / Professional Practices", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Assessment for Seminar / Professional Practices The Seminar / Professional Practices / Case study / Mini-Project shall carry 100 marks and shall be evaluated through continuous assessment only. Every student is expected to present a minimum of 2 presentations / demonstration per semester before the evaluation committee and for each presentation / demonstration, marks can be equally apportioned. The three-member committee consisting of one coordinator and two members appointed by the HOD will evaluate the performance of the student in above activities at the end of the semester, the marks can be consolidated and taken as the final mark. The evaluation shall be based on the seminar paper / report (40 marks), presentation / demonstration (40 marks) and response to the questions asked during presentation / demonstration (20 marks). The final marks obtained by each student in all the above activities should be consolidated and submitted to the Office of Dean (Academic Courses) which in turn should be submitted to Controller of Examinations at the end of each semester. The consolidated final mark obtained by each student is converted to 20 marks and to be utilized as stated in the Clause R13.5.2."},
  {"id": 160, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.10", "heading": "Assessment for Industrial / Practical Training / Internship /", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Assessment for Industrial / Practical Training / Internship / Summer Project The Industrial / Practical Training shall carry 100 marks and shall be evaluated through continuous assessment only. At the end of the Industrial / Practical Training / Internship / Summer Project, the student shall submit a certificate from the organization where the student has undergone training and a brief report about the training. The evaluation will be made based on this report (40 marks), presentation (30 marks) and a Viva-Voce Examination (30 marks). The viva-voce examination will be conducted by a three-member committee constituted by the Head of the Department. The committee comprises of one expert from an industry / organization and two members (a coordinator and a member) from the department. Certificates (issued by the Organization) of the student along with his / her mark statement should be submitted by the concerned Head of the Department / Dean (FET) to the Office of Dean (Academic Courses) which in turn should be submitted to Controller of Examinations at the end of each semester."},
  {"id": 161, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.11", "heading": "ASSESSMENT OF SEMESTER LONG INDUSTRIAL PROJECT", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "ASSESSMENT OF SEMESTER LONG INDUSTRIAL PROJECT / INTERNSHIP"},
  {"id": 162, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.11.1", "heading": "The Viva-voce examination for semester long industrial project or", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "The Viva-voce examination for semester long industrial project or internship shall be based on the report submitted by the student regarding the work carried out in the industrial project or internship. The students must produce an attendance certificate at the time of reviews. The report shall be certified by the coordinator from the industry, supervisor and Head of the Department."},
  {"id": 163, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.11.2", "heading": "Projects / internships undertaken externally should have an internal", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Projects / internships undertaken externally should have an internal guide and an external guide. Both guides are expected to interact regularly monitoring the progress of the student. For the reviews, the external guide should be present at least in online mode to assess and award marks to the student. In the beginning of the project, the internal guide should ensure that the work to be carried out is up to the standard as well as not attracting any IPR issues with the external organization so that the work could be published."},
  {"id": 164, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.11.3", "heading": "The reviews may be conducted in online mode, if the student cannot", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "The reviews may be conducted in online mode, if the student cannot travel to the institution to attend the reviews and this shall be approved by Head of the Department, and such reviews must be recorded. However, the end semester examination must be conducted in physical mode with the coordinator from the industry present physically or through online."},
  {"id": 165, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.11.4", "heading": "In the final report, the Bonafide certificate shall be mandatorily signed by", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "In the final report, the Bonafide certificate shall be mandatorily signed by both the guides. However, if any difficulty is encountered in fulfilling this norm, then the Head of the Department and Dean (FET) can initiate remedial action and complete the evaluation requirement with justification and approval of the Dean (Academic courses) for the same."},
  {"id": 166, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.11.5", "heading": "The Bonafide certificate of the project report shall have the date of Viva", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "The Bonafide certificate of the project report shall have the date of Viva -voce examination and the signatures of the internal and external guides."},
  {"id": 167, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.11.6", "heading": "If the project report or report of industrial project or internship is not", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "If the project report or report of industrial project or internship is not submitted on or before the specified deadline, an extension of time up to a maximum limit of 30 days may be given for the submission of report with due approval obtained from the Head of the Department. If the report is not submitted even beyond the extended time, then the student(s) is deemed to have failed in the Project Work and the student must redo the course again. In the above two cases, double the amount of prescribed Viva-voce examination fee shall be collected from the students."},
  {"id": 168, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.12", "heading": "Assessment for Value Added Courses", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Assessment for Value Added Courses This one / two credit course shall carry 100 marks and shall be evaluated through continuous assessments only. One or two assessments shall be conducted during the semester by the department concerned. The Head of the Department may identify a faculty member as coordinator for the course. A committee consisting of the Head of the Department, faculty handling the course (if available), coordinator and a senior faculty member nominated by the Head of the Department shall monitor the evaluation process. The grades shall be assigned to the students by the above committee based on their relative performance. Certificates issued by the industry if any along with the student's mark / grade statement should be submitted by the concerned Head of the Department through Dean (FET) to the Office of Dean (Academic Courses) which in turn should be submitted to Controller of Examinations at the end of each semester."},
  {"id": 169, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.13", "heading": "Assessment for Online Courses", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Assessment for Online Courses Students may be permitted to credit online courses (NPTEL / SWAYAM / other online platforms) with the approval of the Dean (Academic Courses), subject to a maximum of six credits."},
  {"id": 170, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.13.1", "heading": "On successful completion of the online course, the candidate must submit", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "On successful completion of the online course, the candidate must submit the copy of the certificate and the grade card (if applicable) to the Head of the Department."},
  {"id": 171, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.13.2", "heading": "The Head of the Department shall form a team of faculty members to", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "The Head of the Department shall form a team of faculty members to recommend the credit and grade to be awarded to the candidate by mapping the score earned by the student and results shall be submitted to the Office of Dean (Academic Courses) through Dean (FET) which in turn should be submitted to Controller of Examinations for further processing with due approval from Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 172, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.13.3", "heading": "If the grade card is not submitted by the student, the Head of the", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "If the grade card is not submitted by the student, the Head of the Department shall recommend the same to the Controller of Examinations through Dean (FET), and Dean (Academic Courses) to conduct end semester examination for the online course."},
  {"id": 173, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R13.14", "heading": "Continuous assessment marks approved by the Dean (Academic", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATION", "text": "Continuous assessment marks approved by the Dean (Academic Courses) shall be notified to the students by the respective Head of the Departments within 5 days from the last working day."},
  {"id": 174, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R14", "heading": "PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "PASSING REQUIREMENTS"},
  {"id": 175, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R14.1", "heading": "A student who secures not less than 50 percent of total marks", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "A student who secures not less than 50 percent of total marks prescribed for the course [Continuous Assessment + End Semester Examination] with a minimum of 40 percent of the marks prescribed for the end semester examination, shall be declared to have passed the course and acquired the relevant number of credits. This is applicable for all theory, laboratory, theory integrated with laboratory, laboratory integrated with theory courses (including project work)."},
  {"id": 176, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R14.2", "heading": "If the student gets less than 50 percent of total marks, then the student", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "If the student gets less than 50 percent of total marks, then the student will be awarded only RA (Reappearance) grade."},
  {"id": 177, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R14.3", "heading": "If a student fails to secure a pass in a course, the student shall register and", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "If a student fails to secure a pass in a course, the student shall register and appear for the end semester examination in the subsequent semester or appear for the supplementary examination vide Clause R15.7. In such a case, the Continuous Assessment marks obtained by the student in the first appearance shall be retained and considered valid for one subsequent arrear attempt. However, from the third attempt onwards, to pass the course, the candidate should secure either 50 percent of marks and above considering the sum of 40 percent of marks acquired in continuous assessment and 60 percent of marks earned in end semester examination (satisfying the passing requirement) or 50 percent of marks and above earned in end semester examination alone."},
  {"id": 178, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R14.4", "heading": "The students are allowed to write arrear examination as per Clause", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "The students are allowed to write arrear examination as per Clause R6.10.1."},
  {"id": 179, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R14.5", "heading": "If a student has submitted the project report but absent in the end semester", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "If a student has submitted the project report but absent in the end semester examination of project work, the student is deemed to be failed. If a student attends and fails in the End Semester examination of Project work, he / she shall attend the end semester examination again within 60 days from the date of declaration of the results. The subsequent viva-voce examination will be considered as reappearance with payment of examination fee. In case the student fails in the subsequent viva-voce examination also, the student shall redo the course again."},
  {"id": 180, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R14.6", "heading": "The passing requirement for the courses which are assessed only", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "The passing requirement for the courses which are assessed only through continuous assessment (employability enhancement courses such as value-added courses, skill development courses, online courses with one credit, and internship except project work), shall be fixed as minimum 50 percent and the rest of the grades are decided."},
  {"id": 181, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15", "heading": "AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "AWARD OF LETTER GRADES"},
  {"id": 182, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.1", "heading": "All assessments will be done based on marks. However, for the", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "All assessments will be done based on marks. However, for the purpose of reporting the performance of a student, letter grades, each carrying certain number of points will be awarded as per the range of total marks (out of 100) obtained by the candidate in each course as detailed below in the Table 10. The letter grades and the associated grade points are shown in Table 11. Table 10: Grade Distribution with Range of Marks O A+ A B+ B C RA 91-100 81-90 71-80 61-70 56-60 50-55 <50 An absolute grading system is followed in assigning grades to students for each course registered. Table 11: Letter Grades with Grade Points Letter Grade Grade Significance Grade Points O Outstanding 10 A+ Excellent 9 A Very Good 8 B+ Good 7 B Average 6 C Satisfactory 5 Reappearance RA 0 Registration Shortage of SA 0 Attendance W Withdrawal 0 i. \"RA\" denotes Reappearance required for the examination in the course and \"W\" denotes withdrawal from the course. ii. The Grade \"SA\" denotes inadequate attendance (as per Clause R7) and hence prevented from writing the end semester examination. iii. The Grade \"SA\" and \"W\" will figure only in the Result Sheets."},
  {"id": 183, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.2", "heading": "For the Extra-curricular activities such as NCC / NSS / NSO / YRC /", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "For the Extra-curricular activities such as NCC / NSS / NSO / YRC / RRC / Community Engagement and Social Responsibility, 2 credits are assigned in the curriculum. This shall appear in the grade sheet. In the NCC / NSS, every student shall put in a minimum of 75 percent attendance in the training and attend the camp compulsorily. A satisfactory grade in the above extra-curricular activities is compulsory for the award of a degree."},
  {"id": 184, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.3", "heading": "The training and camp shall be completed during the first year of the", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "The training and camp shall be completed during the first year of the programme. However, for valid reasons, the Head of the Department may permit a student to complete the requirement in the second year."},
  {"id": 185, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.4", "heading": "The grades obtained for the one / two credit value added courses shall", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "The grades obtained for the one / two credit value added courses shall figure in the grade sheet under the title \" Value Added Courses\" / \"Online Courses\". The other grades SA and W will not figure in the grade sheet."},
  {"id": 186, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.5", "heading": "GRADE SHEETS", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "GRADE SHEETS"},
  {"id": 187, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.5.1", "heading": "After the results are declared, Grade Sheets will be issued to each", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "After the results are declared, Grade Sheets will be issued to each student, which will contain the following details:  List of courses enrolled for that semester and the grades obtained by the student.  List of courses studied for the award of Honours / Minor / Specialization degree and any other additional courses in which the student has passed with the grades under the title of additional courses.  The Grade Point Average (GPA) for the semester considering only the courses listed in the curriculum (not the additional courses) and  The Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) of all courses registered from first semester onwards considering only the courses listed in the curriculum (not the additional courses).  However, for the students who have successfully completed the requirements of B. Tech. (Honours), B.Tech. with Specialization, and B.Tech. with Minor vide Clause R16.2, the grades scored in the additional courses required for Honours / Specialization / Minor degree shall be considered for the computation of CGPA."},
  {"id": 188, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.5.2", "heading": "The Grade Point Average (GPA) for each semester will be calculated", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "The Grade Point Average (GPA) for each semester will be calculated only for the students who have passed all the courses of that semester. Similarly, Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) up to any semester will be calculated only for the students who have passed all the courses up to that semester. GPA is the ratio of the sum of the products of the number of credits of curricular courses (Ci) registered and the grade points scored in those courses (GPi), taken for all the courses, to the sum of the number of credits of all the courses successfully cleared (n) during the particular semester. On successful completion of the programme, the CGPA will be calculated in a similar manner as follows, considering all the curricular courses (not the additional courses) enrolled from the first semester. ∑𝑁 𝑖=1 𝐶𝑖 × 𝐺𝑃𝑖 CGPA = ∑𝑁𝑖=0 𝐶𝑖 where N is the total number of courses for the entire programme."},
  {"id": 189, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.5.3", "heading": "If a student studies a greater number of professional and open electives", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "If a student studies a greater number of professional and open electives than required as per the student's programme curriculum (assuming the student decides not to opt for Honours and Minor), the calculation of the final CGPA shall be as per Clauses R16.2.6 and R16.2.7."},
  {"id": 190, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.5.4", "heading": "In the consolidated grade sheet, the CGPA earned shall be converted", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "In the consolidated grade sheet, the CGPA earned shall be converted into percentage of marks as follows: Percentage of Marks = CGPA X 10"},
  {"id": 191, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.5.5", "heading": "The Grade Point Average (GPA) for each semester will be included in", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "The Grade Point Average (GPA) for each semester will be included in the grade card or sheet, even if a student fails in one or more courses within the semester. In such cases, the GPA will be calculated based on the grades obtained in the courses the student has passed. Similarly, the Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) will also be calculated based on the grades obtained in all the courses the student has passed up to and including the current semester."},
  {"id": 192, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.6", "heading": "REVALUATION OF ANSWER SCRIPTS", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "REVALUATION OF ANSWER SCRIPTS A candidate can apply for photocopy of his / her semester examination answer paper in a theory course, within 2 weeks from the declaration of results, on payment of a prescribed fee through proper application to the Controller of Examination through the Head of Department. Students can see the valued answer scripts of the semester examinations and can get it retotaled / revalued by the faculty concerned. Based on the recommendation, the candidate can register for the revaluation through proper application to the Controller of Examination. The answer sheets will be revaluated and the results will be intimated to the student concerned through the Head of the Department. Revaluation is not permitted for practical courses, project phase 1 and phase 2 and Employability Enhancement Courses."},
  {"id": 193, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.7", "heading": "SUPPLEMENTARY EXAMINATION", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "SUPPLEMENTARY EXAMINATION"},
  {"id": 194, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.7.1", "heading": "Only those Students who obtained \"RA\" grade and have prescribed", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "Only those Students who obtained \"RA\" grade and have prescribed attendance and above in a course are eligible to apply for Supplementary Examination."},
  {"id": 195, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.7.2", "heading": "Registration shall be made for supplementary examination within the", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "Registration shall be made for supplementary examination within the stipulated period from the date of notification and the examination fee to be paid is double the amount of fee prescribed for the regular end semester examination."},
  {"id": 196, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.7.3", "heading": "A student is eligible for only one Supplementary Examination for any", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "A student is eligible for only one Supplementary Examination for any course. No second chance will be given. In case a student fails in the Supplementary Examination, he / she must rewrite the examination along with the regular stream in the subsequent semesters, as and when it is conducted."},
  {"id": 197, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.7.4", "heading": "Students who miss the end-semester examination due to valid medical or", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "Students who miss the end-semester examination due to valid medical or some other reason may be permitted with the consent of the Dean (Academic Courses) to appear for the supplementary examination(s) subject to fulfilling of attendance requirement (vide Clause R7)."},
  {"id": 198, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.7.5", "heading": "Supplementary Examinations will be conducted during the first two", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "Supplementary Examinations will be conducted during the first two weeks after the commencement of the next semester."},
  {"id": 199, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.7.6", "heading": "Supplementary examination will be considered as an alternative to the", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "Supplementary examination will be considered as an alternative to the end-semester examination only. The continuous assessment marks already secured by the students will be considered for finalizing the grade."},
  {"id": 200, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R15.7.7", "heading": "A minimum of 50 percent of marks prescribed for the end semester", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "A minimum of 50 percent of marks prescribed for the end semester examination should be scored in the supplementary examination(s) to declare the result as have passed the course and acquired the relevant number of credits."},
  {"id": 201, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16", "heading": "ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE"},
  {"id": 202, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.1", "heading": "A student shall be declared to be eligible for the award of the B.Tech.", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "A student shall be declared to be eligible for the award of the B.Tech. Degree provided the student has: i. Successfully gained the required number of total credits as specified in the curriculum corresponding to the programme within the stipulated duration. ii. Successfully completed the course requirements, appeared for the End Semester Examinations and passed all the courses prescribed in all the 8 semesters within a maximum duration of 7 years reckoned from the commencement of the first semester / 6 years reckoned from the commencement of the third semester in case of lateral entry scheme to which the student was admitted. iii. Successfully passed any additional courses prescribed by the Dean (Academic Courses). iv. Successfully completed the NCC / NSS / NSO / YRC / RRC requirements. v. No disciplinary action is pending against the student. vi. The award of Degree must have been approved by the Academic Council of the Institution."},
  {"id": 203, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2", "heading": "Classification of the Degree Awarded", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "Classification of the Degree Awarded Award of \"Honours\" Qualification"},
  {"id": 204, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.1", "heading": "\"Honours\" Degree shall be awarded to well performing UG students on", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "\"Honours\" Degree shall be awarded to well performing UG students on earning the specific additional credits as prescribed under vide Clause"},
  {"id": 205, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R4.18.1", "heading": "and satisfied the requirement (vide Clause R4.18.2) and after", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "and satisfied the requirement (vide Clause R4.18.2) and after satisfying the relevant degree award conditions."},
  {"id": 206, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.2", "heading": "Students should have obtained a CGPA >= 8.0 at the end of the eighth", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "Students should have obtained a CGPA >= 8.0 at the end of the eighth semester and have satisfied additional credits consideration prescribed for \"Honours\" degree."},
  {"id": 207, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.3", "heading": "The Dean (Academic Courses) of the Institution shall submit the list of", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "The Dean (Academic Courses) of the Institution shall submit the list of students who are eligible for the award of the \"Honours\" degree along with the total credits earned by each student to the Office of the Controller of Examinations. The list shall be validated by the Mentors of the students under consideration and endorsed by the Head of the Department."},
  {"id": 208, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.4", "heading": "If the students registered for \"Honours\" qualification cannot meet the", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "If the students registered for \"Honours\" qualification cannot meet the requirement as stated (vide Clauses R16.2.1 and R16.2.2), they shall not be considered for the award of \"Honours\" degree. However, they shall be awarded only a B.Tech. degree or B.Tech. degree with specialization if the students have opted for additional courses in the same domain."},
  {"id": 209, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.5", "heading": "Students may continue or deregister from the \"Honours\" qualification if", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "Students may continue or deregister from the \"Honours\" qualification if they do not meet the specified requirement."},
  {"id": 210, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.6", "heading": "If a student decides not to opt for Honours, after completing a certain", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "If a student decides not to opt for Honours, after completing a certain number of additional courses, such additional courses studied shall be considered instead of the Professional Elective Courses which are part of the Curriculum."},
  {"id": 211, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.7", "heading": "If the student has studied a greater number of such courses than the", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "If the student has studied a greater number of such courses than the number of Professional Elective courses required as per the curriculum, the courses with higher grades shall be considered for the calculation of CGPA. Remaining courses shall be printed in the grade sheet; however, they will not be considered for calculation of CGPA and the same shall be indicated in a foot note appropriately."},
  {"id": 212, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.8", "heading": "If the student has failed in the additional courses or faced shortage of", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "If the student has failed in the additional courses or faced shortage of attendance, they will not be printed in the grade sheet and will not be considered for CGPA calculation and classification of degree."},
  {"id": 213, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.9", "heading": "The \"Honours\" qualification shall be suffixed to the respective degrees", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "The \"Honours\" qualification shall be suffixed to the respective degrees and shown in the degree certificate as a recognition of higher achievement by the student concerned."},
  {"id": 214, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.10", "heading": "All the students fulfilling the requirement (vide Clauses R16.2.1 and", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "All the students fulfilling the requirement (vide Clauses R16.2.1 and R16.2.2) shall be entitled to receive the transcripts indicating both their achievements. Award of \"Minor\" Qualification"},
  {"id": 215, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.11", "heading": "All the students who successfully complete the additional courses as", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "All the students who successfully complete the additional courses as prescribed i.e., specialization in a specific domain offered by other departments and satisfied the requirement shall be eligible for the award of \"Minor\" degree."},
  {"id": 216, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.12", "heading": "The Dean (Academic Courses) of the Institution shall submit the list of", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "The Dean (Academic Courses) of the Institution shall submit the list of students who are eligible for the award of the \"Minor\" degree along with the total credits earned by each student to the Office of the Controller of Examinations. The list shall be validated by the Mentors of the students under consideration and endorsed by the Head of the Department."},
  {"id": 217, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.13", "heading": "If a student decides not to opt for a Minor degree, after completing a", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "If a student decides not to opt for a Minor degree, after completing a certain number of additional courses, such additional courses studied shall be considered instead of the Open Elective Courses which are part of the Curriculum."},
  {"id": 218, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.14", "heading": "If the student has studied a greater number of such courses than the", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "If the student has studied a greater number of such courses than the number of Open Elective courses required as per the curriculum, the courses with higher grades shall be considered for the calculation of CGPA. Remaining courses shall be printed on the grade sheet; however, they will not be considered for calculation of CGPA and the same shall be indicated in a foot note appropriately."},
  {"id": 219, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.15", "heading": "If the student has failed in the additional courses or faced shortage of", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "If the student has failed in the additional courses or faced shortage of attendance, they will not be printed in the grade sheet and will not be considered for CGPA calculation and classification of degree. Award of B.Tech. Degree with Specialization"},
  {"id": 220, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.16", "heading": "All the students who successfully complete the additional courses as", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "All the students who successfully complete the additional courses as prescribed, which are in the same programme domain (vertical) and satisfy the requirement shall be eligible for the award of B.Tech. degree with Specialization in that domain."},
  {"id": 221, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.17", "heading": "The Dean (Academic Courses) of the Institution shall submit the list of", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "The Dean (Academic Courses) of the Institution shall submit the list of students who are eligible for the award of the B.Tech. degree with specialization along with the total credits earned by each student to the Office of the Controller of Examinations. The list shall be validated by the Mentors of the students under consideration and endorsed by the Head of the Department."},
  {"id": 222, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.18", "heading": "If a student decides not to opt for specialization, after completing a certain", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "If a student decides not to opt for specialization, after completing a certain number of additional courses, such additional courses studied shall be considered instead of the Professional Elective / Open Elective Courses which are part of the Curriculum."},
  {"id": 223, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.19", "heading": "If the student has studied a greater number of such courses than the", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "If the student has studied a greater number of such courses than the number of Professional Elective / Open Elective courses required as per the curriculum, the courses with higher grades shall be considered for the calculation of CGPA. Remaining courses shall be printed on the grade sheet; however, they will not be considered for calculation of CGPA and the same shall be indicated in a foot note appropriately."},
  {"id": 224, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.20", "heading": "If the student has failed in the additional courses or faced shortage of", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "If the student has failed in the additional courses or faced shortage of attendance, they will not be printed in the grade sheet and will not be considered for CGPA calculation and classification of degree. First Class with Distinction"},
  {"id": 225, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.21", "heading": "A student who satisfies the following conditions shall be declared to", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "A student who satisfies the following conditions shall be declared to have passed the examination in First class with Distinction: i) Should have passed the examination in all the courses of all the eight semesters in first appearance within five years (four years in case of lateral entry students), which includes authorized break of study of one year. Withdrawal from examination (vide Clause R18) will not be construed as an appearance. ii) Should have secured a CGPA of not less than 8.00. iii) Should not have been prevented from writing end semester examination due to lack of attendance in any of the courses. The authorized break of study (vide Clause R17) and withdrawal from theexamination (vide Clause R18) will not be construed as an attempt. First Class"},
  {"id": 226, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.22", "heading": "A student who satisfies the following conditions shall be declared to", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "A student who satisfies the following conditions shall be declared to have passed the examination in First class: i) Should have passed the examination in all the courses of all eight semesters within five years (four years in case of lateral entry students), which includes one year of authorized break of study (if availed) or prevention from writing the End Semester Examination due to lack of attendance (if applicable). ii) Should have secured a CGPA of not less than 6.50. The authorized break of study (vide Clause R17) and withdrawal from theexamination (vide Clause R18) will not be construed as an attempt. Second Class"},
  {"id": 227, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.23", "heading": "All other students (not covered in Clauses R16.2.21 and R16.2.22) who", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "All other students (not covered in Clauses R16.2.21 and R16.2.22) who qualify for the award of the degree (vide Clause R16) shall be awarded Second Class."},
  {"id": 228, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.24", "heading": "A student who is absent in the end semester examination in a course /", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "A student who is absent in the end semester examination in a course / project work after having registered for the same shall be considered to have appeared in that examination (except approved withdrawal from end semester examinations as per Clause R18) for the purpose of classification."},
  {"id": 229, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R16.2.25", "heading": "Student earned additional 20 credits as per Clause R4.18 but does not", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "Student earned additional 20 credits as per Clause R4.18 but does not satisfy the conditions mentioned in Clauses R16.2.1 or R16.2.2 shall not be awarded B.Tech. (Honours). In such a case if the student becomes eligible for first class, while computing with the Professional Elective / Open Elective Courses with higher grades, the student shall be awarded B.Tech. in First Class only."},
  {"id": 230, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R17", "heading": "PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY"},
  {"id": 231, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R17.1", "heading": "Break of Study shall be granted by the Dean (Academic Courses) only", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "Break of Study shall be granted by the Dean (Academic Courses) only once for valid reasons for a period of maximum one year during the entire period of study of the degree programme."},
  {"id": 232, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R17.2", "heading": "Prescribed fee to the Institution should be paid during the \"Break of", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "Prescribed fee to the Institution should be paid during the \"Break of Study\" period."},
  {"id": 233, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R17.3", "heading": "The student permitted to re-join after the break of study / prevention due", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "The student permitted to re-join after the break of study / prevention due to lack of attendance, shall be governed by the Curriculum and Regulations in force at the time of re-joining. If the Regulation is changed, then, those students may have to take up additional courses as prescribed by the Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 234, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R17.4", "heading": "Total number of credits to be earned by the student shall be more than or", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "Total number of credits to be earned by the student shall be more than or equal to the total number of credits prescribed in the curriculum in force. If the credit assigned for L T P of the courses are not same in two Regulations under consideration, then equivalence shall be arrived as per the credit assignment followed in the Regulations in force."},
  {"id": 235, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R17.5", "heading": "The authorized break of study (for a maximum of one year) will not be", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "The authorized break of study (for a maximum of one year) will not be counted for the duration specified for passing all the courses for the purpose of classification. (vide Clause R16.2)."},
  {"id": 236, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R17.6", "heading": "The total period for completion of the programme reckoned from, the", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "The total period for completion of the programme reckoned from, the commencement of the first semester (third semester for Lateral Entry Scheme) to which the candidate was admitted shall not exceed the maximum period specified in Clause R5 irrespective of the period of break of study in order that he / she may be eligible for the award of the degree."},
  {"id": 237, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R17.7", "heading": "If any student is detained for lack of requisite attendance, progress and", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "If any student is detained for lack of requisite attendance, progress and good conduct, the period spent in that semester shall not be considered as permitted \"Break of Study\" or \"Withdrawal\" (Clause R18) is not applicable for this case."},
  {"id": 238, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R17.8", "heading": "In case there is any period of break of study more than the permitted", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "In case there is any period of break of study more than the permitted duration of break of study, the student shall be permitted to continue the programme only if the approval is obtained from the Dean (Academic Courses) through the concerned Head of the Department and Dean (FET) before the end of the semester in which the student has taken break of study."},
  {"id": 239, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R17.9", "heading": "If the student has not reported back to the department, after the break of", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "If the student has not reported back to the department, after the break of study, his / her name shall be deleted permanently from the Institution enrollment and the same should be informed to his / her parents immediately. Such students are entitled to seek permission from the Executive Council to continue the programme."},
  {"id": 240, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R17.10", "heading": "If a student in Full Time mode wants to take up job / start-up /", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "If a student in Full Time mode wants to take up job / start-up / entrepreneurship during the period of study, he / she shall apply for authorized break of study for one year. The student shall take up the assignment only after getting approval of the same by the Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 241, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R18", "heading": "PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL                      FROM        THE       END", "text": "PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END SEMESTER EXAMINATIONS"},
  {"id": 242, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R18.1", "heading": "A student may, for valid reasons (medically unfit / unexpected family", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL                      FROM        THE       END", "text": "A student may, for valid reasons (medically unfit / unexpected family situation / Sports approved by the Director (Sports) and Head of the Department) and on prior application, be granted permission to withdraw from appearing for one examination of one course or two or more consecutive examinations of different courses in the end semester examination. Permission cannot be given to withdraw from the examinations in a non-consecutive sequence."},
  {"id": 243, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R18.2", "heading": "Such withdrawal shall be permitted only once during the entire period of", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL                      FROM        THE       END", "text": "Such withdrawal shall be permitted only once during the entire period of study of the degree programme."},
  {"id": 244, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R18.3", "heading": "Withdrawal application is valid only if the student is otherwise eligible", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL                      FROM        THE       END", "text": "Withdrawal application is valid only if the student is otherwise eligible to write the examination (vide Clause R7) and if it is made within 10 days prior to the commencement of the end semester examination and recommended by the Head of the Department and Dean (FET) and approved by the Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 245, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R18.4", "heading": "Notwithstanding the requirement of mandatory 10 days' notice,", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL                      FROM        THE       END", "text": "Notwithstanding the requirement of mandatory 10 days' notice, applications for withdrawal for special cases under extraordinary conditions will be considered on the merit of the case."},
  {"id": 246, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R18.5", "heading": "Withdrawal shall not be construed as an appearance for the eligibility of", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL                      FROM        THE       END", "text": "Withdrawal shall not be construed as an appearance for the eligibility of a student for First Class with Distinction. This provision is not applicable to those who seek withdrawal during VIII semester."},
  {"id": 247, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R18.6", "heading": "Withdrawal from the end semester examination is NOT applicable to", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL                      FROM        THE       END", "text": "Withdrawal from the end semester examination is NOT applicable to arrear courses of previous semesters."},
  {"id": 248, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R18.7", "heading": "The student shall appear for the end semester examination with respect", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL                      FROM        THE       END", "text": "The student shall appear for the end semester examination with respect to the withdrawn courses during the examination conducted in the subsequent semester / supplementary examination in the same semester and need not re-appear for the continuous assessment examination."},
  {"id": 249, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R18.8", "heading": "Withdrawal from the continuous assessment examination is not", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL                      FROM        THE       END", "text": "Withdrawal from the continuous assessment examination is not permitted."},
  {"id": 250, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R18.9", "heading": "Withdrawal is not permitted to the student who has not satisfied the", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL                      FROM        THE       END", "text": "Withdrawal is not permitted to the student who has not satisfied the conditions prescribed in Clause R7 as requirements for appearing in the end semester examination."},
  {"id": 251, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R19", "heading": "DISCIPLINE", "section": "R19. DISCIPLINE", "text": "DISCIPLINE The Institution reserves the right to cancel the admission of any student and ask him / her to discontinue his / her studies at any stage of his / her career on the grounds of unsatisfactory academic performance or misbehavior and conduct."},
  {"id": 252, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R19.1", "heading": "Every student is required to observe discipline and decorous behaviour", "section": "R19. DISCIPLINE", "text": "Every student is required to observe discipline and decorous behaviour both inside and outside the Institution and not to indulge in any activity which will tend to bring down the prestige of the institution."},
  {"id": 253, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R19.2", "heading": "Any act of indiscipline of a student reported to the Dean (Academic", "section": "R19. DISCIPLINE", "text": "Any act of indiscipline of a student reported to the Dean (Academic Courses) will be referred to a Discipline and Welfare Committee constituted by the Vice Chancellor. The Committee will enquire into the charges and recommend suitable punishment if the charges are substantiated. The Vice Chancellor will consider the recommendation of the Discipline and Welfare Committee for appropriate action."},
  {"id": 254, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R19.3", "heading": "If a student indulges in malpractice in any of the end semester", "section": "R19. DISCIPLINE", "text": "If a student indulges in malpractice in any of the end semester examination / continuous assessment tests, he / she shall be liable for punitive action as prescribed by the institution from time to time."},
  {"id": 255, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R19.4", "heading": "Ragging of any dimension is a criminal and nonbailable offence in our", "section": "R19. DISCIPLINE", "text": "Ragging of any dimension is a criminal and nonbailable offence in our country. The current State and Central legislations provide for stringent punishment, including imprisonment. Once the involvement of a studentis established in ragging, the offending student will be dismissed from the Institution and will not be admitted into any other Institution. Avenues also exist for collective punishment if individual cannot be identified in this inhuman act. Every student of the Institution, along with the parent, shall give an undertaking every year in this regard."},
  {"id": 256, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R20", "heading": "REVISION OF REGULATIONS AND CURRICULUM", "section": "R20. REVISION OF REGULATIONS AND CURRICULUM", "text": "REVISION OF REGULATIONS AND CURRICULUM The Academic Council of the Institution reserves the right to revise, amend or change the regulations, the curriculum, syllabus and the scheme of examinations from time to time if found necessary and shall send the recommendations to the Executive Council for approval."},
  {"id": 257, "doc": "ug", "clause": "R21", "heading": "SPECIAL CASES", "section": "R21. SPECIAL CASES", "text": "SPECIAL CASES In the event of any clarification in the interpretation of the above regulations, they shall be referred to the Standing Committee (Internal members of the Academic Council). The Standing Committee will offer suitable interpretation / clarification required for special case on such references and get them ratified in the next meeting of the Academic Council. The decision of the Academic Council is final."},
  {"id": 258, "doc": "pg", "clause": "Preamble", "heading": "Institute Profile: Vision, Mission, Quality Policy, Objectives, Motto", "section": "Preamble", "text": "PERIYAR MANIAMMAI INSTITUTE OF SCIENCE & TECHNOLOGY Periyar Nagar, Vallam, Thanjavur - 613403 Tamil Nadu, India Periyar Maniammai Institute of Science & Technology is committed to imparting quality education, emphasizing the integration of proficiency and human values, along with the ongoing enhancement of educational quality. Vision Statement: To be a university of global dynamism with excellence in knowledge and innovation, ensuring social responsibility for creating an egalitarian society. Mission:  Offering well-balanced programs with scholarly faculty and state-of-the-art facilities to impart a high level of knowledge.  Providing student-centered education and fostering their growth in critical thinking, creativity, entrepreneurship, problem-solving, and collaborative work.  Engaging in progressive and meaningful research with a focus on sustainable development.  Empowering students to acquire the skills necessary for global competencies.  Instilling universal values, self-respect, gender equality, dignity, and ethics. Quality Policy: To be a leading institution of excellence in education and research, providing professional competence to meet academic, scholastic, and societal needs. Objectives:  To provide value-based education with social responsibility and ethics to both urban and underserved rural students.  To achieve excellence in education and empower students to attain global competence.  To promote a culture of research and innovation in young minds, fostering academic excellence, and encouraging lifelong learning.  To engage in specialized areas with a proven ability to make distinctive contributions to the objectives of the higher education system across diverse disciplines.  To engage in extramural studies, extension programmes, and field outreach activities to contribute to the development of society. The Motto: THINK – INNOVATE – TRANSFORM PERIYAR MANIAMMAI INSTITUTE OF SCIENCE & TECHNOLOGY PG REGULATIONS: R-2024 CHOICE BASED CREDIT SYSTEM (CBCS) (Common to all M.A. / MBA / MCA / M.Sc. / MSW / M.Com. / M.Tech. - 2 Years Programmes) Full-Time Programmes (4 Semesters) (with effect from the academic year 2024 - 2025)"},
  {"id": 259, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R1 (part 1)", "heading": "DEFINITIONS AND NOMENCLATURE", "section": "R1. DEFINITIONS AND NOMENCLATURE", "text": "DEFINITIONS AND NOMENCLATURE i. \"Institute\" means Periyar Maniammai Institute of Science & Technology (Deemed to be University). ii. \"Degree\" refers to the academic award conferred upon a student on successful completion of a programme designed to achieve the defined attributes. It is referred to as a Postgraduate (PG) Degree, that is M.A. / MBA / MCA / M.Sc. / MSW / M.Com. / M.Tech. Degree. iii. \"Discipline\" means branch of a M.Tech. Degree Programme, like Computer Science and Engineering, Environmental Engineering etc. / branch of a M.Sc. Degree Programme, like Computer Science, Data Science etc. / Arts Degree Programmes in Computer Applications / Business Administration / English / Tamil / Commerce / Social Work. iv. \"Programme\" means cohesive arrangement of courses, co-curricular and extracurricular activities to accomplish predetermined objectives leading to awarding of a degree. v. \"Course\" means a theory / practical / theory integrated with practical / practical integrated with theory subject studied in a semester, like Applied Mathematics, Operating Systems, Advanced Data Structures, Community Engagement and Social Responsibility, Operations Management etc. vi. \"Dean (Academic Courses)\" means the authority of the Institute who is responsible for all the academic activities of the departments for implementation of relevant rules and regulations. vii. \"Faculty Dean\" means the Dean of the Faculty concerned. viii. \"Controller of Examinations\" means the authority of the Institute who is responsible for all the activities of the examinations. ix."},
  {"id": 260, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R1 (part 2)", "heading": "DEFINITIONS AND NOMENCLATURE", "section": "R1. DEFINITIONS AND NOMENCLATURE", "text": "\"HoD\" means the Head of the Department concerned. x. \"BoS\" means Board of Studies for each programme offered in the department. xi. \"Chairperson, BoS\" means Chairperson of Board of Studies. xii. \"Department Advisory Committee\" means the committee constituted by the Institute for approving academic matters of the department. xiii. \"Specialization\" means award of a programme with specific courses on thrust areas or as per the industrial / research requirement. xiv. \"E-Resources\" means learning materials saved electronically in online storage or cloud platform, which shall be accessed from anywhere and anytime online or shall be accessed offline by downloading the relevant materials. xv. \"MOOCs\" means Massive Open Online Courses available at both introductory and advanced levels accessible from \"E-Resources\". xvi. \"AICTE\" means All India Council for Technical Education established at New Delhi. xvii. \"UGC\" means University Grants Commission established at New Delhi. xviii. \"Academic Council\" means the approval granting authority for all academic related activities like framing of academic policies, approval of regulations, courses, syllabus etc. xix. \"Bonafide Student\" means one who has enrolled for at least one course in the curriculum as per regulations and has paid the tuition fee for the same. xx. \"MoU\" means the agreement signed between two parties either in India or Abroad to improve academic standards."},
  {"id": 261, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2", "heading": "ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "ADMISSION PROCEDURE"},
  {"id": 262, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1", "heading": "Regular Admission", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Regular Admission The students seeking admission to the Master of Technology / Master of Computer Applications / Master of Science / Master of Commerce / Master of Social work / Master of Arts / Master of Business Administration programmes shall require satisfying eligibility criteria as prescribed by the Institute from time to time."},
  {"id": 263, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.1", "heading": "Students for admission to the first semester of the Post Graduate Degree", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Students for admission to the first semester of the Post Graduate Degree Programme shall be required to have passed an appropriate qualifying Degree Examination accepted by the Executive Council of the Institute."},
  {"id": 264, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.2", "heading": "The Executive Council of the Institute may decide to restrict admission", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "The Executive Council of the Institute may decide to restrict admission in any particular year to students having the subset of qualifications prescribed at the time of admission."},
  {"id": 265, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.3", "heading": "Eligibility conditions for admission such as marks, class obtained, the", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Eligibility conditions for admission such as marks, class obtained, the number of attempts in the qualifying examination and physical fitness shall be as prescribed by the Institute from time to time."},
  {"id": 266, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.4", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of the M.A. degree", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of the M.A. degree programme in Tamil, English, Political Science, History, or Periyar Thought or MSW (Master of Social Work) degree programme must have completed a Bachelor's degree with a minimum duration of three years from a recognized University or Institution."},
  {"id": 267, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.5", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of the MBA degree", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of the MBA degree programme shall be required to have passed any Bachelor's degree with a minimum duration of 3 years from a recognized University or Institution with at least 50% of marks (45% in case of candidates belonging to reserved category) in the qualifying examination. The candidate should have qualified in TANCET / MAT / CAT / PMIST Entrance Examination or any equivalent State / National level Entrance Examination."},
  {"id": 268, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.6", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of the MCA degree", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of the MCA degree programme shall be required to have passed a 3-year BCA / B.Sc. Computer Science / B.Sc. Information Technology or any other equivalent degree. OR Should have passed a 3-year B.Sc. / B.Com. / B.A. / B.Voc. etc., preferably with Mathematics at 10+2 level or at undergraduate level. OR Candidates with 4-year B.E. or B.Tech. degree programme in any discipline. AND The candidate should have obtained the Bachelor's degree from a recognized University or Institution with at least 50% of marks (45% in case of candidates belonging to reserved category) in the qualifying examination."},
  {"id": 269, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.7", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M. Com. degree", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M. Com. degree programme shall be required to have passed a bachelor's degree with a minimum duration of 3 years in Commerce / Accounting and Finance / Professional Accounting / Corporate Secretaryship / Commerce with Computer Applications / Banking Management / Financial Management / Business Administration / Banking from a recognized University or Institution with at least 50% of marks (45% in case of candidates belonging to reserved category) in the qualifying examination."},
  {"id": 270, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.8", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Sc. Mathematics", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Sc. Mathematics degree programme shall be required to have passed a bachelor's degree with a minimum duration of 3 years in Mathematics / Applied Mathematics or Integrated B.Sc. B.Ed. with Mathematics as one of the core courses or any other equivalent degree in relevant discipline from a recognized University or Institution."},
  {"id": 271, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.9", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Sc. Physics degree", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Sc. Physics degree programme shall be required to have passed a bachelor's degree with a minimum duration of 3 years in Physics / Applied Physics or Integrated B.Sc. B.Ed. with Physics as one of the core courses or any other equivalent degree in relevant discipline from a recognized University or Institution."},
  {"id": 272, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.10", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year M.Sc. Chemistry degree", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year M.Sc. Chemistry degree programme shall be required to have obtained a bachelor's degree with a minimum duration of 3 years in Chemistry / Applied Chemistry or Integrated B.Sc. B.Ed. with Chemistry as one of the core courses or any other equivalent degree in relevant discipline from a recognized University or Institution."},
  {"id": 273, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.11", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Sc. Biotechnology", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Sc. Biotechnology degree programme shall be required to have passed a bachelor's degree with a minimum duration of 3 years such as Biotechnology / Chemistry / Biochemistry / Micro biology / Botany / Zoology / Applied Chemistry or Integrated B.Sc. B.Ed. with Chemistry as one of the core courses from a recognized University or Institution."},
  {"id": 274, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.12", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Sc. Computer", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Sc. Computer Science / M.Sc. Data Science / M.Sc. Computer Science (Augmented Reality and Virtual Reality) degree programme shall be required to have passed a bachelor's degree with a minimum duration of 3 years such as B.Sc. (Computer Science / Information Technology / Data Science / Software Engineering / Artificial Intelligence / Cyber Security or equivalent) / B.C.A. degree or any other equivalent degree with Computer Science or Mathematics as a core course from a recognized University or Institution."},
  {"id": 275, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.13", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Tech. Environmental", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Tech. Environmental Engineering degree programme shall be required to have passed B.E or B.Tech. in Civil Engineering / Chemical Engineering / Biotechnology / Geo-Informatics / Mechanical Engineering / Electrical and Electronics Engineering / Agriculture Engineering or any other related programme from a recognized University or Institution with at least 50% of marks (45% in case of candidates belonging to reserved category) in the qualifying examination."},
  {"id": 276, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.14", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Tech.", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Tech. Nanotechnology degree programme shall be required to have passed B.E or B.Tech. in Biotechnology / Electrical and Electronics Engineering / Electronics and Communication Engineering / Mechanical Engineering / Chemical Engineering / M.Sc. in Physics / Chemistry / Biochemistry or any other related field from a recognized University or Institution with at least 50% of marks (45% in case of candidates belonging to reserved category) in the qualifying examination."},
  {"id": 277, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.15", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Tech. Renewable", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Tech. Renewable Energy degree programme shall be required to have passed B.E or B.Tech. in. Mechanical Engineering / Chemical Engineering / Biotechnology / Electro Chemical Engineering / Electrical and Electronics Engineering or any other related field from a recognized University or Institution with at least 50% of marks (45% in case of candidates belonging to reserved category) in the qualifying examination."},
  {"id": 278, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.16", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Tech. Wireless", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Tech. Wireless Communication degree programme shall be required to have passed B.E. / B.Tech. in Electronics and Communication Engineering / Tele Communication Engineering / Information Technology / Electrical and Electronics Engineering or any other related field from a recognized University or Institution with at least 50% of marks (45% in case of candidates belonging to reserved category) in the qualifying examination."},
  {"id": 279, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.17", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Tech. Power", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Tech. Power Electronics and Drives degree programme shall be required to have passed B.E. / B.Tech. in Electrical and Electronics Engineering / Electronics and Communication Engineering / Electronics and Instrumentation Engineering or any other related field from a recognized University or Institution with at least 50% of marks (45% in case of candidates belonging to reserved category) in the qualifying examination."},
  {"id": 280, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.1.18", "heading": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Tech. Computer", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Candidates seeking admission to the first year of M.Tech. Computer Science and Engineering degree programme shall be required to have passed B.E. or B.Tech. in Computer Science and Engineering / Information Technology / MCA degree or any other related field from a recognized University or Institution with at least 50% of marks (45% in case of candidates belonging to reserved category) in the qualifying examination."},
  {"id": 281, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.2", "heading": "Credit Requirements for Admission", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Credit Requirements for Admission"},
  {"id": 282, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.2.1", "heading": "A 3-year bachelor's degree with a minimum of 120 credits is eligible for", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "A 3-year bachelor's degree with a minimum of 120 credits is eligible for MA / MBA / MCA / M.Com. / M.Sc. / MSW degree programmes."},
  {"id": 283, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.2.2", "heading": "A 4-year bachelor's degree B.E. / B. Tech. with a minimum of 160 credits", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "A 4-year bachelor's degree B.E. / B. Tech. with a minimum of 160 credits is eligible for the M.Tech. degree programme."},
  {"id": 284, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.2.3", "heading": "A 4-year bachelor's degree with Honours / Honours with Research with", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "A 4-year bachelor's degree with Honours / Honours with Research with a minimum of 160 credits is eligible for a 1-year (2 semesters) MA / MBA / MCA / M.Com. / M.Sc. / MSW degree programme."},
  {"id": 285, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.3", "heading": "A student is eligible for a Master's Programme in a discipline", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "A student is eligible for a Master's Programme in a discipline corresponding to either major or minor discipline in UG programme. In this case, the Institute can admit the students in the Master's Programme based on the student's performance in the UG programme."},
  {"id": 286, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.4", "heading": "Irrespective of the major or minor disciplines chosen by a student in a", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "Irrespective of the major or minor disciplines chosen by a student in a UG programme, a student is also eligible for admission in any discipline of a Master's Programme if the student qualifies the National level or Institute level entrance examination in the discipline of the Master's Programme."},
  {"id": 287, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R2.5", "heading": "If, at any time after admission, it is found that a candidate has not fulfilled", "section": "R2. ADMISSION PROCEDURE", "text": "If, at any time after admission, it is found that a candidate has not fulfilled any of the requirements stipulated by the Institute, the Dean (Academic Courses) may revoke the admission of the candidate and report the matter to the Registrar for further action."},
  {"id": 288, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R3", "heading": "PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "section": "R3. PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "text": "PROGRAMMES OF STUDY"},
  {"id": 289, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R3.1", "heading": "A student may be given admission to any one of the programmes of study", "section": "R3. PROGRAMMES OF STUDY", "text": "A student may be given admission to any one of the programmes of study (as given in the following table) approved by AICTE / UGC and offered at the Institute. Sl. Programme Name of the PG Programme No. Code 1. M.A. English EN 2. M.A. Tamil TA 3. M.A. History HY 4. M.A. Periyar Thought PT 5. M.A. Political Science PS 6. M.C.A. Master of Computer Applications CA 7. M.Com. MC 8. M.Sc. Mathematics MS 9. M.Sc. Physics PH 10. M.Sc. Chemistry CH 11. M.Sc. Data Science DS 12. M.Sc. Computer Science CO 13. M.Sc. Computer Science (AR & VR) CR 14. M.Sc. Biotechnology BY M.B.A. Dual Specialization  Finance  Human Resource 15.  Marketing MB  Operations  Business Analytics 16. MSW Master of Social Work SW 17. M.Tech. Computer Science and Engineering CS 18. M.Tech. Environmental Engineering ER 19. M.Tech. Nano Technology NT 20. M.Tech. Power Electronics and Drives PE 21. M.Tech. Renewable Energy RE 22. M.Tech. Wireless Communication WC"},
  {"id": 290, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4", "heading": "STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES"},
  {"id": 291, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.1", "heading": "Categorization of Courses", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Categorization of Courses Every M.A. / MBA / MCA / M.Com. / M.Sc. / MSW / M.Tech. degree programme shall have a curriculum with syllabus comprising of Theory, Theory Integrated with Practical, Practical Integrated with Theory, and Practical courses with well-defined Programme Educational Objectives (PEOs), Programme Specific Outcomes (PSOs), and Programme Outcomes (POs) as per Outcome Based Education (OBE). The content of each course is designed based on the Course Outcomes (COs). The programmes shall cover the following category of courses as per the guidelines of / UGC / AICTE. a. Foundation Courses Include Mathematics, Universal Human Values, Communication skills, Management courses, and other basic courses with respect to each discipline. b. Professional Core Courses include the core courses relevant to the chosen specialization / branch. c. Professional Elective Courses include the elective courses relevant to the chosen specialization / branch. d. Open Elective Course shall provide an opportunity to study a course from any discipline that includes the course relevant to the chosen specialization, the course that enhances soft and managerial skills, the course a student can choose from the curriculum of other Master's degree programmes and the course offered by the other departments such as Indian Knowledge System, any course of study relevant to societal development, and other courses relevant for higher studies / research etc. e. Employability Enhancement Courses include Internship, Career Development Skills, Creative and Innovative Projects, Coding Techniques, Seminar, Professional Practices, Value Added Courses, Case Study, and Industrial Training. f. Online Courses allow the students to habituate independent learning through Massive Open Online Courses (MOOCs) restricted to NPTEL, SWAYAM and other courses offered online by premier Universities or Institutions. g. Research Methodology and IPR Course includes topics on the process of research and creation of patents through research. There must be a minimum number of core courses and enough elective courses available for students to choose from. The combination of various courses should be designed in a way that, by the end of the programme, students are not only well-prepared for their specific professional fields but also have developed a sense of social consciousness. The credit requirements for each category of courses are outlined in Table 1."},
  {"id": 292, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.2", "heading": "Every MA / MBA / MCA / M.Com. / M.Sc. / MSW / M. Tech. degree", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Every MA / MBA / MCA / M.Com. / M.Sc. / MSW / M. Tech. degree programme will have a balanced curriculum as per UGC / AICTE guidelines and syllabus for the courses with required outcomes approved by the Academic Council."},
  {"id": 293, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.3", "heading": "The curriculum of any M.A. / MBA / MCA / M.Com. / M.Sc. / MSW /", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The curriculum of any M.A. / MBA / MCA / M.Com. / M.Sc. / MSW / M. Tech. degree programme is designed to include a maximum of 80 credits for the award of the degree. Table 1. Credit Requirements for each category of Courses Sl. No. Category of Courses Credits Foundation Courses (Humanities and Social Sciences including 1. 8 Management Courses, Basic Science and Engineering Science Courses with respect to each discipline) 2. Professional Core Courses 30 3. Professional Elective Courses 9 Open Elective Course (Soft and Managerial Skills, Core and Elective Courses 4. 3 offered by other Departments, Indian Knowledge System, Economics and Finance) Employability Enhancement Courses (Professional Practices, Value-added, Skill 5. Development Courses including Community 24 Engagement and Social Responsibility, Internship, and Projects) 7. Online Course 3 8. Research Methodology and IPR Course 3"},
  {"id": 294, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.4", "heading": "The curriculum of a semester shall normally have a blend of 6 lecture-", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The curriculum of a semester shall normally have a blend of 6 lecture- based courses and laboratory courses not exceeding 2 except for the pre-final and final semesters. In addition, Employability Enhancement Course(s) may be included. Each course may have credits assigned as per Clause R4.5. However, the total number of courses per semester shall not exceed 9, including EM Courses. Pre-final semester may have 4 lecture courses, and a Project (Phase 1). The final semester should include only Project (Phase 2) for Engineering stream."},
  {"id": 295, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.5", "heading": "Credit Assignment", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Credit Assignment Each course is assigned a certain number of credits based on the details provided in Table 2. Table 2. Credit Assignment Contact Period per Week Credit One Lecture Period 1 One Tutorial Period 1 Two Practical Periods (also for employability enhancement courses like Seminar / Project Work / Case Study etc.) Two weeks summer Industrial Training / Internship 1 The contact periods per week for practical courses can only be in multiples of 2."},
  {"id": 296, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.6", "heading": "Students may be permitted to do additional elective / open elective /", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Students may be permitted to do additional elective / open elective / online courses subject to the recommendation of the Mentor and approval of the Head of the Department. However, the maximum number of credits registered in any semester shall not exceed 30."},
  {"id": 297, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.7", "heading": "A student shall register for additional courses by paying the prescribed", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "A student shall register for additional courses by paying the prescribed fee."},
  {"id": 298, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.8", "heading": "Students Induction Programme", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Students Induction Programme All PG students should undergo one-week mandatory induction programme at the beginning of the first semester. The programme comprises physical activity, universal human values, proficiency modules, creative arts, lectures by eminent people, visits to local areas and familiarization to department / branch & innovations."},
  {"id": 299, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.9", "heading": "Assigning Course Codes", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Assigning Course Codes Category of Course UG/PG Regulation Courses / Classification Sequence 1 character 2 characters Programmes 1 character Number 2 characters 2 characters The course code consists of 8 characters, and it is divided into 5 parts. Part 1: One character (Alphabet) – U or P represents UG or PG. Part 2: Two characters (Numerals) represent Regulations. Part 3: Two characters (Alphabets) represent the Category of Courses / Programme – Core Courses, Programme Elective Courses, Open Elective Courses, and Online Courses. Employability Enhancement Courses (EM): Year and Semester-wise programme specific skill enhancement courses. Value Added Courses (VA): Courses related to programme specific, domain specific, skill based, and courses related to thrust areas and industrial requirements. Audit Courses (AU): Non-credit courses - Courses related to general skills, life skills, language skills, visionary skills, cyber security, understanding historical events, understanding the successful stories of Philanthropists, Indian Constitution, Environmental Science etc. Part 4: One character (single numeral) – 1 to 9 represents the classification of the courses related to the specific programme. Classification Code Purpose (6th character) Year of Study: 1-2 1 to 2 for all PG programmes 7 Open Elective Courses 8 Online Courses Elective Courses related to the specific programme Part 5: Two characters (Numerals) represent the sequence number of the courses in each category, further, to represent the courses to be offered in the odd and even semesters. Sequence 01 to 49 represents courses in the odd semester. Sequence 51 to 99 represents courses in the even semester. The codes for the Value Added and Audit courses will be general, applied to all programmes offered at the Institute. Although there are only four segments in the codes assigned to these courses, they consist of eight characters in total. Part 4 and Part 5 are combined to create a sequential number ranging from 001 to 999."},
  {"id": 300, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.10", "heading": "Project Work", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Project Work"},
  {"id": 301, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.10.1", "heading": "Project work is an important component of postgraduate programmes.", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Project work is an important component of postgraduate programmes. The Project work for M.Tech. consists of Project (Phase 1) and Project (Phase 2). The Project (Phase 1) is to be undertaken during semester III. Project (Phase 2), which is a continuation of Project (Phase 1) is to be undertaken during semester IV. For all other PG programmes, the Project Work must be undertaken in the final semester i.e., during semester IV."},
  {"id": 302, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.10.2", "heading": "The Project work for M.A. / M.Sc. / M.Com. / MSW / MBA / M.C.A.", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The Project work for M.A. / M.Sc. / M.Com. / MSW / MBA / M.C.A. programmes shall be pursued for a minimum of 16 weeks during the final semester, along with other courses."},
  {"id": 303, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.10.3", "heading": "The Project work shall be carried out under the supervision of a \"qualified", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The Project work shall be carried out under the supervision of a \"qualified teacher\" in the Department concerned. In this context \"qualified teacher\" means a faculty member possessing a PG degree with a minimum of 3 years of teaching experience or Ph.D. degree."},
  {"id": 304, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.10.4", "heading": "A student may, however, undergo Project in industry / academic /", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "A student may, however, undergo Project in industry / academic / research institutions in lieu of project work of all PG programmes (Project Phase 2 for M. Tech. programmes) for a minimum of 90 days and a maximum of 120 days during Semester IV. Students shall undergo the industrial project with the approval obtained from the Head of the Department and the Dean of the Faculty concerned, preferably one month before the start of the industrial project."},
  {"id": 305, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.10.5", "heading": "The work carried out during Industrial Project shall be jointly supervised", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The work carried out during Industrial Project shall be jointly supervised by a supervisor of the department and an external guide (mentor) from the industry, who shall be part of the project evaluation committee along with the supervisor in the department of the student."},
  {"id": 306, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.10.6", "heading": "Both guides are expected to interact regularly monitoring the progress of", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Both guides are expected to interact regularly monitoring the progress of the student. For the reviews the external guide should be present at least in online mode to assess and award marks to the student. The internal guide should ensure in the beginning of the project that the work to be carried out is up to standard as well as not attracting any IPR issues with the external organization so that the thesis work could be published. The reviews may be conducted in online mode, if the student cannot travel to the Institute to attend the reviews and this shall be approved by HoD, and such reviews must be recorded."},
  {"id": 307, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.10.7", "heading": "In the final Thesis report, the Bonafide certificate shall be signed by both", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "In the final Thesis report, the Bonafide certificate shall be signed by both the guides mandatorily. However, if any difficulty is encountered in fulfilling this norm, then the HoD can initiate remedial action and complete the evaluation requirement with justification and approval of the Dean (Academic courses) for the same."},
  {"id": 308, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.10.8", "heading": "The Bonafide certificate of the project report shall have the date of viva", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The Bonafide certificate of the project report shall have the date of viva voce examination and the signatures of the internal and external guides."},
  {"id": 309, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.10.9", "heading": "The industrial project is apart from the summer industrial training or", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The industrial project is apart from the summer industrial training or summer internship, if any."},
  {"id": 310, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.11", "heading": "Thesis / Dissertation", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Thesis / Dissertation Every student shall undertake a thesis / dissertation work during the semester which is specified in the curriculum. The work will be carried out individually under the supervision of a guide from the same department. The students have to submit the thesis / dissertation report on or before the last working day of the semester and the assessment shall be carried out as per the System of Examinations (vide Clause RXX)."},
  {"id": 311, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.12", "heading": "Industrial Training / Internship", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Industrial Training / Internship"},
  {"id": 312, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.12.1", "heading": "The students may undergo Industrial training for a period (a minimum of", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The students may undergo Industrial training for a period (a minimum of 4 weeks and a maximum of 6 weeks in one or more slots) as specified in the Curriculum during the summer / winter vacation."},
  {"id": 313, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.12.2", "heading": "The students may undergo Internship at a Research organization /", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The students may undergo Internship at a Research organization / University / industry / Innovation Hubs / Community Centres / Social Service Organizations / Financial institutions (after due approval from the Head of the Department) for the period prescribed in the curriculum during the summer / winter vacation, in lieu of Industrial training."},
  {"id": 314, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.12.3", "heading": "If Industrial Training / Internship is not prescribed in the curriculum, the", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "If Industrial Training / Internship is not prescribed in the curriculum, the student may undergo Industrial Training / Internship optionally and the credits earned will be indicated in the Grade Sheet as per details provided in Table 3. If the number of credits earned is 1 or 2, then these credits shall not be considered for computation of CGPA. However, it shall be recorded in the grade sheet."},
  {"id": 315, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.12.4", "heading": "The training / Internship must be undergone continuously in the same", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The training / Internship must be undergone continuously in the same organization for the entire period of each slot (a slot equals 2 weeks). Table 3. Assigned Credits for Industrial Training / Internship Duration of Training Period / Credit(s) Internship Two weeks 1 Four weeks 2 Six weeks 3"},
  {"id": 316, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.12.5", "heading": "The student is expected to submit a report and it shall be evaluated by a", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The student is expected to submit a report and it shall be evaluated by a team of faculty members nominated by the Head of the Department. Based on the recommendations, the student will be awarded credits, and the results will be sent to the Controller of Examinations for further processing."},
  {"id": 317, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.12.6", "heading": "During summer the student is allowed to undergo a maximum of 6 weeks", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "During summer the student is allowed to undergo a maximum of 6 weeks Industrial Training / Internship. In such cases, Industrial Training / Internship need to be undergone continuously from one organization only. If the student earns three credits in Industrial Training / Internship, then he / she may optionally drop one Professional Elective within 15 days of the commencement of the semester and the same is to be recommended by the Head of the Department and the Dean of the Faculty concerned."},
  {"id": 318, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.13", "heading": "Medium of Instruction", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Medium of Instruction The medium of instruction is English for all courses, seminar presentations and project / thesis / dissertation reports. However, bilingual language policy (English and Tamil) shall be adopted for all examinations. The medium of instruction is Tamil for the M.A. Tamil programme offered by the Department of Languages."},
  {"id": 319, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.14", "heading": "Value Added Courses", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Value Added Courses"},
  {"id": 320, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.14.1", "heading": "Students may optionally undergo Value Added Courses and the credits", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Students may optionally undergo Value Added Courses and the credits earned through the Value-Added Courses shall be over and above the total credit requirement prescribed in the curriculum for the award of the degree. Courses with two / three credits shall be offered by a Department with the prior approval from the Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 321, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.14.2", "heading": "The details of the syllabus, timetable and faculty may be sent to the Office", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The details of the syllabus, timetable and faculty may be sent to the Office of the Dean (Academic Courses) after approval from the Departmental Advisory Committee concerned."},
  {"id": 322, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.14.3", "heading": "Students shall be allowed to take these courses offered in other", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Students shall be allowed to take these courses offered in other Departments also, but with the permission of the Head of the Department of student and Head of the department offering the course."},
  {"id": 323, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.14.4", "heading": "The courses once approved by the institute, which are represented by any", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The courses once approved by the institute, which are represented by any department, shall be made available in the institute website and these courses can be offered by the departments with information to Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 324, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.15", "heading": "Off Campus Courses and Transfer of Credits", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Off Campus Courses and Transfer of Credits"},
  {"id": 325, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.15.1", "heading": "Students are permitted to optionally enroll and study a maximum of three", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Students are permitted to optionally enroll and study a maximum of three off-campus courses in physical / online / hybrid mode under each PG programme with the approval of Department Advisory Committee and Dean (Academic Courses) as per the Regulations. The successful completion of these courses through any of the above modes shall be considered in lieu of professional elective / open elective courses of curriculum as approved by Department Advisory Committee."},
  {"id": 326, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.15.2", "heading": "Students are permitted to optionally enroll and study these courses", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Students are permitted to optionally enroll and study these courses through SWAYAM / NPTEL platforms and credit transfer is to be done based on the marks and certificate provided by the NPTEL. The number of credits and transfer of credits are based on the procedure explained in Table 4 and the Mapping of the marks with the grades is explained in Table 5. The mapping of marks with grades is applicable, only if the student passes the course as per the guidelines of NPTEL. Table 4: Duration of the Course and Number of Credits Sl. No. No. of Weeks Credits 1 4 weeks 1 2 8 weeks 2 3 12 weeks 3 4 16 weeks 4 Table 5: Mapping of Marks Scored in NPTEL Course and Letter Grades Sl. No. Letter Grade Marks 1 O 90 - 100 2 A+ 80 - 89 3 A 70 - 79 4 B+ 60 - 69 5 B 50 - 59 6 C 40 - 49"},
  {"id": 327, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.15.3", "heading": "Students are also permitted to enroll and undergo courses in online mode", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Students are also permitted to enroll and undergo courses in online mode at Universities in India / Abroad. Further, the students are permitted to study courses of a particular semester in a University / Institution based on MoU. The marks / credits earned by the student shall be transferred based on the decision of the Credit Equivalence Committee constituted by Dean (Academic Courses) and approved by the institute."},
  {"id": 328, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.15.4", "heading": "If the students are permitted to undergo courses in online mode or in any", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "If the students are permitted to undergo courses in online mode or in any MOOCs platform, a course coordinator shall be nominated from the Department who shall also attend such course and shall coordinate the question paper setting and answer script evaluation for the continuous assessment and end semester examination conducted by the University. The passing requirements are as per regulations."},
  {"id": 329, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.16", "heading": "Self Study Courses", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Self Study Courses"},
  {"id": 330, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.16.1", "heading": "Students may be permitted to credit one or two Self Study courses with", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Students may be permitted to credit one or two Self Study courses with the approval of the Department Advisory Committee and the Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 331, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R4.16.2", "heading": "The purpose of the course is to permit the student to study a course / topic", "section": "R4. STRUCTURE OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The purpose of the course is to permit the student to study a course / topic of the student's choice. The students shall study on their own under the guidance of a faculty member. No formal lectures need be delivered. The syllabus of the course and mode of assessments shall be approved by the Department Advisory Committee and forwarded to Dean (Academic Courses) for formal approval of the course by the academic bodies, preferably before the commencement of the semester. The self-study course of 3 credits can be considered as one elective course. One Faculty member approved by the Head of the Department shall be responsible for the periodic monitoring and evaluation of the course."},
  {"id": 332, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R5", "heading": "DURATION OF THE PROGRAMMES", "section": "R5. DURATION OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "DURATION OF THE PROGRAMMES"},
  {"id": 333, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R5.1", "heading": "A student is ordinarily expected to complete the M.A. / M.B.A. / MCA /", "section": "R5. DURATION OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "A student is ordinarily expected to complete the M.A. / M.B.A. / MCA / M.Com. / M.Sc. / MSW / M.Tech. degree programme in 4 semesters (two academic years) but in any case, not more than 8 Semesters (four academic years)."},
  {"id": 334, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R5.2", "heading": "Each semester shall normally consist of 90 working days including the", "section": "R5. DURATION OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "Each semester shall normally consist of 90 working days including the days during which the continuous assessment examinations are conducted. The Dean of the Faculty concerned shall ensure that every teacher imparts instruction as per the number of periods / hours specified in the syllabus and that the teacher delivers the full content of the specified syllabus for the course being taught."},
  {"id": 335, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R5.3", "heading": "The total period for completion of the programme reckoned from the", "section": "R5. DURATION OF THE PROGRAMMES", "text": "The total period for completion of the programme reckoned from the commencement of the first semester to which the candidate was admitted shall not exceed the maximum period specified in Clause R5.1 irrespective of the period of Break of Study (vide Clause R17) or prevention (vide Clause R7.7) in order that he / she may be eligible for the award of the degree (vide Clause R16.1)."},
  {"id": 336, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6", "heading": "COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION The courses that a student registers in a semester includes: i. Courses of the current semester (including mandatory non-credit courses). ii. Course(s) in which he / she has not been permitted to appear for the end semester examinations for want of the minimum required attendance if such courses are offered in that semester. iii. Professional or Programme elective course(s) opted by the students in lieu of the same category of courses in which he / she has failed, if the courses are offered in the semester. iv. The project work in the III / IV semester. v. Any other course(s) the student wishes to register as per norms with the approval of the Head of the Department and the Dean of the Faculty concerned."},
  {"id": 337, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.1", "heading": "Each student, on admission, shall be assigned to a Mentor (vide Clause", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Each student, on admission, shall be assigned to a Mentor (vide Clause R9), who shall advice and counsel the student about the details of the academic programme and the choice of courses, considering the student's academic background and career objectives."},
  {"id": 338, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.2", "heading": "Each student on admission shall register for all the courses prescribed in", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Each student on admission shall register for all the courses prescribed in the curriculum of the first semester of study."},
  {"id": 339, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.3", "heading": "After registering for a course, the student should attend classes, satisfy", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "After registering for a course, the student should attend classes, satisfy attendance requirements (vide Clause R7), earn continuous assessment marks, and appear for the end semester examinations."},
  {"id": 340, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.4", "heading": "Registration for all the courses listed in the curriculum from the semesters", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Registration for all the courses listed in the curriculum from the semesters II to IV will commence five working days prior to the commencement of the succeeding semester. The candidate makes the choice of electives in consultation with his / her Mentor."},
  {"id": 341, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.5", "heading": "The student shall enroll for the courses with the guidance of the Mentor.", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The student shall enroll for the courses with the guidance of the Mentor. If the student wishes, the student may drop or add courses (vide Clause R6.9) within five working days after the commencement of the concerned semester and complete the registration process duly authorized by the Course Instructor / Mentor."},
  {"id": 342, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.6", "heading": "Late registration will be permitted with a fine amount as prescribed by", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Late registration will be permitted with a fine amount as prescribed by the Institute up to two weeks from the last date specified for registration."},
  {"id": 343, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.7", "heading": "The list of students approved by the respective Course Instructor as", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The list of students approved by the respective Course Instructor as discussed in the Class Committee (vide Clause R10) shall be final and would be considered for attendance, grades, and calculation of CGPA and no changes shall be made thereafter."},
  {"id": 344, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.8", "heading": "The candidate will be eligible for enrollment only if he / she has cleared", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The candidate will be eligible for enrollment only if he / she has cleared all the dues to the Institute such as Hostel fees, Library due, Laboratory breakages etc., of the previous semester and paid all required prescribed fees for the current semester, provided he / she is not debarred from the Institute on account of disciplinary matters."},
  {"id": 345, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.9", "heading": "Instead of two electives in the curriculum, the student may be permitted", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Instead of two electives in the curriculum, the student may be permitted to choose a maximum of 2 courses from other PG programmes with the approval of the Head of the Department of student and Head of the Department offering such courses."},
  {"id": 346, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.10", "heading": "A student who has passed all the courses prescribed in the curriculum for", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "A student who has passed all the courses prescribed in the curriculum for the award of the degree shall not be permitted to re-enroll to improve the marks in a course or the CGPA."},
  {"id": 347, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.11", "heading": "FLEXIBILITY TO ADD OR DROP COURSES", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "FLEXIBILITY TO ADD OR DROP COURSES"},
  {"id": 348, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.11.1", "heading": "A student must earn the total number of credits specified in the", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "A student must earn the total number of credits specified in the curriculum of the chosen programme of study to be eligible to obtain the degree. However, the student is permitted to earn more than the total number of credits prescribed in the curriculum of the programme. In such cases, the minimum number of credits required for the completion of the programme would be considered for CGPA calculation."},
  {"id": 349, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.11.2", "heading": "From second semester onwards, each student has to register all courses", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "From second semester onwards, each student has to register all courses in the curriculum of a respective semester (with the facility to drop courses to a maximum of 8 credits). The dropping of courses shall be decided as per prerequisite requirements in consultation with the Mentor."},
  {"id": 350, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.11.3", "heading": "The student can also register for courses in which he / she failed in the", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The student can also register for courses in which he / she failed in the earlier semesters. In such cases the student shall do reappearance registration for those courses or redo the courses when they are offered."},
  {"id": 351, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.11.4", "heading": "In case, the student fails to secure pass in an elective course, he / she shall", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "In case, the student fails to secure pass in an elective course, he / she shall be allowed to opt for a change in elective and register for the same and do attend the classes to meet the criteria stated in Clause R7 and the failed elective shall not be listed in the Grade Sheet."},
  {"id": 352, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.11.5", "heading": "In any case, adding or dropping or redoing of courses, the total number", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "In any case, adding or dropping or redoing of courses, the total number of credits that is allowed to register per semester cannot exceed 30."},
  {"id": 353, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.11.6", "heading": "For an elective to be offered, the department shall specify the minimum", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "For an elective to be offered, the department shall specify the minimum number of students required."},
  {"id": 354, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.12", "heading": "Reappearance Registration", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Reappearance Registration"},
  {"id": 355, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.12.1", "heading": "If a student fails in a theory / practical / theory integrated with practical", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "If a student fails in a theory / practical / theory integrated with practical course / practical integrated with theory course, the student shall do reappearance registration for that course in the subsequent semester, and appear for the end semester examination, or appear for the supplementary examination vide Clause R15. However, the continuous assessment marks obtained by the student will be retained for the subsequent arrear attempt or for the supplementary examination."},
  {"id": 356, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.12.2", "heading": "In the third attempt, to pass the course, the candidate should secure either", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "In the third attempt, to pass the course, the candidate should secure either 50 percent of marks and above considering the sum of 50 percent of marks acquired in continuous assessment and 50 percent of marks earned in end semester examination (satisfying the passing requirement) or 50 percent of marks and above earned in end semester examination alone."},
  {"id": 357, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.12.3", "heading": "If the course in which the student has failed is a professional elective or", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "If the course in which the student has failed is a professional elective or programme elective, the student will be permitted to register for the same in the subsequent semesters and shall appear for the end semester examination. If a student registers for the same professional / programme elective, then the Clauses R6.12.1 and R6.12.2 are applicable. If a student registers for any other professional / programme elective, he / she must attend the classes and fulfil the attendance requirements (vide Clause R7), earn continuous assessment marks, and appear for the end semester examination."},
  {"id": 358, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.12.4", "heading": "The student who fails in project work / thesis / dissertation shall register", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The student who fails in project work / thesis / dissertation shall register for the same in the subsequent semester, when offered next, and repeat the course. In this case, the student must satisfy attendance requirements (vide Clause R7), earn continuous assessment marks and appear for the end semester examination."},
  {"id": 359, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.12.5", "heading": "Students are not eligible to reappear for the courses that they have already", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Students are not eligible to reappear for the courses that they have already passed in a semester for improvement of Grade / Marks."},
  {"id": 360, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.13", "heading": "Redoing a Course", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "Redoing a Course Redoing a course means re-registering for a course, attending all classes, fulfilling the attendance requirements as per Clause R7, earning fresh continuous assessment marks and appearing for the end semester examinations. A student must redo a course in the following conditions."},
  {"id": 361, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.13.1", "heading": "If a student is prevented from writing the end semester examination of", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "If a student is prevented from writing the end semester examination of any core course due to lack of attendance, the student has to register for that course again when offered next and redo the course."},
  {"id": 362, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.13.2", "heading": "If a student is prevented from writing the end semester examination of", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "If a student is prevented from writing the end semester examination of any professional / programme elective course due to lack of attendance, the student can opt to register for the same course again when offered next and redo the course, or he / she can opt to register for a different professional / programme elective course when it is offered, attend classes, fulfill the attendance requirements as per Clause R7, secure continuous assessment marks and appear for end semester examinations."},
  {"id": 363, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.13.3", "heading": "If a student fails to secure a pass in any theory (including professional /", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "If a student fails to secure a pass in any theory (including professional / programme elective) / practical / theory integrated with practical / practical integrated with theory course, he / she is given a maximum of three arrear attempts to complete the course as per Clause R14.3. If the student fails to secure a pass even in the third attempt, he / she shall register for the same when offered next and redo the course."},
  {"id": 364, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.13.4", "heading": "The student who fails in any Project work (Phase 1 or Phase 2 in case of", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The student who fails in any Project work (Phase 1 or Phase 2 in case of M.Tech. programme) shall register for the course again, when offered next, and redo the course. In this case, the student shall attend the reviews and fulfill the attendance requirements as per Clause R7."},
  {"id": 365, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.13.5", "heading": "The student who fails in Seminar / Internship / Case Study and Industrial", "section": "R6. COURSE ENROLLMENT AND REGISTRATION", "text": "The student who fails in Seminar / Internship / Case Study and Industrial / Practical Training shall register for the same in the subsequent semester and redo the course. In this case, the student shall attend the classes and fulfill the attendance requirements as per Clause R7."},
  {"id": 366, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7", "heading": "REQUIREMENTS FOR APPEARING FOR THE END", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "REQUIREMENTS FOR APPEARING FOR THE END SEMESTER EXAMINATIONS A student who has fulfilled the conditions, vide Clause R7.3 and Clause"},
  {"id": 367, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.4", "heading": "shall be deemed to have satisfied the attendance requirements for", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "shall be deemed to have satisfied the attendance requirements for appearing for the end semester examination of a particular course."},
  {"id": 368, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.1", "heading": "All students must attend every lecture, tutorial, and practical classes.", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "All students must attend every lecture, tutorial, and practical classes."},
  {"id": 369, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.2", "heading": "Attendance record will be maintained based upon roll calls (or any", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "Attendance record will be maintained based upon roll calls (or any equivalent operation) in every scheduled lecture, tutorial, and practical class. The Class Advisor will maintain and consolidate the attendance record for all the courses (lectures, tutorials, and practicals together, as applicable)."},
  {"id": 370, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.3", "heading": "Ideally every student is expected to attend all periods and earn 100", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "Ideally every student is expected to attend all periods and earn 100 percent attendance. However, the student shall secure not less than 75 percent attendance, course wise, considering the number of periods required for that course, as specified in the curriculum."},
  {"id": 371, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.4", "heading": "If a student secures attendance between 65 percent and less than 75", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "If a student secures attendance between 65 percent and less than 75 percent in any course in the current semester, due to medical reasons (hospitalization / accident / specific illness) or due to participation in the College / University / State / National / International level Sports events, with prior permission from the Head of the Department and the Dean concerned, the student shall be given exemption from the prescribed attendance requirement and the student shall be permitted to appear for the end semester examination of that course. In all such cases, the students should submit the required documents on joining after the absence to the Head of the Department through the class advisor."},
  {"id": 372, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.5", "heading": "A student shall normally be permitted to appear for the end semester", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "A student shall normally be permitted to appear for the end semester examination of the courses if the student has satisfied the attendance requirements (Clauses R7.3 and R7.4) and has registered for the examination in those courses of that semester by paying the prescribed fee."},
  {"id": 373, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.6", "heading": "A student who has an attendance of less than 75 percent will not be", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "A student who has an attendance of less than 75 percent will not be permitted to appear for the end semester examination in the course in which the shortage exists. His / her registration for that course will be treated as cancelled and he / she shall be awarded 'SA' grade (\"Shortage of Attendance\" i.e., registration is cancelled due to lack of attendance) in that course. This grade shall appear in the result sheet. The student should register and repeat the course as and when it is offered next as per Clause R6.13."},
  {"id": 374, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.7", "heading": "Students who do not satisfy Clauses R7.3 and R7.4 or who secure less", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "Students who do not satisfy Clauses R7.3 and R7.4 or who secure less than 65 percent attendance in a course will not be permitted to write the end semester examination of that course (vide Clause R7.6). The student must register and redo the course when it is offered next as per Clause"},
  {"id": 375, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R6.13", "heading": "If the course in which the student has been prevented is a", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "If the course in which the student has been prevented is a professional / programme elective, the student can opt to redo the same course or opt for different professional / programme elective course as per Clause R6.13.2."},
  {"id": 376, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.8", "heading": "If a student has shortage of attendance in all the registered courses, he /", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "If a student has shortage of attendance in all the registered courses, he / she would not be permitted to move to the higher semester and must repeat the current semester in the subsequent year."},
  {"id": 377, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.9", "heading": "In the case of reappearance (arrear) registration for a course, the", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "In the case of reappearance (arrear) registration for a course, the attendance requirement as mentioned in Clauses R7.3 and R7.4 is not applicable. However, the student must register for the examination in that course by paying the prescribed fee."},
  {"id": 378, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.10", "heading": "If the student needs leave for a short duration (less than two weeks), prior", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "If the student needs leave for a short duration (less than two weeks), prior application for the leave shall have to be submitted to the Head of the Department concerned stating the reasons for the leave requested along with supporting documents and such leave may be granted by the Head of the Department."},
  {"id": 379, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.11", "heading": "Absence for the period not exceeding two weeks in a semester due to", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "Absence for the period not exceeding two weeks in a semester due to sickness or any other unavoidable reasons for which prior application could not be made may be condoned by the Head of the Department provided the given explanation is acceptable."},
  {"id": 380, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.12", "heading": "If the period of absence is likely to exceed two weeks, a prior application", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "If the period of absence is likely to exceed two weeks, a prior application for grant of leave will have to be submitted through Head of the Department and the Dean of the Faculty concerned to the Dean (Academic Courses) with supporting documents. In such case the decision to grant leave shall be taken by the Dean (Academic Courses) on the recommendation of the Head of the Department and the Dean of the Faculty concerned."},
  {"id": 381, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.13", "heading": "A student who is absent due to illness or any other emergency, up to a", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "A student who is absent due to illness or any other emergency, up to a maximum of two weeks, should approach the Class Advisor / Course Coordinator / Course Instructor for assignments and laboratory work."},
  {"id": 382, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.14", "heading": "In case, the period of absence on medical grounds is more than 20", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "In case, the period of absence on medical grounds is more than 20 working days during the semester, the student may apply for withdrawal from the semester, i.e. withdrawal from all courses registered in that semester."},
  {"id": 383, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R7.15", "heading": "If a student is continuously absent from the Institute for more than four", "section": "R7. REQUIREMENTS             FOR        APPEARING        FOR      THE      END", "text": "If a student is continuously absent from the Institute for more than four weeks without any notification to the Head of the Department / Dean of the Faculty concerned / Dean (Academic Courses), his / her name will be removed from the Institute rolls and the same should be informed to his / her parents immediately."},
  {"id": 384, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R8", "heading": "CLASS ADVISOR", "section": "R8. CLASS ADVISOR", "text": "CLASS ADVISOR There shall be a Class Advisor for each class. The Class Advisor will be one among the course instructors of the class. He / She will be appointed by the Head of the department concerned. The Class Advisor is the ex-officio member and the Convener of the class committee. The responsibilities of the Class Advisor shall be: a. To act as the channel of communication between the HoD and the students of the respective class. b. To collect and maintain various details such as attendance, assessment marks and long leave particulars. c. To help the Chairperson of the class committee in planning and conducting the class committee meetings. d. To monitor the academic performance of the students including attendance and to inform the class committee. e. To coordinate with each instructor in performing analysis of results of continuous assessments and end semester examinations and in estimating CO – PO attainment. f. To attend to the students' welfare activities like awards, medals, scholarships, and industrial visits."},
  {"id": 385, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R9", "heading": "MENTOR", "section": "R9. MENTOR", "text": "MENTOR To help the students in planning their courses of study and for general advice on the academic programme, the Head of the Department will attach a certain number of students to a teacher of the Department, who shall function as Mentor for those students throughout their period of study. The Mentor shall advise the students in registering and reappearance (arrear) registering of courses, authorize the process, monitor their attendance and progress and counsel them periodically. If necessary, the Mentor may also discuss with or inform the parents about the progress / performance of the students concerned. The number of students assigned to a Mentor will be decided by the Head of the Department. However, the strength shall not exceed 20 students per Mentor. The responsibilities of the Mentor shall be: a. To inform the interpretation of Regulations to the students and their rights and duties. b. To inform the code of conduct to be maintained in the campus and disciplinary actions. c. To inform the students about the various facilities and activities available to enhance the student's curricular and co-curricular activities. d. To guide in the process of enrollment and registration of the courses. e. To authorize the final registration of the courses at the beginning of each semester. f. To monitor the academic and general performance of the students including attendance and to counsel them accordingly. g. To collect and maintain the students' academic and co-curricular records. h. To facilitate and collect students' feedback about the course and course instructor. i. To facilitate and collect the course exit survey and programme exit survey. j. To provide all the details of the academic, including feedback, training, scholarship, placement, co-curricular, and extracurricular activities of the students to the Dean (Academic Courses) through the HoD and the Dean of the Faculty concerned."},
  {"id": 386, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R10 (part 1)", "heading": "CLASS COMMITTEE", "section": "R10. CLASS COMMITTEE", "text": "CLASS COMMITTEE A class committee consists of all teachers of the class concerned, student representatives and a chairperson who does not handle any course for the class. It is like the 'Quality Circle' (more commonly used in industries), with the overall goal of improving the teaching-learning process. The class committee shall be constituted by the HoD within 7 days from the commencement of classes. The Class Advisor and the HoD will attend the meeting. The Dean (Academic Courses) and the Mentor(s) shall be called to attend the meeting as special invitees if required. The functions of the class committee include:  Solving problems experienced by students in the classroom and in the laboratories in consultation with the HoD / Dean of Faculty concerned / Dean (Academic Courses).  Clarifying the Regulations of the degree programme and the details of rules therein.  Informing the student representatives about the academic schedule including the dates of assessments and the syllabus coverage for each assessment.  Informing the student representatives, the details of Regulations regarding weightage used for each assessment.  Discussing in the class committee meeting the breakup of marks for each experiment / exercise / module of work, in case of practical courses (laboratory / project work / seminar, etc.) and informing the students.  Analyzing the performance of the students of the class after each assessment and finding ways and means of improving their performance."},
  {"id": 387, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R10 (part 2)", "heading": "CLASS COMMITTEE", "section": "R10. CLASS COMMITTEE", "text": " Identifying the students who are low achievers or weak in their courses if any, and requesting the teachers concerned to provide some additional help or guidance or coaching to such students. The class committee is normally constituted by the Head of the Department. However, if the students of different programmes are mixed in each class, the class committee is to be constituted by the Dean (Academic Courses). At least 4 student representatives from the respective class (usually 2 boys and 2 girls) shall be included in the class committee. The Chairperson of the class committee is required to prepare the minutes of every meeting, submit the same to the Head of the Department within two days of the meeting and arrange to circulate the same among students concerned and teachers. A copy of the minutes shall be displayed in the notice board. If there are some points in the minutes requiring action by the Institute, the same shall be brought to the notice of the Registrar through Dean (Academic Courses). The first meeting of the class committee shall be held within 10 days from the date of commencement of the semester. The enrollment of courses including add and drop of the courses will be finalized. The nature and weightage of continuous assessments shall be decided in the first meeting, within the framework of the Regulations and the same shall be communicated to the students. Two or three subsequent meetings in a semester may be held at suitable intervals."},
  {"id": 388, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R10 (part 3)", "heading": "CLASS COMMITTEE", "section": "R10. CLASS COMMITTEE", "text": "During these meetings the student members representing the entire class, shall meaningfully interact and express their opinions and suggestions of the class students to improve the effectiveness of the teaching-learning process. In each meeting, the action taken report based on the minutes of the previous meeting is to be presented and discussed by the Chairperson of the class committee. After the completion of the end semester examination and evaluation process, the course instructor shall keep the record of marks and grades earned by the students for the computation of CO and PO attainments."},
  {"id": 389, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R11", "heading": "COMMON COURSE COMMITTEE", "section": "R11. COMMON COURSE COMMITTEE", "text": "COMMON COURSE COMMITTEE A theory course handled by more than one teacher, or each common theory course offered to more than one discipline or group of disciplines, shall have a \"Common Course Committee\" comprising of all the instructors teaching that common course with one of them nominated as Course Coordinator. The nomination of the Course Coordinator shall be made by the Dean (Academic Courses) in consultation with the Dean of the concerned Faculty and the Heads of the Departments, from among the instructors teaching the common course either from a single department or several departments. The committee shall be constituted by the Dean (Academic Courses) within 5 days from the commencement of the semester. The first meeting of the Common Course Committee shall be held within 5 days from the date of formation of the committee. The lesson plan, books and references to be followed shall be decided at the first meeting. The \"Common Course Committee\" shall meet as often as possible and ensure uniform evaluation of continuous assessments after arriving at a common scheme of evaluation for the assessments (vide Clause R13). Wherever feasible, the common course committee shall prepare a common question paper for the continuous assessment tests, objective type test and end semester examination. The question paper for the end semester examination shall be set by the Course Co-Ordinator, in consultation with all the teachers. The common course committee shall meet to decide the multiplication factor for the respective batch of students, if required. The minutes in this regard shall be sent to all the concerned HoDs and the Controller of Examinations."},
  {"id": 390, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R12", "heading": "PERFORMANCE ANALYSIS COMMITTEE", "section": "R12. PERFORMANCE ANALYSIS COMMITTEE", "text": "PERFORMANCE ANALYSIS COMMITTEE The Performance Analysis Committee will consist of the same members as the class committee but including the Dean (Academic Courses), Director IQAC, Dean of the Faculty, the Head of the Department and excluding the student members. An external member from an allied department shall be nominated by the Dean (Academic Courses) in consultation with the Vice Chancellor to the Performance Analysis Committee. The meeting of the Performance Analysis Committee is to be held within 10 days from the last day of the end semester examinations to analyze the performance of the students in all courses of study by estimating the CO - PO attainment levels and finalize the grade ranges for each course and forward the statement of grades to Dean (Academic Courses) immediately, through the Head of the Department. The Performance Analysis Committee, by collective wisdom, should ensure that the clustering / grading / pass–fail decisions have been reasonably balanced. The attendance registers of all the courses with all the continuous assessment marks, end semester marks, Tabulation Register, grades, and grade-ranges entered in the register are also to be sent to Dean (Academic Courses) immediately through the Head of the Department for forwarding to the Controller of Examinations."},
  {"id": 391, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13", "heading": "SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS The end Semester examinations for theory, theory integrated with practical, practical, practical integrated with theory, and project courses will be 3 hours duration. These examinations shall normally be conducted between October and December during the odd semesters and between April and June during the even semesters. For practical, and project courses, the end semester examination will be conducted with an external examiner appointed by the Controller of Examinations."},
  {"id": 392, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.1", "heading": "Assessment Procedures for Awarding Marks", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Assessment Procedures for Awarding Marks All M.A. / M.Sc. / MSW / M.Com. / MBA / MCA / M.Tech. degree programmes consist of theory / practical / theory integrated with practical / practical integrated with theory / Employability Enhancement Courses such as Professional Practices, Case Study and Industrial / Practical Training / Internship / Project Work / Thesis / Dissertation / Value Added Courses and Audit Courses. Appearance in End Semester Examination is mandatory for all courses including Theory, Theory integrated with Practical, Practical, Practical integrated with Theory, project work, and all lecture-based employability enhancement courses. Performance in each course of study shall be evaluated based on: i) Continuous Assessments throughout the semester and ii) End Semester Examination The evaluation shall be based on Outcome Based Education and the relevant rubrics shall be followed. The commencement date of assessments and the number of weeks to be considered for syllabus coverage shall be fixed as per the academic schedule prescribed by the Dean (Academic Courses) and Controller of Examinations."},
  {"id": 393, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.2", "heading": "Each course, Theory, Theory Integrated with Practical, Practical,", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Each course, Theory, Theory Integrated with Practical, Practical, Practical Integrated with Theory, Project work, thesis, and dissertation shall be evaluated for a maximum of 100 marks. The weightage for continuous assessment and end semester examination marks are given in Table 6."},
  {"id": 394, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.3", "heading": "Some domain specific courses included under Employability", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Some domain specific courses included under Employability Enhancement Courses are evaluated by internal assessments only. There is no evaluation for Audit Courses. However, minimum attendance requirements as per Clause R7 shall be satisfied. TABLE 6. Weightage of Marks Marks Weightage (%) SL.No. Category of Courses Continuous End Semester Assessment Examination 1 Theory Courses 50 50 2 Practical Courses 75 25 Theory integrated with Theory – 25 3 Theory - 50 Practical Courses Practical - 25 Practical integrated with Theory - 25 4 Practical - 25 Theory Courses Practical - 50 Project Work / thesis / 5 60 40 dissertation Value Added Courses, Skill Development Programmes, 6 100 - Internship and Online Courses (with one credit)"},
  {"id": 395, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.4", "heading": "Every teacher is required to maintain an 'ATTENDANCE AND", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Every teacher is required to maintain an 'ATTENDANCE AND ASSESSMENT RECORD' for every semester, which consists of attendance marked in each class of Theory / Theory Integrated with Practical / Practical / Practical integrated with Theory / Employability Enhancement Courses / Audit Courses, the assessment marks, and the record of class work (topics covered), separately for each course handled by the teacher. The attendance book completed in all aspects should be submitted to the HoD periodically (three times in a semester) for checking the syllabus coverage and the records of assessment marks and attendance. The HoD and the Dean of Faculty concerned will affix signature and date after due verification. At the end of the semester, the record should be verified by the Dean (Academic Courses) who shall keep this document in safe custody for 5 years. The records of attendance and assessment of both current and previous semesters should be available for auditing."},
  {"id": 396, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.5", "heading": "Assessment for Theory Courses", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Assessment for Theory Courses"},
  {"id": 397, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.5.1", "heading": "The End Semester Examinations for theory courses will be 3 hours", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "The End Semester Examinations for theory courses will be 3 hours duration and shall normally be conducted between October and December during the odd semesters and between April and June during the even semesters."},
  {"id": 398, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.5.2", "heading": "Continuous Assessment Evaluation for Theory Courses", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Continuous Assessment Evaluation for Theory Courses  The mode(s) of internal evaluation is / are to be decided for each course in the class committee.  There shall be assignment / tutorial / quiz / case study / seminar / mini-project type of assessment for each course as decided in the class committee and the faculty must evaluate fairly for all the students relatively for 25 marks.  All regular assessment tests are to be conducted for 100 marks and the marks obtained by the students are reduced to 25 marks while evaluating continuous assessment marks. Three assessment tests are to be conducted for each course.  The question paper is to be set considering the appropriate Bloom's Taxonomy levels and to cope with the prescribed course outcomes.  The regular first assessment test is to be conducted between 30 and 35 days from the commencement of classes for the semester with the portion of syllabus covered up to 4 weeks. The test duration shall be 1 hour.  The second assessment test, termed as Mid-term test is to be conducted between 60 and 65 days from the commencement of classes for the semester with the portion of syllabus covered up to 8 weeks. The test duration shall be 2 hours. The question paper should have 5 questions in Part A and 3 questions in Part B.  The third assessment test, termed as Model Examination is to be conducted between 80 and 85 days from the commencement of classes for the semester with the portion of syllabus covered up to 11 weeks. The test duration shall be 3 hours. The pattern of the question paper is as per the end semester regular examination.  The sum of marks obtained through assignment / tutorial / quiz / case study / seminar / mini-project type of assessment as per Clause R13.9 (out of 25 marks) and the marks obtained through 3 assessment tests (out of 25 marks), i.e., out of 50 marks, shall be submitted as continuous assessment marks."},
  {"id": 399, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.5.3", "heading": "In case, a student misses the assessment due to medical reasons", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "In case, a student misses the assessment due to medical reasons (hospitalization / accident / specific illness) or due to participation in the College / University / State / National / International level Competitions / conferences / seminars with prior permission from the Head of the Department and Dean of the Faculty concerned, only one re-assessment may be given at the end of the semester after getting approval from the Dean (Academic Courses) by the concerned Head of the Department and Course Instructor."},
  {"id": 400, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.6", "heading": "Assessment for Theory Integrated with Practical / Practical", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Assessment for Theory Integrated with Practical / Practical integrated with Theory Courses Each theory integrated with practical or practical integrated with theory course shall be evaluated for a maximum of 100 marks as shown in Table 7. Table 7: Assessment Pattern and Weightage Marks (in percentage) Category of Sl.No. Assessment End Course Assessment for Semester for Theory Laboratory Examination Theory integrated 25 (Two 25 (Continuous 50 (Theory 1. with Practical Assessments) Evaluation) Examination) Practical integrated 25 (One 50 (Continuous 25 (Practical 2. with theory Assessment) Evaluation) Examination) For theory integrated with practical courses, the end semester examination will be conducted as theory examination. The two assessment tests for theory are written tests. For practical integrated with theory courses, the end semester examination will be conducted and evaluated with an external examiner appointed by the Controller of Examinations. The procedure for conduct of continuous assessments for practical component is as per the Clause R13.7. The weighted average shall be converted into 50 marks for continuous assessment in case of theory integrated with practical courses and into 75 marks for practical integrated with theory courses."},
  {"id": 401, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.7", "heading": "Assessment for Practical Courses", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Assessment for Practical Courses"},
  {"id": 402, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.7.1", "heading": "Every practical experiment shall be evaluated based on the student's", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Every practical experiment shall be evaluated based on the student's performance during the laboratory class and the maintenance of the records."},
  {"id": 403, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.7.2", "heading": "There shall be at least one assessment test for practical courses.", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "There shall be at least one assessment test for practical courses."},
  {"id": 404, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.7.3", "heading": "The criteria for arriving at the continuous assessment marks of 75 will be", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "The criteria for arriving at the continuous assessment marks of 75 will be as per the following scheme: for successful completion of all the prescribed experiments done in the laboratory including observation and record work, 75 percent of marks shall be awarded, and 25 percent marks shall be awarded for the assessment test. The total marks earned by the student in continuous assessments shall be converted into a maximum of 75 marks and rounded to the nearest integer in case of practical courses and to a maximum of 25 marks in case of Theory integrated with Practical courses. The total marks earned by the student in continuous assessments shall be converted into a maximum of 50 marks and rounded to the nearest integer in case of Practical integrated with Theory courses."},
  {"id": 405, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.7.4", "heading": "The end semester examination for practical courses shall be for 25 marks", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "The end semester examination for practical courses shall be for 25 marks and shall include viva-voce also as a part of it. The viva-voce examination shall be conducted by an external examiner appointed by the Controller of Examinations."},
  {"id": 406, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.7.5", "heading": "The end semester examination for practical courses will be of 3 hours", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "The end semester examination for practical courses will be of 3 hours duration and shall normally be conducted before the start of the theory examinations for that semester."},
  {"id": 407, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.8", "heading": "Assessment for Project Work", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Assessment for Project Work"},
  {"id": 408, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.8.1", "heading": "For Project work out of 100 marks, the maximum mark for continuous", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "For Project work out of 100 marks, the maximum mark for continuous assessment is fixed as 60 and the end semester examination (project report evaluation and viva-voce examination) carries 40 marks. For all PG programmes, the project work shall be assigned to a single student. In the case of M.Tech. programme, the Project Phase 2 in the fourth semester must be continuation of Project Phase 1 in the third semester with the same supervisor if the student is pursuing his / her project work within the campus."},
  {"id": 409, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.8.2", "heading": "There shall be three assessments (each 100 marks) during the semester by", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "There shall be three assessments (each 100 marks) during the semester by a review committee. The student shall make a presentation on the progress made before the committee. The Head of the Department shall constitute a review committee for each programme. There shall be a minimum of three members in the review committee. The committee shall consist of the supervisor (project guide), project coordinator and domain expert from the concerned / allied department. The total marks obtained in the three reviews shall be reduced to a maximum of 60 marks (as per the distribution given in Table 9) rounded to the nearest integer. The review meetings, if necessary, may also be arranged in online mode with prior approval from the Dean (Academic Courses) and a suitable record of the meetings shall be maintained."},
  {"id": 410, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.8.3", "heading": "Each student is expected to submit the project report on or before the last", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Each student is expected to submit the project report on or before the last working day of the semester. The end semester examination for the project work shall consist of the evaluation of the final project report submitted by the student by an external examiner, followed by a viva-voce examination conducted separately for each student by a committee consisting of the external examiner and an internal examiner (other than project guide). The project coordinator shall be the internal examiner. The Head of the Department, with the approval of the Controller of Examinations shall appoint the external examiner for the end semester examination of the project work."},
  {"id": 411, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.8.4", "heading": "The continuous assessment and viva-voce examination marks for project", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "The continuous assessment and viva-voce examination marks for project work shall be distributed as indicated below in Table 8. Table 8: Continuous Assessment and End Semester Examination Marks for the Project Work Continuous Assessment (60 Marks) End Semester Examination (40 Marks) Viva-Voce Review I Review II Review III Project Report Examination Guide External Internal External 10 20 30 10 10 10 10"},
  {"id": 412, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.8.5", "heading": "If the project report is not submitted on or before the specified deadline,", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "If the project report is not submitted on or before the specified deadline, an extension of time up to a maximum limit of 30 days may be given for the submission of project work with due approval obtained from the Dean (Academic Courses) and the same needs to be communicated to Controller of Examinations. If the project report is not submitted even beyond the extended time, then the student is deemed to have failed in the Project Work. In the above two cases, double the amount of prescribed Viva-voce examination fee shall be collected from the students."},
  {"id": 413, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.8.6", "heading": "A student may, however, in certain cases, be permitted to work on the", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "A student may, however, in certain cases, be permitted to work on the project in an Industrial / Research organization on the recommendation of the Head of the Department, with the approval of the Dean (Academic Courses). In such cases, the project work shall be jointly supervised by a faculty member (project guide) of the department and an Expert / Scientist from the organization (project coordinator) and the student shall be instructed to report the progress periodically and to attend the project reviews for evaluating the progress. The student will produce a certificate of attendance from the Industry / Research organization where the project is carried out. In case of industrial projects, the marks allotted for the project guide will be shared equally by the guide from the department and the coordinator from the industry."},
  {"id": 414, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.9", "heading": "Assessment for Seminar / Professional Practices / Case Study / Mini", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Assessment for Seminar / Professional Practices / Case Study / Mini Project The Seminar / Professional Practices / Case study / Mini-Project shall carry 100 marks and shall be evaluated through continuous assessment only. Every student is expected to present a minimum of 2 presentations / demonstration per semester before the evaluation committee and for each presentation / demonstration, marks can be equally apportioned. The three-member committee consisting of one coordinator and two members appointed by the Head of the Department will evaluate the performance of the student in above activities at the end of the semester, the marks can be consolidated and taken as the final mark. The evaluation shall be based on the seminar paper / report (40 marks), presentation / demonstration (40 marks) and response to the questions asked during presentation / demonstration (20 marks). The final marks obtained by each student in all the above activities should be consolidated and submitted by the concerned HoD to the Dean (Academic Courses) which in turn should be submitted to Controller of Examinations at the end of each semester. The consolidated final mark obtained by each student is reduced to 25 marks and to be utilized as stated in the Clause R13.5.2."},
  {"id": 415, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.10", "heading": "Assessment for Industrial / Practical Training / Internship", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Assessment for Industrial / Practical Training / Internship The Industrial / Practical Training shall carry 100 marks and shall be evaluated through continuous assessment only. At the end of the Industrial / Practical Training / Internship, the student shall submit a certificate from the organization where the student has undergone training and a brief report about the training. The evaluation will be made based on this report (40 marks), presentation (30 marks) and a Viva-Voce Examination (30 marks). The viva-voce examination will be conducted by a three-member committee constituted by the HoD. The committee comprises of one expert from an industry and two members (a coordinator and a member) from the Department. Certificates (issued by the Organization) of the student along with his / her mark statement should be submitted by the concerned HoD to the Dean (Academic Courses) which in turn should be submitted to Controller of Examinations at the end of each semester."},
  {"id": 416, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.11", "heading": "ASSESSMENT OF SEMESTER LONG INDUSTRIAL PROJECT", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "ASSESSMENT OF SEMESTER LONG INDUSTRIAL PROJECT"},
  {"id": 417, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.11.1", "heading": "The Viva-Voce examination for semester long industrial project shall be", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "The Viva-Voce examination for semester long industrial project shall be based on the report submitted by the student regarding the work carried out in the industrial project. The students must produce an attendance certificate at the time of reviews. The report shall be certified by the coordinator from the industry, supervisor (internal guide) and Head of the Department."},
  {"id": 418, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.11.2", "heading": "Projects undertaken externally should have an internal guide and an", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Projects undertaken externally should have an internal guide and an external guide. Both guides are expected to interact regularly monitoring the progress of the student. For the reviews the external guide should be present at least in online mode to assess and award marks to the student. In the beginning of the project, the internal guide should ensure that the work to be carried out is up to the standard as well as not attracting any IPR issues with the external organization so that the work could be published."},
  {"id": 419, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.11.3", "heading": "The reviews may be conducted in online mode, if the student cannot", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "The reviews may be conducted in online mode, if the student cannot travel to the institute to attend the reviews and this shall be approved by HoD, and such reviews must be recorded. However, the end semester examination must be conducted in physical mode with the mentor (coordinator) from the industry present physically or through online."},
  {"id": 420, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.11.4", "heading": "In the final report, the Bonafide certificate shall be signed by both the", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "In the final report, the Bonafide certificate shall be signed by both the guides mandatorily. However, if any difficulty is encountered in fulfilling this norm, then the HoD can initiate remedial action and complete the evaluation requirement with justification and approval of the Dean (Academic courses) for the same."},
  {"id": 421, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.11.5", "heading": "The Bonafide certificate of the project report shall have the date of viva", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "The Bonafide certificate of the project report shall have the date of viva voce examination and the signatures of the internal and external guides, including the HoD and the examiners."},
  {"id": 422, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.11.6", "heading": "If the project report or report of industrial project is not submitted on or", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "If the project report or report of industrial project is not submitted on or before the specified deadline, an extension of time up to a maximum limit of 30 days may be given for the submission of report with due approval obtained from the Head of the Department. If the report is not submitted even beyond the extended time, then the student is deemed to have failed in the Project Work and the student must redo the course again. In the above two cases, double the amount of prescribed Viva-voce examination fee shall be collected from the students."},
  {"id": 423, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.12", "heading": "Assessment for Thesis / Dissertation", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Assessment for Thesis / Dissertation"},
  {"id": 424, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.12.1", "heading": "Students shall carryout a thesis / dissertation work as specified in the", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Students shall carryout a thesis / dissertation work as specified in the curriculum, which may be evaluated for 100 marks through Continuous Assessment and external Viva-voce examination. The work may be evaluated by a committee consisting of one coordinator and two members appointed by the Head of the Department and Dean of concerned Faculty. There shall be three assessments (each 100 marks) during the semester by a review committee. The student shall make a presentation on the progress made before the committee. The total marks obtained in the three reviews shall be reduced to a maximum of 60 marks rounded to the nearest integer. The review meetings, if necessary, may also be arranged in online mode with prior approval from the Dean (Academic Courses) and a suitable record of the meetings shall be maintained."},
  {"id": 425, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.12.2", "heading": "The student is expected to submit the thesis / dissertation report on or", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "The student is expected to submit the thesis / dissertation report on or before the last working day of the semester. A Viva-voce examination carrying 40 marks will be conducted by a committee consisting of an internal examiner and the external examiner appointed by the controller of examinations."},
  {"id": 426, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.12.3", "heading": "The weightages for continuous assessment and Viva-voce examination", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "The weightages for continuous assessment and Viva-voce examination for thesis / dissertation work shall be distributed as per the Table 9. Table 9: Weightage for Continuous Assessments and Viva-voce Continuous Assessment (60 Marks) End Semester Examinations (40 Marks) Thesis / Viva-voce Review I Review II Review III Dissertation Examination Guide External Internal External 10 20 30 10 10 10 10"},
  {"id": 427, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.12.4", "heading": "If the thesis / dissertation report is not submitted on or before the specified", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "If the thesis / dissertation report is not submitted on or before the specified deadline, an extension of time up to a maximum limit of 30 days may be given for the submission of dissertation work with due approval obtained from the Dean (Academic Courses) and the same needs to be communicated to Controller of Examinations. If the thesis / dissertation report is not submitted even beyond the extended time, then the student is deemed to have failed in the thesis / dissertation. In the above two cases, double the amount of prescribed Viva-voce examination fee shall be collected from the students."},
  {"id": 428, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.12", "heading": "Assessment for Value Added Courses", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Assessment for Value Added Courses This one / two credit course shall carry 100 marks and shall be evaluated through continuous assessments only. One or two assessments shall be conducted during the semester by the department concerned. The HoD may identify a faculty member as coordinator for the course. A committee consisting of the Head of the Department, faculty handling the course (if available), coordinator and a senior faculty member nominated by the Head of the Department shall monitor the evaluation process. The grades shall be assigned to the students by the above committee based on their relative performance. Certificates issued by the industry if any along with the student's mark / grade statement should be submitted by the concerned Head of the Department to the Office of Dean (Academic Courses) which in turn should be submitted to Controller of Examinations at the end of each semester."},
  {"id": 429, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.13", "heading": "Assessment for Online Courses", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Assessment for Online Courses Students may be permitted to credit online courses (NPTEL / SWAYAM) with the approval of the Head of the Department and Dean (Academic Courses), subject to a maximum of six credits."},
  {"id": 430, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.13.1", "heading": "On successful completion of the online course, the candidate must submit", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "On successful completion of the online course, the candidate must submit the copy of the certificate and the grade card (if applicable) to the Head of the Department."},
  {"id": 431, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.13.2", "heading": "The Head of the Department shall form a team of faculty members to", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "The Head of the Department shall form a team of faculty members to recommend the credit and grade to be awarded to the candidate by mapping the score earned by the student and results shall be submitted to the Office of Dean (Academic Courses) which in turn should be submitted to Controller of Examinations for further processing with due approval from Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 432, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.13.3", "heading": "If the grade card is not submitted by the student, the HoD shall", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "If the grade card is not submitted by the student, the HoD shall recommend to the Controller of Examinations through Dean (Academic Courses) to conduct end semester examination on the online course."},
  {"id": 433, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R13.14", "heading": "Continuous assessment marks approved by the Dean (Academic Courses)", "section": "R13. SYSTEM OF EXAMINATIONS", "text": "Continuous assessment marks approved by the Dean (Academic Courses) shall be displayed to students by the respective HoDs within 5 days from the last working day."},
  {"id": 434, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R14", "heading": "PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "PASSING REQUIREMENTS"},
  {"id": 435, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R14.1", "heading": "A student who secures not less than 50 percent of total marks prescribed", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "A student who secures not less than 50 percent of total marks prescribed for the course [Continuous Assessment + End Semester Examinations] with a minimum of 50 percent of the marks prescribed for the end semester examination, shall be declared to have passed the course and acquired the relevant number of credits. This is applicable for all theory, practical, theory integrated with practical, and practical integrated theory courses."},
  {"id": 436, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R14.2", "heading": "If the student gets less than 50 percent of total marks, then the student", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "If the student gets less than 50 percent of total marks, then the student will be awarded only RA (Reappearance) grade."},
  {"id": 437, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R14.3", "heading": "If a student fails to secure a pass in a course, the student shall register and", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "If a student fails to secure a pass in a course, the student shall register and appear for the end semester examination in the subsequent semester or appear for the supplementary examination vide Clause R15. In such a case, the Continuous Assessment marks obtained by the student in the first appearance shall be retained and considered valid for one subsequent arrear attempt. However, in the third attempt, if a student fails to obtain pass marks i.e., (Continuous Assessment + End Semester Examination) as per Clause R14.1, then the student shall be declared to have passed the examination if he / she secures a minimum of 50 percent of marks prescribed for the end semester examination alone."},
  {"id": 438, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R14.4", "heading": "The students are allowed to write arrear examination as per Clause", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "The students are allowed to write arrear examination as per Clause R6.12.1."},
  {"id": 439, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R14.5", "heading": "If a student has submitted the project report but absent in the end semester", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "If a student has submitted the project report but absent in the end semester examination of project work, the student is deemed to be failed. If a student attends and fails in the End Semester examination of Project work, he / she shall attend the end semester examination again within 60 days from the date of declaration of the results. The subsequent viva-voce examination will be considered as reappearance with payment of double the amount of prescribed examination fee. In case the student fails in the subsequent viva-voce examination also, the student shall redo the course again."},
  {"id": 440, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R14.6", "heading": "The passing requirement for the courses which are assessed only through", "section": "R14. PASSING REQUIREMENTS", "text": "The passing requirement for the courses which are assessed only through continuous assessment (employability enhancement courses such as value-added courses, skill development courses, online courses with one credit, and internship except project work), shall be fixed as minimum 50 percent and the rest of the grades are decided."},
  {"id": 441, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15", "heading": "AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "AWARD OF LETTER GRADES"},
  {"id": 442, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.1", "heading": "All assessments will be done based on marks. However, for the purpose", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "All assessments will be done based on marks. However, for the purpose of reporting the performance of a student, letter grades, each carrying certain number of points will be awarded as per the range of total marks (out of 100) obtained by the candidate in each course as detailed below in the Table 10. The letter grades and the associated grade points are shown in Table 11. Table 10: Grade Distribution with Range of Marks O A+ A B+ B C RA 91-100 81-90 71-80 61-70 56-60 50-55 <50 An absolute grading system will be followed in assigning grades to students for each course registered. Table 11: Letter Grades with Grade Points Letter Grade Grade Significance Grade Points O Outstanding 10 A+ Excellent 9 A Very Good 8 B+ Good 7 B Average 6 C Satisfactory 5 Reappearance RA 0 Registration Shortage of SA 0 Attendance W Withdrawal 0 i) \"RA\" denotes Reappearance required for the examination in the course and \"W\" denotes withdrawal from the course. ii) The Grade \"SA\" denotes inadequate attendance (as per Clause R7) and hence prevented from writing the end semester examination. iii) The Grade \"SA' and \"W\" will figure only in the Result Sheets."},
  {"id": 443, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.2", "heading": "The grades obtained for the one / two credit value added courses shall", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "The grades obtained for the one / two credit value added courses shall figure in the grade sheet under the title 'Value Added Courses' / 'Online Courses'. The other grades RA, and SA will not figure in the grade sheet."},
  {"id": 444, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.3", "heading": "GRADE SHEETS", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "GRADE SHEETS"},
  {"id": 445, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.3.1", "heading": "After the results are declared, Grade Sheets will be issued to each student,", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "After the results are declared, Grade Sheets will be issued to each student, which will contain the following details:  List of courses enrolled for that semester and the grades obtained by the student.  The Grade Point Average (GPA) for the semester considering only the courses listed in the curriculum (not the additional courses) and  The Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) of all courses registered from first semester onwards considering only the courses of curriculum (not the additional courses)."},
  {"id": 446, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.3.2", "heading": "The Grade Point Average (GPA) for each semester will be calculated only", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "The Grade Point Average (GPA) for each semester will be calculated only for the students who have passed all the courses of that semester. Similarly, Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) up to any semester will be calculated only for the students who have passed all the courses up to that semester. GPA is the ratio of the sum of the products of the number of credits of curricular courses (Ci) registered and the grade points scored in those courses (GPi), taken for all the courses, to the sum of the number of credits of all the courses successfully cleared (n) during the particular semester. On successful completion of the programme, the CGPA will be calculated in a similar manner as follows, considering all the curricular courses (not the additional courses) enrolled from the first semester. ∑𝑁 𝑖=1 𝐶𝑖 × 𝐺𝑃𝑖 𝐶𝐺𝑃𝐴 = ∑𝑁𝑖=1 𝐶𝑖 where N is the total number of courses for the entire programme. \"RA\" and \"SA\" grades will be excluded for calculating GPA and CGPA."},
  {"id": 447, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.3.3", "heading": "In the consolidated grade sheet, the CGPA earned shall be converted into", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "In the consolidated grade sheet, the CGPA earned shall be converted into percentage of marks as follows: Percentage of Marks = CGPA X 10"},
  {"id": 448, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.3.4", "heading": "The Grade Point Average (GPA) for each semester will be included in the", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "The Grade Point Average (GPA) for each semester will be included in the grade card or sheet, even if a student fails in one or more courses within the semester. In such cases, the GPA will be calculated based on the grades obtained in the courses the student has passed. Similarly, the Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) will also be calculated based on the grades obtained in all the courses the student has passed up to and including the current semester."},
  {"id": 449, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.4", "heading": "REVALUATION OF ANSWER SCRIPTS", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "REVALUATION OF ANSWER SCRIPTS A candidate can apply for photocopy of his / her semester examination answer paper in a theory course, within 2 weeks from the declaration of results, on payment of a prescribed fee through proper application to the Controller of Examinations through the Head of Department. Students can see the valued answer scripts of the semester examinations and can get it retotaled / revalued by the faculty concerned. Based on the recommendation, the candidate can register for the revaluation through proper application to the Controller of Examinations. The answer sheets will be revaluated and the results will be intimated to the student concerned through the Head of the Department. Revaluation is permitted only for theory courses, and not permitted for practical courses, project work and Employability Enhancement Courses."},
  {"id": 450, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.5", "heading": "SUPPLEMENTARY EXAMINATION", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "SUPPLEMENTARY EXAMINATION"},
  {"id": 451, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.5.1", "heading": "Only those Students who obtained \"RA\" grade and have prescribed", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "Only those Students who obtained \"RA\" grade and have prescribed attendance and above in a course are eligible to apply for Supplementary Examination."},
  {"id": 452, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.5.2", "heading": "Registration shall be made for supplementary examination within the", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "Registration shall be made for supplementary examination within the stipulated period from the date of notification and the examination fee to be paid is double the amount of fee prescribed for the regular end semester examinations."},
  {"id": 453, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.5.3", "heading": "A student is eligible for only one Supplementary Examination for any", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "A student is eligible for only one Supplementary Examination for any course. No second chance will be given. In case a student fails in the Supplementary Examination, he / she must rewrite the examination along with the regular stream in the subsequent semesters, as and when it is conducted."},
  {"id": 454, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.5.4", "heading": "Students who miss the end-semester examination due to valid medical or", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "Students who miss the end-semester examination due to valid medical or some other reason may be permitted with the consent of the Dean (Academic Courses) to appear for the supplementary examination(s) subject to fulfilling of attendance requirement (vide Clause R7)."},
  {"id": 455, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.5.5", "heading": "Supplementary Examinations will be conducted during the first two", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "Supplementary Examinations will be conducted during the first two weeks after the commencement of the next semester."},
  {"id": 456, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.5.6", "heading": "Supplementary examination will be considered as an alternative to the", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "Supplementary examination will be considered as an alternative to the end-semester examination only. The continuous assessment marks already secured by the students will be considered for finalizing the grade."},
  {"id": 457, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.5.7", "heading": "A minimum of 50 percent of marks prescribed for the end semester", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "A minimum of 50 percent of marks prescribed for the end semester examination should be scored in the supplementary examination(s) to declare the result as have passed the course and acquired the relevant number of credits."},
  {"id": 458, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R15.5.8", "heading": "If a student receives an \"RA\" grade due to involvement in malpractice", "section": "R15. AWARD OF LETTER GRADES", "text": "If a student receives an \"RA\" grade due to involvement in malpractice during an examination, he or she will not be permitted to appear for the supplementary examination."},
  {"id": 459, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R16", "heading": "ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE"},
  {"id": 460, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R16.1", "heading": "A student shall be declared to be eligible for the award of the M.A. / MBA", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "A student shall be declared to be eligible for the award of the M.A. / MBA / MCA / M.Com. / M.Sc. / MSW / M.Tech. degree, provided the student has: i) Successfully gained the required number of total credits as specified in the curriculum corresponding to the student's programme within the stipulated duration. ii) Successfully completed the course requirements, appeared for the End Semester Examinations and passed all the courses prescribed in all the 4 semesters within a maximum duration of 4 years reckoned from the commencement of the first semester. iii) Successfully passed any additional courses prescribed by the Dean (Academic Courses). iv) No disciplinary action is pending against the student. v) The award of Degree must have been approved by the Academic Council of the Institution."},
  {"id": 461, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R16.2", "heading": "Classification of the Degree Awarded", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "Classification of the Degree Awarded First Class with Distinction"},
  {"id": 462, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R16.2.1", "heading": "A student who satisfies the following conditions shall be declared to have", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "A student who satisfies the following conditions shall be declared to have passed the examination in First class with Distinction: i) Should have passed the examination in all the courses of all the four semesters in first appearance within three years, which includes authorized break of study of one year. Withdrawal from examination (vide Clause R18) will not be construed as an appearance. ii) Should have secured a CGPA of not less than 8.00. iii) Should not have been prevented from writing end semester examination due to lack of attendance in any of the courses. iv) The authorized break of study (vide Clause R17) and withdrawal from the examination (vide Clause R18) will not be construed as an attempt. First Class"},
  {"id": 463, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R16.2.2", "heading": "A student who satisfies the following conditions shall be declared to have", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "A student who satisfies the following conditions shall be declared to have passed the examination in First class: i) Should have passed the examination in all the courses of all four semesters within 4 years, which includes one year of authorized break of study (if availed) or prevention from writing the End Semester Examination due to lack of attendance (if applicable). ii) Should have secured a CGPA of not less than 6.50. iii) The authorized break of study (vide Clause R17) and withdrawal from the examination (vide Clause R18) will not be construed as an attempt. Second Class"},
  {"id": 464, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R16.2.3", "heading": "All other students (not covered in Clauses R16.2.1 and R16.2.2) who", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "All other students (not covered in Clauses R16.2.1 and R16.2.2) who qualify for the award of the degree (vide Clause R16) shall be declared to have passed the examination in Second Class."},
  {"id": 465, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R16.3", "heading": "A student who is absent in the end semester examination in a course /", "section": "R16. ELIGIBILITY FOR THE AWARD OF DEGREE", "text": "A student who is absent in the end semester examination in a course / project work / dissertation / thesis after having registered for the same shall be considered to have appeared in that examination (except approved withdrawal from end semester examinations as per Clause R18) for the purpose of classification."},
  {"id": 466, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R17", "heading": "PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY"},
  {"id": 467, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R17.1", "heading": "Break of Study shall be granted by the Dean (Academic Courses) only", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "Break of Study shall be granted by the Dean (Academic Courses) only once for valid reasons for a period of maximum one year during the entire period of study of the degree programme."},
  {"id": 468, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R17.2", "heading": "Prescribed fee to the Institute should be paid during the \"Break of Study\"", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "Prescribed fee to the Institute should be paid during the \"Break of Study\" period."},
  {"id": 469, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R17.3", "heading": "The student permitted to re-join after the break of study / prevention due", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "The student permitted to re-join after the break of study / prevention due to lack of attendance, shall be governed by the Curriculum and Regulations in force at the time of re-joining. If the Regulation is changed, then, those students may have to take up additional courses as prescribed by the Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 470, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R17.4", "heading": "Total number of credits to be earned by the student shall be more than or", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "Total number of credits to be earned by the student shall be more than or equal to the total number of credits prescribed in the curriculum in force. If the credit assigned for L T P of the courses are not same in two Regulations under consideration, then equivalence shall be arrived as per the credit assignment followed in the Regulations in force."},
  {"id": 471, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R17.5", "heading": "The authorized break of study (for a maximum of one year) will not be", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "The authorized break of study (for a maximum of one year) will not be construed for the duration specified for passing all the courses for the purpose of classification. (vide Clause R16.2)."},
  {"id": 472, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R17.6", "heading": "The total period for completion of the programme reckoned from, the", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "The total period for completion of the programme reckoned from, the commencement of the first semester to which the candidate was admitted shall not exceed the maximum period specified in Clause R5 irrespective of the period of break of study (vide Clause R17) in order that he / she may be eligible for the award of the degree."},
  {"id": 473, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R17.7", "heading": "If any student is detained due to a lack of requisite attendance, progress,", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "If any student is detained due to a lack of requisite attendance, progress, or good conduct, the period spent in that semester shall not be considered as a permitted \"Break of Study\" or \"Withdrawal\", and Clause R17 or R18 shall not apply to this case."},
  {"id": 474, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R17.8", "heading": "In case there is any period of break of study more than the permitted", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "In case there is any period of break of study more than the permitted duration of break of study, the student shall be permitted to continue the programme only if the approval is obtained from the Dean (Academic Courses) through the concerned HoD before the end of the semester in which the student has taken break of study."},
  {"id": 475, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R17.9", "heading": "If the student has not reported back to the department, after the break of", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "If the student has not reported back to the department, after the break of study, his / her name shall be deleted permanently from the Institute enrollment. Such students are not entitled to seek readmission under any circumstances."},
  {"id": 476, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R17.10", "heading": "If a student in Full Time mode wants to take up job / start-up /", "section": "R17. PROVISION FOR AUTHORISED BREAK OF STUDY", "text": "If a student in Full Time mode wants to take up job / start-up / entrepreneurship during the period of study, he / she shall apply for authorized break of study for one year. The student shall take up the assignment only after getting approval of the same by the Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 477, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R18", "heading": "PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END SEMESTER", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END SEMESTER", "text": "PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END SEMESTER EXAMINATIONS"},
  {"id": 478, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R18.1", "heading": "A student may, for valid reasons (medically unfit / unexpected family", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END SEMESTER", "text": "A student may, for valid reasons (medically unfit / unexpected family situation / Sports approved by the Director, Sports and HoD) and on prior application, be granted permission to withdraw from appearing for one examination of one course or two or more consecutive examinations of different courses in the end semester examination. Permission cannot be given to withdraw from the examinations in a non-consecutive sequence."},
  {"id": 479, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R18.2", "heading": "Such withdrawal shall be permitted only once during the entire period of", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END SEMESTER", "text": "Such withdrawal shall be permitted only once during the entire period of study of the degree programme."},
  {"id": 480, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R18.3", "heading": "Withdrawal application is valid only if the student is otherwise eligible to", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END SEMESTER", "text": "Withdrawal application is valid only if the student is otherwise eligible to write the examination (vide Clause R7) and if it is made within 10 days prior to the commencement of the end-semester examination and recommended by the HoD and approved by the Dean (Academic Courses)."},
  {"id": 481, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R18.4", "heading": "Notwithstanding the requirement of mandatory 10 days' notice,", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END SEMESTER", "text": "Notwithstanding the requirement of mandatory 10 days' notice, applications for withdrawal for special cases under extraordinary conditions will be considered on the merit of the case."},
  {"id": 482, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R18.5", "heading": "Withdrawal shall not be construed as an appearance for the eligibility of", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END SEMESTER", "text": "Withdrawal shall not be construed as an appearance for the eligibility of a student for First Class with Distinction. This provision is not applicable to those who seek withdrawal during IV semester."},
  {"id": 483, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R18.6", "heading": "Withdrawal from the end semester examination is NOT applicable to", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END SEMESTER", "text": "Withdrawal from the end semester examination is NOT applicable to arrear courses of previous semesters."},
  {"id": 484, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R18.7", "heading": "The student shall appear for the end semester examination with respect to", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END SEMESTER", "text": "The student shall appear for the end semester examination with respect to the withdrawn courses during the examination conducted in the subsequent semester or appear for the supplementary examination vide Clause R15 and need not re-appear for the continuous assessment examination."},
  {"id": 485, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R18.8", "heading": "Withdrawal from the continuous assessment examination is not permitted.", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END SEMESTER", "text": "Withdrawal from the continuous assessment examination is not permitted."},
  {"id": 486, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R18.9", "heading": "Withdrawal is not permitted for a student who has not satisfied the", "section": "R18. PROVISION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM THE END SEMESTER", "text": "Withdrawal is not permitted for a student who has not satisfied the conditions prescribed in Clause R7 as requirements for appearing in the end-semester examination."},
  {"id": 487, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R19", "heading": "DISCIPLINE", "section": "R19. DISCIPLINE", "text": "DISCIPLINE The Institute reserves the right to cancel the admission of any student and ask him / her to discontinue his / her studies at any stage of his / her career on the grounds of unsatisfactory academic performance or misbehavior and conduct."},
  {"id": 488, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R19.1", "heading": "Every student is required to observe discipline and decorous behaviour", "section": "R19. DISCIPLINE", "text": "Every student is required to observe discipline and decorous behaviour both inside and outside the Institute and not to indulge in any activity which will tend to bring down the prestige of the institution."},
  {"id": 489, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R19.2", "heading": "Any act of indiscipline of a student reported to the Dean (Academic", "section": "R19. DISCIPLINE", "text": "Any act of indiscipline of a student reported to the Dean (Academic Courses) will be referred to a Discipline and Welfare Committee constituted by the Vice Chancellor. The Committee will enquire into the charges and recommend suitable punishment if the charges are substantiated. The Vice Chancellor will consider the recommendation of the Discipline and Welfare Committee for appropriate action."},
  {"id": 490, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R19.3", "heading": "If a student indulges in malpractice in any of the end semester", "section": "R19. DISCIPLINE", "text": "If a student indulges in malpractice in any of the end semester examination / continuous assessment tests, he / she shall be liable for punitive action as prescribed by the institution from time to time."},
  {"id": 491, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R19.4", "heading": "Ragging of any dimension is a criminal and non-bailable offence in our", "section": "R19. DISCIPLINE", "text": "Ragging of any dimension is a criminal and non-bailable offence in our country. The current State and Central legislations provide for stringent punishment, including imprisonment. Once the involvement of a student is established in ragging, the offending student will be dismissed from the Institution and will not be admitted into any other Institution. Avenues also exist for collective punishment if individual cannot be identified in this inhuman act. Every student of the Institute, along with the parent, shall give an undertaking every year in this regard and this should be submitted at the time of enrolment."},
  {"id": 492, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R20", "heading": "REVISION OF REGULATIONS AND CURRICULUM", "section": "R20. REVISION OF REGULATIONS AND CURRICULUM", "text": "REVISION OF REGULATIONS AND CURRICULUM The Academic Council of the Institute reserves the right to revise, amend or change the regulations, the curriculum, syllabus and the scheme of examinations from time to time if found necessary and shall send the recommendations to the Executive Council for approval."},
  {"id": 493, "doc": "pg", "clause": "R21", "heading": "SPECIAL CASES", "section": "R21. SPECIAL CASES", "text": "SPECIAL CASES In the event of any clarification in the interpretation of the above regulations, they shall be referred to the Standing Committee (Internal members of the Academic Council). The Standing Committee will offer suitable interpretation / clarification required for special case on such references and get them ratified in the next meeting of the Academic Council. The decision of the Academic Council is final."},
  {"id": 494, "doc": "phd", "clause": "Preamble", "heading": "Institute Profile: Vision, Mission, Quality Policy, Objectives, Motto", "section": "Preamble", "text": "PERIYAR MANIAMMAI INSTITUTE OF SCIENCE & TECHNOLOGY Periyar Nagar, Vallam, Thanjavur - 613403 Tamil Nadu, India Periyar Maniammai Institute of Science & Technology is committed to imparting quality education, emphasizing the integration of proficiency and human values, along with the ongoing enhancement of educational quality. Vision Statement: To be a university of global dynamism with excellence in knowledge and innovation, ensuring social responsibility for creating an egalitarian society. Mission:  Offering well-balanced programs with scholarly faculty and state-of-the-art facilities to impart a high level of knowledge.  Providing student-centered education and fostering their growth in critical thinking, creativity, entrepreneurship, problem-solving, and collaborative work.  Engaging in progressive and meaningful research with a focus on sustainable development.  Empowering students to acquire the skills necessary for global competencies.  Instilling universal values, self-respect, gender equality, dignity, and ethics. Quality Policy: To be a leading institution of excellence in education and research, providing professional competence to meet academic, scholastic, and societal needs. Objectives:  To provide value-based education with social responsibility and ethics to both urban and underserved rural students.  To achieve excellence in education and empower students to attain global competence.  To promote a culture of research and innovation in young minds, fostering academic excellence, and encouraging lifelong learning.  To engage in specialized areas with a proven ability to make distinctive contributions to the objectives of the higher education system across diverse disciplines.  To engage in extramural studies, extension programmes, and field outreach activities to contribute to the development of society. The Motto: THINK – INNOVATE – TRANSFORM PERIYAR MANIAMMAI INSTITUTE OF SCIENCE & TECHNOLOGY VALLAM, THANJAVUR – 613403"},
  {"id": 495, "doc": "phd", "clause": "Ordinances", "heading": "ORDINANCES", "section": "", "text": "ORDINANCES (Effective from the academic year 2024-2025) Ph.D."},
  {"id": 496, "doc": "phd", "clause": "Ordinances", "heading": "ORDINANCES", "section": "", "text": "ORDINANCES"},
  {"id": 497, "doc": "phd", "clause": "O.1", "heading": "A candidate who has qualified for the award of Master's degree of this", "section": "", "text": "A candidate who has qualified for the award of Master's degree of this Institute or a recognized Institute or University in the discipline as prescribed in the regulations of the Academic Council is eligible to apply for the Ph.D. programme of this Institute."},
  {"id": 498, "doc": "phd", "clause": "O.2", "heading": "The award of the Ph.D. degree shall be in accordance with the regulations", "section": "", "text": "The award of the Ph.D. degree shall be in accordance with the regulations of the Academic Council of this Institute."},
  {"id": 499, "doc": "phd", "clause": "O.3", "heading": "The eligibility for admission, admission policy and procedure shall be", "section": "", "text": "The eligibility for admission, admission policy and procedure shall be decided from time to time by the Executive Council of the Institute, following guidelines issued by the Academic Council, Periyar Maniammai Institute of Science and Technology."},
  {"id": 500, "doc": "phd", "clause": "O.4", "heading": "Notwithstanding any that are stated in the regulations, the Academic", "section": "", "text": "Notwithstanding any that are stated in the regulations, the Academic Council has the right to modify any of those from time to time."},
  {"id": 501, "doc": "phd", "clause": "Title", "heading": "Ph.D. Regulations - 2024", "section": "", "text": "Ph.D. Regulations - 2024"},
  {"id": 502, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R1", "heading": "DEFINITIONS AND NOMENCLATURE", "section": "R1. DEFINITIONS AND NOMENCLATURE", "text": "DEFINITIONS AND NOMENCLATURE i. \"Institute\" means Periyar Maniammai Institute of Science & Technology (Deemed to be University). ii. \"Programme\" means Doctoral Programme leading to awarding of Ph.D.degree in various disciplines. iii. \"Dean (Academic Courses)\" means the authority of the Institute who is responsible for all the academic activities of the departments for implementation of relevant rules and regulations. iv. \"Director (Academic Research)\"means the authority of the Institute who oversees and coordinates all academic research activities, ensuring the implementation of research policies, promoting research excellence, and facilitating collaboration across departments. v. \"Controller of Examinations\" means the authority of the Institute who is responsible for all the activities of the examinations. vi. \"HoD\" refers to the Head of the Department where the Ph.D. is registered. vii. \"Academic Council\" means the approval granting authority for all academic related activities like framing of academic policies, approval of regulations, courses, syllabus etc. viii. \"ResearchAdvisoryBoard\" refers to the committee constituted by the Institute to approveresearch-related matters for each department and the Institute as a whole. ix. \"Supervisor\" means a faculty member assigned to mentor, guide, and oversee the scholar's research activities, ensuring academic rigor and successful completion of the dissertation. x. \"Research Scholar\" refers to an enrolled candidatepursuing original research under the guidance of a supervisor, aimed at contributing new knowledge in a chosen field of expertise. xi. \"Chairperson\" refers to the Chairperson of the Academic Council or Research Advisory Board, who is the Vice Chancellor. xii. \"Doctoral Committee\" refers to a panel of experts, including supervisor, internal faculty and an external specialist, responsible for guiding, monitoring, and evaluating the scholar's research progress and dissertation work. xiii. \"Course Work\" refers to a set of mandatory academic courses designed to build foundational knowledge and research skills, typically completed by the scholar prior to progressing independent research. xiv. \"E-Resources\" means learning materials saved electronically in online storage or cloud platform, which shall be accessed from anywhere and anytime online or shall be accessed offline by downloading the relevant materials. xv. \"MOOCs\" means Massive Open Online Courses available at both introductory and advanced levels accessible from \"E-Resources\". xvi. \"AICTE\" means All India Council for Technical Education established at New Delhi. xvii. \"UGC\" means University Grants Commission established at New Delhi."},
  {"id": 503, "doc": "phd", "clause": "RAB", "heading": "Formation of Research Advisory Board", "section": "R1. DEFINITIONS AND NOMENCLATURE", "text": "Formation of Research Advisory Board The Research Advisory Board is constituted for framing the guidelines and for issuance of directions or instructions to carry research work by the scholars efficiently and for monitoring the integrity of the quality of the work. The constitution of the Research Advisory Board is as follows: No. of Category Nature Members 1 Chairperson Vice Chancellor 1 Member Dean (Academic Courses) 1 Member Controller of Examinations Senior Faculty - Nominated by the Vice 1 Member Chancellor based on seniority by rotation for a period of two years Educationist / Industrialist - Nominated by the 1 Member Executive Council Academic Expert - Nominated by the 1 Member Academic Council for a period of two years Member 1 Director (Academic Research) Secretary The members nominated for this Board must be approved by the Academic Council and then by the Executive Council.  This Board shall be vested with powers to monitor the complete activities of each scholar and examine all matters from admission to award of Ph.D. Degree as per regulations stipulated by the Institute.  This Board shall meet once in a semester and the minutes of the meeting should be brought to the Academic Council for approval / ratification / information as applicable.  The Board shall be vested with powers to include new norms in addition to the prevailing rules and regulations in accordance with the conduct of comprehensive examination.  The recommendations of the Board shall be briefed out in the Academic Council by the Director (Academic Research) and subsequently will be discussed in the Executive Council.  The income and expenditure statement due to Institutional Fee, organizing Doctoral Committee meetings and infrastructural development shall be submitted by Director (Academic Research) to this Board for its approval."},
  {"id": 504, "doc": "phd", "clause": "RAB Roles", "heading": "The major roles of Research Advisory Board", "section": "Research Advisory Board", "text": "The major roles of Research Advisory Board  To make recommendations on strategic and policy matters with respect to research programmes.  Each member will serve the board for three years unless otherwise stated.  To make recommendations on the infrastructural development for the research activities proposed by the Faculty / Research Scholars.  To make recommendations / suggestions on the eligibility criteria for Research Supervisorrecognition.  To scrutinize the eligibility norms of the faculty towards obtaining Supervisor status.  To make recommendations on the constitution of Doctoral Committees.  To make recommendations / suggestions on the list of examiners (Indian / Foreign) for thesis evaluation and conduct of Viva voce examination confidentially before submitting to the Controller of Examinations.  To encourage interdepartmental, inter/intra-institutional research activities and establish modalities for preparing and undertaking joint research projects covering more than one knowledge domain, as well as policies for involving external agencies and experts in such projects.  To fix the norms for sitting fee, hospitability charges and travelling allowance to be provided by the Institute to the members participating in the meetings."},
  {"id": 505, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R2", "heading": "Categories of Admission", "section": "Research Advisory Board", "text": "Categories of Admission Candidates will be admitted to the Ph.D. programme of the Institute under one of the following categories: a. Regular full-time scholars with or without Institute fellowship or with project support. For admission to Ph.D. programmes under both the Regular and Project categories, the departments must adopt a common cut-off at the time of calling for interviews and use a common merit list for selection across all categories. b. Research Scholars who are faculty or staff members of the Institute. c. Research scholars under the external registration programme sponsored by and employed in industry / organization having R & D facilities, national laboratories, reputed Universities / colleges or employed in research / analysis jobs in public sector / private sector / Government. A research scholar under the external registration programme will normally carry out part or all of his / her research work in the industry / organization / national laboratories / colleges employing the scholar under the supervision of a co-guide also employed in the same organization and a guide at Periyar Maniammai Institute of Science & Technology."},
  {"id": 506, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R3", "heading": "ELIGIBILITY", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "ELIGIBILITY"},
  {"id": 507, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R3.1", "heading": "Minimum Educational Qualifications", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Minimum Educational Qualifications The minimum educational qualifications for admission to the Ph.D. programme of the Institute are as follows:"},
  {"id": 508, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R3.2", "heading": "Ph.D. in Engineering", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Ph.D. in Engineering a. Candidates with a Master's degree in Engineering / Technology with a good academic record or a Master's degree by Research (M.S. By Research) in Engineering / Technology disciplines, with a good academic record. b. Candidates with Master's degree in sciences with a good academic record are eligible for the relevant Engineering discipline and with a valid GATE score or UGC / CSIR-NET or equivalent qualification in the relevant area acceptable for the year of registration."},
  {"id": 509, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R3.3", "heading": "Ph.D. in Sciences and Humanities", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Ph.D. in Sciences and Humanities Master's degree in sciences or in an eligible discipline (including M.Phil.) with a good academic record or equivalent and having a valid GATE score or UGC / CSIR-NET or equivalent qualification acceptable for the current year in the relevant area."},
  {"id": 510, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R3.4", "heading": "Ph.D. in Management", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Ph.D. in Management Master's degree or equivalent in a relevant discipline with a good academic record and qualifying in national level examinations such as JMET / CAT / MAT / GATE / UGC or CSIR / NET / JRF or equivalent or international level post graduate admission examination such as GMAT or equivalent. Master's degree in Engineering / Technology with a good academic record or a Master's degree by Research in Engineering / Technology in a relevant discipline are exempted from qualifying in National level examinations."},
  {"id": 511, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R3.5", "heading": "Ph.D. in Architecture", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Ph.D. in Architecture a. Candidates with a Master's degree in Architecture with a good academic record or a Master's degree by Research (M.S. By Research) in Architecture / Town Planning disciplines, with a good academic record."},
  {"id": 512, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R3.6", "heading": "Institute Faculty or Staff members / Research Scholars under", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Institute Faculty or Staff members / Research Scholars under External Registration"},
  {"id": 513, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R3.6.1", "heading": "For Research Scholars in the above categories, the minimum educational", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "For Research Scholars in the above categories, the minimum educational qualifications are the same as prescribed for Research Scholars in R3.2, R3.3, R3.4, and R3.5 for admission to the Ph.D. programme in the respective categories. However, valid GATE score or CSIR / UGC NET/ JRF/ CAT or equivalent qualification as applicable for regular full time research scholars may not be required in these cases."},
  {"id": 514, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R3.6.2", "heading": "The research scholars in the above categories are classified as part-time", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The research scholars in the above categories are classified as part-time scholars."},
  {"id": 515, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R3.7", "heading": "Admission Brochure", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Admission Brochure  The list of eligible disciplines in which the minimum educational qualifications must be obtained will be provided by each department in the Admission Brochure or on the institute's website, and it will be updated from time to time.  The Department / Selection Committee may find fit to consider meritorious candidates from disciplines other than listed in the Admission Brochure if there is a good match between the educational / research background of the candidate and the proposed area of research.  The admission brochure will also include details about inter-disciplinary research areas, which may be pursued by the Research Scholars for the Ph.D. degree and the corresponding eligible disciplines given by the departments."},
  {"id": 516, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R4", "heading": "Selection Procedure", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Selection Procedure  Eligible candidates possessing the minimum educational qualifications and satisfying additional criteria set by the departments from time to time, will be called for an Interview and / or Test by the Selection Committee of the respective departments.  Candidates with valid scores in national-level examinations need not take the entrance test and will be called directly for an interview.  Based on the academic record and the performance of the candidates in the interview and / or test, the Selection Committee will recommend to the Chairperson of the Academic Council, the names of candidates found suitable for admission to the Ph.D. Programme.  The Institute shall maintain the list of all the Ph.D. registered students on its Website on year-wise basis. The list shall include the name of the registered candidate, topic of his / her research, name of his / her supervisor and co-supervisor if applicable, date of enrollment or registration."},
  {"id": 517, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R5", "heading": "Admission", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Admission  Candidates whose selection is approved by the Chairperson,Academic Council will be admitted to the Ph.D. programme after payment of prescribed fees.  A candidate is not eligible for re-registration for Ph.D. after cancellation of his / her earlier registration for any reason. Based on the merits of the individual case and taking into consideration of any special circumstances, a candidate may be considered for re-registration."},
  {"id": 518, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R6", "heading": "Duration of the Programme", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Duration of the Programme"},
  {"id": 519, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R6.1", "heading": "Ph.D. programme shall be for a minimum duration of three years, including", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Ph.D. programme shall be for a minimum duration of three years, including the period of course work, and a maximum of five years."},
  {"id": 520, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R6.2", "heading": "Ph.D. Research Scholars should submit the thesis within 5 years from the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Ph.D. Research Scholars should submit the thesis within 5 years from the date of registration. Extension beyond this period shall be considered by the Research Advisory Board for a period of 2 years based on the recommendations of the Doctoral Committee."},
  {"id": 521, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R6.3", "heading": "The women candidates shall be provided maternity leave / child care leave", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The women candidates shall be provided maternity leave / child care leave once in the entire duration of Ph.D. for upto 8 months."},
  {"id": 522, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R7", "heading": "Choice of Supervisor", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Choice of Supervisor"},
  {"id": 523, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R7.1", "heading": "Allotment of Research Scholars to guides will be made by the Director", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Allotment of Research Scholars to guides will be made by the Director (AcademicResearch) in consultation with the Head of the Department taking into consideration the research profile of the department and the preferences of the Research Scholars and guides."},
  {"id": 524, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R7.2", "heading": "There shall be not more than two guides from the Institute for a Research", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "There shall be not more than two guides from the Institute for a Research Scholar. External Supervisors are not allowed. However, a co-supervisor can be allowed in interdisciplinary areas from within or other departments of the institute or from other institutions with the approval of the Research Advisory Board and agreed upon by the consenting institutions."},
  {"id": 525, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R7.3", "heading": "The allocation of supervisor for the selected research scholar shall be", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The allocation of supervisor for the selected research scholar shall be decided by the department concerned depending on the number of scholars per research supervisor."},
  {"id": 526, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R7.4", "heading": "A research supervisor, who is a Professor, shall be allowed to guide up to 8", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "A research supervisor, who is a Professor, shall be allowed to guide up to 8 candidates at any given point of time. An Associate Professor shall guide up to a maximum of 6 candidates and an Assistant Professor can guide up to 4 scholars at a given point of time."},
  {"id": 527, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R7.5", "heading": "In case of the relocation of a woman research scholar due to marriage or", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "In case of the relocation of a woman research scholar due to marriage or otherwise, the research data shall be allowed to be transferred to the university to which the scholar intends to relocate, provided all the other conditions in these regulations are followed in letter and spirit, and the research work does not pertain to a project secured by the parent institution/supervisor from any funding agency. The scholar will, however, give due credit to the parent guide and the institution for the part of the research already done."},
  {"id": 528, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R8", "heading": "Eligibility for being guides", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Eligibility for being guides The following staff may act as guide for Ph.D. scholars:  Faculty members of the Institute having a doctoral degree  Scientific / Design staff of the Institute with a doctoral degree"},
  {"id": 529, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R8.1", "heading": "Continuance of retired faculty members / emeritus faculty as guides", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Continuance of retired faculty members / emeritus faculty as guides  When a faculty member, who has guided a candidate for at least 3 years, retires, he / she will continue to be a guide for a maximum period of 12 months. However, a co-guide who is in service will be appointed if required.  A faculty member who is to retire within three years may be permitted to become a guide to a new scholar, with another faculty member who is not likely to retire within five years as a co-guide, at the time of registration. Upon retirement, the faculty member will continue to be a co-guide and will be invited to the Doctoral Committee meetings, Synopsis meeting, and Viva voce examination.  Emeritus Fellows / Emeritus Professors, who hold office at this Institute for a period of 2 years or more, can become co-guides for Scholars along with a guide from the institute, with at least 5 years' service still left at the time of registration of the Scholar.  In case a faculty member who is a guide goes on leave exceeding one year duration, another faculty member will be identified to become a co-guide of the Research Scholar.  The induction of new guides after 3 years of registration of a Research Scholar will be considered by the Doctoral Committee and forwarded to the Research Advisory Board for approval."},
  {"id": 530, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R9", "heading": "Recognition of Supervisorship", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Recognition of Supervisorship"},
  {"id": 531, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R9.1", "heading": "Recognition of Supervisor for guiding research scholars will be accorded by", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Recognition of Supervisor for guiding research scholars will be accorded by the Research Advisory Board, on application to the Director (Academic Research) through proper channel in a prescribed format."},
  {"id": 532, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R9.2", "heading": "Faculty members seeking supervisor recognition should possess:", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Faculty members seeking supervisor recognition should possess: i. A Ph.D. degree in the relevant area of research in which he / she proposes to guide the scholars. ii. A minimum of two years research or teaching experience after acquiring Ph.D. degree. iii. At least five research publications in indexed journals in case of regular Professor / Associate Professor of the Institution or three research publications in indexed journals in case of regular Assistant Professor (at least one in Web of Science–SCIE/SSCI/AHCI or PubMed indexed journal article as First Author/Corresponding Author)."},
  {"id": 533, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R9.3", "heading": "The applicant should fulfil the above norms i.e. requirement as stated in", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The applicant should fulfil the above norms i.e. requirement as stated in Clause R9.2 (ii) after the completion of his / her Ph.D. degree."},
  {"id": 534, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R10", "heading": "Doctoral Committee", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Doctoral Committee"},
  {"id": 535, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R10.1", "heading": "The Head of the Department will intimate to the Director (Academic", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Head of the Department will intimate to the Director (Academic Research), for each Scholar the area of research, the name(s) of the guide(s) and a panel of experts, indicating their area of specialization for constitution of a Doctoral Committee, within 2 weeks of the date of joining of the Research Scholar. The supervisor should submit a request form in a prescribed format to the HoD to enable the constitution of the Doctoral Committee."},
  {"id": 536, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R10.2", "heading": "The Doctoral Committee shall be constituted as follows:", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Doctoral Committee shall be constituted as follows: The Doctoral Committee typically consists of three members, including the supervisor, and if a co-supervisor is present, the committee will have four members. Role of the Sl.No. Mode of Selection Member Approved by Research Advisory Board – 1 Supervisor Forwarded and recommended by the Head of the Department A faculty member from the same / allied department, with research interests similar to the candidate's proposed research area, 2 Internal member shall be nominated by the Chairperson of the Academic Council from a panel of names suggested by the Head of the Department. A faculty member from another institution, with research interests similar to the 3 External member candidate's proposed research area, shall be nominated by the Chairperson of the Academic Council from a panel of names suggested by the Head of the Department. 4 Co-supervisor If applicable"},
  {"id": 537, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R10.3", "heading": "In case any member goes on leave exceeding one year duration, or resigns", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "In case any member goes on leave exceeding one year duration, or resigns or retires from the Institute, the Chairperson, Academic Council will nominate another member based on the suggestion of the Doctoral Committee."},
  {"id": 538, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R10.4", "heading": "Scientific / Design staff and others who are eligible to guide Ph.D. Scholars", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Scientific / Design staff and others who are eligible to guide Ph.D. Scholars may be nominated as members of the Doctoral Committee."},
  {"id": 539, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R11", "heading": "Registration", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Registration"},
  {"id": 540, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R11.1", "heading": "The Doctoral Committee will meet normally within a month of being", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Doctoral Committee will meet normally within a month of being constituted, where the Research Scholar will make a presentation. The Doctoral Committee will fix / approve the date of registration for the Ph.D. programme, consider the proposed research topic and prescribe or approve the courses of study in this meeting."},
  {"id": 541, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R11.2", "heading": "The minutes of the first DC meeting will be sent to the Director (Academic", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The minutes of the first DC meeting will be sent to the Director (Academic Research) for the approval of the competent authority."},
  {"id": 542, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12", "heading": "Course Work", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Course Work"},
  {"id": 543, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.1", "heading": "The Doctoral Committee shall prescribe 5 courses by considering the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Doctoral Committee shall prescribe 5 courses by considering the proposed research topic."},
  {"id": 544, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.2", "heading": "All courses prescribed for Ph.D. coursework are in conformity with the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "All courses prescribed for Ph.D. coursework are in conformity with the credit-hour instructional requirement and shall specify content, instructional, and assessment methods. They are duly approved by the authorized academic bodies."},
  {"id": 545, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.3", "heading": "The coursework is considered a prerequisite for Ph.D. preparation. A", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The coursework is considered a prerequisite for Ph.D. preparation. A minimum of four credits shall be assigned to one or more courses on Research Methodology, which may cover areas such as quantitative methods, computer applications, research ethics, review of published research in the relevant field, training, fieldwork, etc. Other courses shall be advanced-level courses that prepare students for the Ph.D. degree."},
  {"id": 546, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.4", "heading": "The courses on Research Methodologies and Research Ethics are mandatory", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The courses on Research Methodologies and Research Ethics are mandatory and must be attended in offline mode at the institute, either as part of a Faculty Development Programme or according to the schedules provided by the institute. R12.5`The prescribed courses shall be post-graduate level courses of the Institute. Course work subjects may be taken from Core or Elective subjects offered in the institute at PG level / Core or Elective subjects offered in other institutions at PG level / Coursera / IITs' NPTEL with the recommendation of Doctoral Committee. The PG Regulations 2024 are to be followed when scholars attend courses in online mode."},
  {"id": 547, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.6", "heading": "Changes in prescribed courses shall be made only by the Doctoral", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Changes in prescribed courses shall be made only by the Doctoral Committee. The Doctoral Committee may prescribe additional courses for a Scholar wherever found necessary."},
  {"id": 548, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.7", "heading": "All candidates admitted to the Ph.D. programmes are required to complete", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "All candidates admitted to the Ph.D. programmes are required to complete the coursework prescribed by the Doctoral Committee during the initial one or two semesters."},
  {"id": 549, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.8", "heading": "The credit assigned to the Ph.D. coursework is a minimum of 14 credits and", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The credit assigned to the Ph.D. coursework is a minimum of 14 credits and a maximum of 16 credits."},
  {"id": 550, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.9", "heading": "On the recommendations of the Doctoral Committee, a candidate shall study", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "On the recommendations of the Doctoral Committee, a candidate shall study one or two courses under the guidance of the supervisor as \"Directed Study\"."},
  {"id": 551, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.10", "heading": "Research Scholar shall submit a registration form for the course work to", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Research Scholar shall submit a registration form for the course work to be completed in the prescribed format to the Director (Academic Research) through the supervisor. The Director (Academic Research) shall forward the same to the Controller of Examinations for further action."},
  {"id": 552, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.11", "heading": "A Ph.D. scholar must obtain a minimum of 60% of marks or the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "A Ph.D. scholar must obtain a minimum of 60% of marks or the equivalent grade on the UGC 7-point scale (or an equivalent grade/CGPA on a point scale where a grading system is followed) in the coursework to be eligible to continue in the programme and submit the dissertation/thesis."},
  {"id": 553, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.12", "heading": "The Doctoral Committee may give credit to courses already undergone by", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Doctoral Committee may give credit to courses already undergone by a Research Scholar in this Institute or other Institutions, provided they are the same or equivalent to those prescribed, and the performance level of the Scholar in them meets the minimum requirements."},
  {"id": 554, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.13", "heading": "Grades", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Grades Based on the performance, each student is awarded a final grade at the end of the semester examination in each course. The grades and the corresponding grade points are as follows: Letter Grade Grade Significance Grade Points O Outstanding 10 A+ Excellent 9 A Very Good 8 B+ Good 7 B Average 6 C Satisfactory 5"},
  {"id": 555, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.14", "heading": "Research Scholars shall obtain a minimum CGPA of 7.0 in the courses", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Research Scholars shall obtain a minimum CGPA of 7.0 in the courses taken by them subject to a minimum of \"B\" grade in the prescribed courses. If more than the minimum required courses have been taken, only the courses with the best performance will be considered for computing the CGPA."},
  {"id": 556, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.15", "heading": "A student is considered to have completed the subject successfully and", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "A student is considered to have completed the subject successfully and earned the credits if he / she secures a grade higher than \"C\". Once a course is successfully completed, it cannot be repeated."},
  {"id": 557, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R12.16", "heading": "The Grade Point Average (GPA) will be calculated if the candidate has", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Grade Point Average (GPA) will be calculated if the candidate has passed all the courses registered in that Semester. Similarly, Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) will be calculated only if the candidatehas passed all the registered courses prescribed by the Doctoral Committee. GPA is the ratio of the sum of the products of the number of credits of the courses (Ci) registered and the grade points scored in those courses (GPi), taken for all the courses, to the sum of the number of credits of all the courses successfully cleared (n) during the particular semester. On successful completion of the coursework, the CGPA will be calculated in a similar manner as follows, considering all the courses enrolled as prescribed by the Doctoral Committee. ∑𝑁 𝑖=1 𝐶𝑖 × 𝐺𝑃𝑖 𝐶𝐺𝑃𝐴 = ∑𝑁𝑖=1 𝐶𝑖 where N is the total number of courses."},
  {"id": 558, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R13", "heading": "Change of Supervisor", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Change of Supervisor"},
  {"id": 559, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R13.1", "heading": "The research scholar may request the Director (Academic Research) for a", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The research scholar may request the Director (Academic Research) for a change of supervisor after obtaining consent from the current supervisor. In this case, the Doctoral Committee of the research scholar may recommend a change of supervisor or the appointment of a co-supervisor for valid reasons. The recommendations of the Doctoral Committee shall be submitted to the Research Advisory Board for approval."},
  {"id": 560, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R14", "heading": "Progress Report", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Progress Report"},
  {"id": 561, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R14.1", "heading": "The supervisor has to review the research proposal and finalize the topic", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The supervisor has to review the research proposal and finalize the topic of research."},
  {"id": 562, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R14.2", "heading": "The supervisor shall guide the research scholar in developing the study", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The supervisor shall guide the research scholar in developing the study design and research methodology, and in identifying the course(s) that the scholar may need to take, before forwarding the same to the Doctoral Committee for its suggestions and recommendations."},
  {"id": 563, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R14.3", "heading": "The supervisor has to periodically review and assist in the progress of the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The supervisor has to periodically review and assist in the progress of the research work of the research scholar."},
  {"id": 564, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R14.4", "heading": "The research scholar shall submit a written progress report in a required", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The research scholar shall submit a written progress report in a required format for every six months. The report should be forwarded through the supervisor to the Head of the Department for consideration of the Doctoral Committee."},
  {"id": 565, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R14.5", "heading": "The minutes of the Doctoral Committee, including its suggestions and", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The minutes of the Doctoral Committee, including its suggestions and recommendations, along with the progress report(s) submitted by the scholars, should be forwarded to the Director (Academic Research) for further processing."},
  {"id": 566, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R14.6", "heading": "The progress made by the Research Scholar shall be reviewed by the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The progress made by the Research Scholar shall be reviewed by the Doctoral Committee once a year for the first 3 years and every six months thereafter."},
  {"id": 567, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R14.7", "heading": "Continuance of registration and award / continuance of scholarship /", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Continuance of registration and award / continuance of scholarship / Research Assistantship will be based on the recommendation of the Doctoral Committee."},
  {"id": 568, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R14.8", "heading": "In case of Research Scholars under external registration, the Doctoral", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "In case of Research Scholars under external registration, the Doctoral Committee will pay particular attention to the quantum of effort put in by the Scholars towards doctoral studies and progress."},
  {"id": 569, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R14.9", "heading": "Inadequacy of effort / progress can be a reason for cancellation of", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Inadequacy of effort / progress can be a reason for cancellation of registration."},
  {"id": 570, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R15", "heading": "Comprehensive Examination", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Comprehensive Examination"},
  {"id": 571, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R15.1", "heading": "Every Ph.D. scholar shall take and perform satisfactorily in the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Every Ph.D. scholar shall take and perform satisfactorily in the Comprehensive Examination in his / her Department."},
  {"id": 572, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R15.2", "heading": "The Comprehensive Examination shall be conducted by a Comprehensive", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Comprehensive Examination shall be conducted by a Comprehensive Examination Committee of the department, consisting of the scholar's Doctoral Committee members and at least two additional members: one faculty member from the institute and an external expert from industry or another institution, both nominated by the Chairperson of the Academic Council."},
  {"id": 573, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R15.3", "heading": "If the performance of a research scholar in the Comprehensive", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "If the performance of a research scholar in the Comprehensive Examination is not satisfactory on the first attempt, he / she will be given one more opportunity to appear for the Comprehensive Examination within six months of the initial attempt."},
  {"id": 574, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R15.4", "heading": "The registration of a Research Scholar who fails to complete successfully", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The registration of a Research Scholar who fails to complete successfully the Comprehensive Examination in both attempts will be cancelled."},
  {"id": 575, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R15.5", "heading": "The objective of the Comprehensive Examination is to test the general", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The objective of the Comprehensive Examination is to test the general capability of the research scholar and the breadth of his / her knowledge in his / her discipline and areas related to his / her field of research."},
  {"id": 576, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R15.6", "heading": "The Comprehensive Examination will usually consist of a written test and", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Comprehensive Examination will usually consist of a written test and oral examination or only oral examination."},
  {"id": 577, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R15.7", "heading": "The Comprehensive Examination Committee shall intimate to the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Comprehensive Examination Committee shall intimate to the Research Scholar sufficiently in advance the scope of the Comprehensive Examination, so as to enable the Scholar to prepare adequately for it."},
  {"id": 578, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R15.8", "heading": "The research scholars are normally expected to complete successfully the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The research scholars are normally expected to complete successfully the Comprehensive Examination within a year after his / her registration in the Ph.D. programme and in any case not later than three semesters after his / her registration in the Ph.D. programme."},
  {"id": 579, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R16", "heading": "Enrollment", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Enrollment"},
  {"id": 580, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R16.1", "heading": "All Research Scholars who are in residence and whose registration is still", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "All Research Scholars who are in residence and whose registration is still in force, are required to enroll in person each semester on the stipulated date till their submission of thesis after payment of the requisite fees. Those not in residence may pre-enroll in absentia during the stipulated period after payment of the requisite fees. The enrollment will be completed only after successful completion of progress meeting during the semester. The enrollment will be cancelled if the progress is not satisfactory."},
  {"id": 581, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R17", "heading": "Minimum Residential Requirement", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Minimum Residential Requirement"},
  {"id": 582, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R17.1", "heading": "For scholars pursuing full-time research, the minimum period required to", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "For scholars pursuing full-time research, the minimum period required to be at the institute to carry out study and research, from the date of registration for the Ph.D. programme to the date of submission of the Ph.D. thesis, shall be 24 months."},
  {"id": 583, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R17.2", "heading": "The minimum residential requirement for Ph.D. scholars under external", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The minimum residential requirement for Ph.D. scholars under external registration and for research scholars not employed by the institute is from the commencement of the courses on Research Methodologies and Research Ethics until their completion, which is a maximum period of two weeks or as per the schedules provided by the institute."},
  {"id": 584, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R17.3", "heading": "This is to ensure that those courses are studied in offline mode", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "This is to ensure that those courses are studied in offline mode mandatorily and 100 percent attendance is expected."},
  {"id": 585, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R18", "heading": "Relief from Ph.D. programme to take up job", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Relief from Ph.D. programme to take up job"},
  {"id": 586, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R18.1", "heading": "Ph.D. Scholars who got a job offer can get relief from the programme,", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Ph.D. Scholars who got a job offer can get relief from the programme, while keeping their registration alive on payment of the requisite fees every semester, on the following condition:  Scholars who take up jobs will be relieved on their request, based on the recommendations of Doctoral Committee, if they have completed their comprehensive examination."},
  {"id": 587, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R18.2", "heading": "The renewal of their registration for every year / semester however, will", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The renewal of their registration for every year / semester however, will be considered only if the Doctoral Committee finds his / her progress to be satisfactory and recommends continuance of registration."},
  {"id": 588, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R19", "heading": "Withdrawal from the programme", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Withdrawal from the programme"},
  {"id": 589, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R19.1", "heading": "A Scholar may be permitted by the Director (Academic Research) to", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "A Scholar may be permitted by the Director (Academic Research) to withdraw from the programme for a semester or longer for reasons of ill health or other valid grounds duly recommended by the Doctoral Committee."},
  {"id": 590, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R19.2", "heading": "Normally a scholar will be permitted to withdraw from the programme", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Normally a scholar will be permitted to withdraw from the programme only for a maximum continuous period of two semesters."},
  {"id": 591, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R20", "heading": "Cancellation of Registration", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Cancellation of Registration"},
  {"id": 592, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R20.1", "heading": "The registration of a Research Scholar whose progress is not found to be", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The registration of a Research Scholar whose progress is not found to be satisfactory by the Doctoral Committee or who has not enrolled, is liable to be cancelled."},
  {"id": 593, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R20.2", "heading": "The registration of a Research Scholar who has not submitted his / her", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The registration of a Research Scholar who has not submitted his / her thesis before the end of the maximum permissible period as in Clause"},
  {"id": 594, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R6.2", "heading": "will be cancelled.", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "will be cancelled."},
  {"id": 595, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R20.3", "heading": "The registration is liable for cancellation by the Director (Academic", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The registration is liable for cancellation by the Director (Academic Research) if two consecutive six-monthly progress reports are not submitted or not satisfactory."},
  {"id": 596, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R20.4", "heading": "The research scholar wishes to withdraw the course and wishes to cancel", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The research scholar wishes to withdraw the course and wishes to cancel his / her registration."},
  {"id": 597, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R20.5", "heading": "In all the above cancellation cases, the feed paid by the research scholar", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "In all the above cancellation cases, the feed paid by the research scholar shall not be refunded."},
  {"id": 598, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R21", "heading": "Synopsis of Thesis", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Synopsis of Thesis"},
  {"id": 599, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R21.1", "heading": "The research scholar shall be permitted to submit the synopsis only after", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The research scholar shall be permitted to submit the synopsis only after obtaining the confirmation of registration i.e., after successful completion of Comprehensive Examination."},
  {"id": 600, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R21.2", "heading": "On satisfactory completion of the prescribed courses, the comprehensive", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "On satisfactory completion of the prescribed courses, the comprehensive examination and the research work, the scholar shall submit the requisite copies of the Synopsis of his / her research work in the required format through the supervisor and Head of the Department to the Office of the Director (Academic Research) for consideration of the Doctoral Committee."},
  {"id": 601, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R21.3", "heading": "Prior to the submission of the synopsis, the scholar is required to present", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Prior to the submission of the synopsis, the scholar is required to present at least two seminars on the topic of their research. The third Doctoral Committee meeting may be held after the scholar has presented the first seminar. The first seminar will typically be presented to the faculty members of the department in the absence of the Doctoral Committee members.The second seminar presentation will be held during the third Doctoral Committee meeting in the presence of the committee members."},
  {"id": 602, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R21.4", "heading": "The Scholar should have at least 2 research papers in Web of Science–SCI", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Scholar should have at least 2 research papers in Web of Science–SCI / SCIE/SSCI/AHCI or PubMed/Scopus indexed journal article as First Author in the relevant areas of researcheither published or accepted for publication."},
  {"id": 603, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R21.5", "heading": "The Research Scholar shall present the Synopsis before the Doctoral", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Research Scholar shall present the Synopsis before the Doctoral Committee on satisfying the Clauses R21.1 to R21.4. The Doctoral Committee will, if it approves the work reported in the Synopsis, permit the Research Scholar to submit the thesis and recommend a panel of at least eight examiners from other reputed Indian / Foreign institutes or universities."},
  {"id": 604, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R22", "heading": "Submission of Thesis", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Submission of Thesis"},
  {"id": 605, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R22.1", "heading": "The Research Scholar shall, within three months of acceptance of the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Research Scholar shall, within three months of acceptance of the Synopsis, submit requisite copies of the thesis and abstract of the thesis as stipulated."},
  {"id": 606, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R22.2", "heading": "The Doctoral Committee may grant additional time beyond three months", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Doctoral Committee may grant additional time beyond three months on request from the Scholar for valid reasons."},
  {"id": 607, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R23", "heading": "Panel of Examiners", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Panel of Examiners"},
  {"id": 608, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R23.1", "heading": "The thesis shall be referred by the Chairperson, Academic Council to two", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The thesis shall be referred by the Chairperson, Academic Council to two examiners (one examiner from India and another examiner from reputed foreign universities) chosen from the panel of examiners recommended by the Doctoral Committee at its Synopsis meeting."},
  {"id": 609, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R23.2", "heading": "The examiners must be at the level of Associate Professor or above.", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The examiners must be at the level of Associate Professor or above."},
  {"id": 610, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R24", "heading": "Thesis Evaluation", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Thesis Evaluation"},
  {"id": 611, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R24.1", "heading": "The examiner is expected to send the report on the thesis within two", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The examiner is expected to send the report on the thesis within two months from the date of receipt of the thesis."},
  {"id": 612, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R24.2", "heading": "In case of undue delay in receiving the thesis report, the Chairperson,", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "In case of undue delay in receiving the thesis report, the Chairperson, Academic Council shall appoint another examiner in his / her place for evaluating the thesis."},
  {"id": 613, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R24.3", "heading": "If one of the two thesis examiners do not commend the thesis, it shall be", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "If one of the two thesis examiners do not commend the thesis, it shall be referred to a third examiner from the panel of examiners for evaluation."},
  {"id": 614, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R24.4", "heading": "If an examiner suggests resubmission of the thesis, after revision, the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "If an examiner suggests resubmission of the thesis, after revision, the Research Scholar will be allowed to resubmit the thesis within the time stipulated by the Doctoral Committee failing which the revised thesis will not be accepted and his / her registration will be cancelled."},
  {"id": 615, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R24.5", "heading": "If two examiners, after referral to a third examiner, if necessary, report the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "If two examiners, after referral to a third examiner, if necessary, report the thesis as not commended, the registration of the Scholar shall stand cancelled."},
  {"id": 616, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R24.6", "heading": "If reports of two examiners after referral to a third examiner, if necessary,", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "If reports of two examiners after referral to a third examiner, if necessary, declare the thesis as 'commended', the Doctoral Committee in its final meeting will consider the reports and recommend for conduct of Viva voce which will be conducted normally not earlier than two weeks from the date of the constitution of the Viva voce board. The Doctoral Committee will suggest a panel of at least four expert members out of which one member will be nominated for the Viva voce board by the Chairperson of the Academic Council."},
  {"id": 617, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R24.7", "heading": "In all other cases, not covered by the above Regulations the matter will be", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "In all other cases, not covered by the above Regulations the matter will be referred to the Doctoral Committee for consideration."},
  {"id": 618, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R25", "heading": "Viva Voce Examination", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Viva Voce Examination"},
  {"id": 619, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R25.1", "heading": "The following is the composition of the public Viva voceexamination", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The following is the composition of the public Viva voceexamination board: a. Research Supervisor –Convener b. Indian Examiner who evaluated the thesis c. A subject expert nominated by the Vice- Chancellor from the suggested panel of examiners by the Doctoral Committee as representative for foreign examiner"},
  {"id": 620, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R25.2", "heading": "The Doctoral Committee members of the Research Scholar concerned will", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Doctoral Committee members of the Research Scholar concerned will be invitees to the Viva voce."},
  {"id": 621, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R25.3", "heading": "The Viva voce board will examine the Scholar on his / her thesis work and", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Viva voce board will examine the Scholar on his / her thesis work and evaluate his / her performance as satisfactory or otherwise."},
  {"id": 622, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R25.4", "heading": "The Viva voce board will ensure that the Scholar answers satisfactorily the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Viva voce board will ensure that the Scholar answers satisfactorily the questions raised by the thesis examiner(s)."},
  {"id": 623, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R25.5", "heading": "If the report of the Viva voce board declares the performance of the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "If the report of the Viva voce board declares the performance of the Research Scholar not satisfactory, he / she may be asked to reappear for Viva voce at a later date (not earlier than a month and not later than six months from the date of the first Viva voce)."},
  {"id": 624, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R25.6", "heading": "On the second occasion, the Viva voce board will also include the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "On the second occasion, the Viva voce board will also include the members of the Doctoral Committee."},
  {"id": 625, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R25.7", "heading": "If the Viva voce board on the second occasion also evaluates the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "If the Viva voce board on the second occasion also evaluates the performance of the Research Scholar not satisfactory, the matter will be referred to Academic Council for a decision."},
  {"id": 626, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R25.8", "heading": "The Viva voce board may also recommend revision to be made in the final", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The Viva voce board may also recommend revision to be made in the final version of the thesis after taking into consideration suggestions of the examiners who evaluated the thesis and the discussion at the Viva voce."},
  {"id": 627, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R25.9", "heading": "The convenor of the Viva voce board shall forward the thesis to the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The convenor of the Viva voce board shall forward the thesis to the Director (Academic Research) certifying that the revisions recommended by the Viva voce board, if any, have been incorporated in the copy of the thesis along with the report of the Viva voce board."},
  {"id": 628, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R25.10", "heading": "All the Research Scholars shall submit five copies of the final form of", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "All the Research Scholars shall submit five copies of the final form of thesis in A5 size and an electronic version in PDF format after the Viva voce board recommends the award of the Ph.D. degree."},
  {"id": 629, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R25.11", "heading": "Final version of thesis (soft copy) and scanned copies of declaration and", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Final version of thesis (soft copy) and scanned copies of declaration and certificate will be uploaded in UGC website (Shodhganga@INFLIBNET) for the benefit of research community around the world."},
  {"id": 630, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R26", "heading": "Award of Ph.D. Degree", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Award of Ph.D. Degree"},
  {"id": 631, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R26.1", "heading": "If the performance of the Research Scholar in the Viva voce is", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "If the performance of the Research Scholar in the Viva voce is satisfactory, he / she will be awarded Ph.D. degree on the recommendation of the Academic Council and with the approval of the Executive Council of the Institute."},
  {"id": 632, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R26.2", "heading": "The award of Ph.D. degrees to the scholars who have completed all the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "The award of Ph.D. degrees to the scholars who have completed all the requirements for the award of Ph.D. degree as and when approved by the Academic Council and Executive Council, will be considered on request so as to reduce the period of waiting by Scholars for getting the degrees."},
  {"id": 633, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R26.3", "heading": "Plagiarism of any sort is strictly prohibited. Even after the award of Ph.D.", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "Plagiarism of any sort is strictly prohibited. Even after the award of Ph.D. Degree, if it is found that the candidate has indulged in some sort of plagiarism in his / her thesis, his/her degree would be withdrawn by the institution and the candidate will be debarred from any further registration, after the decision being taken by the Research Advisory Board."},
  {"id": 634, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R26.4", "heading": "If it is found that the Supervisor has also abetted the crime, the", "section": "R3. ELIGIBILITY", "text": "If it is found that the Supervisor has also abetted the crime, the recognition of the supervisorship would be permanently cancelled and the candidates registered under him/ her will be transferred to other Supervisors in consultation with the scholars, after the decision being taken by the Research Advisory Board."},
  {"id": 635, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R27", "heading": "DISCIPLINE", "section": "R27. DISCIPLINE", "text": "DISCIPLINE The Institute reserves the right to cancel the admission of any scholar and ask him / her to discontinue his / her studies at any stage of his / her career on the grounds of unsatisfactory academic performance or misbehavior and conduct."},
  {"id": 636, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R27.1", "heading": "Every scholar is required to observe discipline and decorous behaviour", "section": "R27. DISCIPLINE", "text": "Every scholar is required to observe discipline and decorous behaviour both inside and outside the Institute and not to indulge in any activity which will tend to bring down the prestige of the institution."},
  {"id": 637, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R27.2", "heading": "Any act of indiscipline of a scholar reported to the Dean (Academic", "section": "R27. DISCIPLINE", "text": "Any act of indiscipline of a scholar reported to the Dean (Academic Courses) will be referred to a Discipline and Welfare Committee constituted by the Vice Chancellor. The Committee will enquire into the charges and recommend suitable punishment if the charges are substantiated. The Vice Chancellor will consider the recommendation of the Discipline and Welfare Committee for appropriate action."},
  {"id": 638, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R27.3", "heading": "If acandidate indulges in malpractice including plagiarism, he / she shall", "section": "R27. DISCIPLINE", "text": "If acandidate indulges in malpractice including plagiarism, he / she shall be liable for punitive action as prescribed by the institution from time to time."},
  {"id": 639, "doc": "phd", "clause": "Appeal", "heading": "Appeal", "section": "R27. DISCIPLINE", "text": "Appeal Council whose decision will be final."},
  {"id": 640, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R28", "heading": "Special Cases", "section": "R27. DISCIPLINE", "text": "Special Cases"},
  {"id": 641, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R28.1", "heading": "The Academic Council of the Institute reserves the right to revise,", "section": "R27. DISCIPLINE", "text": "The Academic Council of the Institute reserves the right to revise, amend or change the regulations, syllabus for the courses prescribed by the Doctoral Committee, especially for the courses of \"Directed Study\", and the scheme of examinations from time to time if found necessary and shall send the recommendations to the Executive Council for approval."},
  {"id": 642, "doc": "phd", "clause": "R28.2", "heading": "In the event of any clarification in the interpretation of the above", "section": "R27. DISCIPLINE", "text": "In the event of any clarification in the interpretation of the above regulations, they shall be referred to the Standing Committee (Internal members of the Academic Council). The Standing Committee will offer suitable interpretation / clarification required for special case on such references and get them ratified in the next meeting of the Academic Council. The decision of the Academic Council is final."},
];
